{"parentUuid":"3464b35e-cb55-41c2-ae11-0600bace0b99","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d3cef047-f25f-4980-9952-f7c49a687725","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MACFhvcPnoWbGU6pH1CpM7","type":"tool_result","content":"total 120\ndrwx------   9 kenneth  staff    288 Nov 10 10:35 .\ndrwx------  46 kenneth  staff   1472 Nov  9 20:58 ..\n-rw-r--r--   1 kenneth  staff  22913 Nov 10 12:32 chargebee-jusprin-emails-draft.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 kenneth  staff   5028 Nov  9 18:56 chargebee-readiness-2026-11-09.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 kenneth  staff   5615 Nov 10 10:35 jusprin1-users-and-obico-discount-report.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 kenneth  staff   6622 Nov  9 21:49 jusprinv2-prod-rollout-state.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 kenneth  staff   2331 Nov  9 18:53 prod-ingress-kubectl-diff.txt\n-rw-r--r--   1 kenneth  staff   2350 Nov  9 18:56 proposed-billing-fix.patch\n-rw-r--r--   1 kenneth  staff    770 Nov  9 22:05 proposed-cf-product.patch\n5:are switched on, whether the \"Print Smart, - The Obico team\" lines live in each template or in the\n7:template can pick its own sender profile.\n32:- Proposed instead: a customer custom field on both Chargebee sites, `cf_product`, which the server\n35:  receipt included. Tested on the test site 2026-11-10: a customer create carrying `cf_product`\n40:- Not yet confirmed: the exact merge-field name Chargebee gives a customer custom field\n41:  (expected `{{customer.cf_product}}`; to check in the template editor's field list).\n46:   the segment `cf_product = jusprin2`, with its own subject and body, and possibly its own sender\n49:2. **Conditional blocks** (works on any plan): in each existing template, the JusPrin text inside\n50:   `{{#customer.cf_product = jusprin2}} … {{/customer.cf_product = jusprin2}}` and the current Obico\n51:   text inside `{{^customer.cf_product = jusprin2}} … {{/customer.cf_product = jusprin2}}`. Sender,\n98:1. Create the `cf_product` customer field on the test site; add the conditional blocks (or segments) there; send Chargebee's test mail for each and read them.\n99:2. Server: set `cf_product` in `ensure_customer`; deploy to staging; one staging checkout to see the field arrive.\n100:3. Live site, with Kenneth's yes: the same field, the same template edits, and (with segments) the sender profile. This has to happen before the JusPrin 2 plans and pack go on sale on the live site.\n107:- Segments are saved subscription filters. Test site: created segment \"JusPrin 2 plans\" = plan starts with `jusprin-` AND plan does not contain `unlimited` (matches only JusPrin 2 Hobby/Workshop; plan name filters don't work, ids do).\n108:- Adding a second \"Active subscription is created\" email for that segment shows: \"You can enable only one notification for an email group on this plan. To use more notifications on your Live site, upgrade to higher plan.\" So a JusPrin version beside Obico's needs a Chargebee upgrade on the live site. Public pricing lists segmentation and multiple notifications from the \"Flow\" plan, \"$99 + 0.65%\"; the actual upgrade price is via the account manager.\n109:- Test-site leftovers from this check: segment \"JusPrin 2 plans\"; an unpublished, not-enabled \"Active subscription is created\" email for that segment (notification 7508689). A segment change on the Obico welcome email was discarded.\n111:## Conditional blocks tried on the test site (2026-11-10, Kenneth chose conditional blocks)\n114:- Heading, body and closing paragraph: per email, accept `{{#customer.cf_product = jusprin2}}`. Merge name confirmed in the editor's field list: `customer.cf_product`.\n116:- Obico logo at the top and the italic \"Obico was previously known as…\" line: the master template, shared by every email. The notes line refuses conditionals (\"Mustache not allowed in notes\"); the logo is an image block. Email bodies offer only text, button and section blocks, no image.\n118:Changed on the test site (originals in the session scratchpad, test_site_originals.txt):\n119:- Obico Admin signature: `{{^C}}Print Smart,{{/C}}{{#C}}Happy printing,{{/C}}` / `{{^C}}- The Obico team{{/C}}{{#C}}The JusPrin team{{/C}}` (C = customer.cf_product = jusprin2).\n121:- Master template: unchanged.\n124:Result, read in each customer's Email Logs preview (delivery itself bounced: Gmail rejects admin@obico.io mail from the test site under obico.io's DMARC policy; the live site's copies do arrive):\n125:- jusprinv2-mailtest-jp (cf_product = jusprin2): \"Welcome to JusPrin\", the JusPrin body, the support line, \"Happy printing, / The JusPrin team\". Still Obico's logo at the top and \"Obico was previously known as…\" at the bottom.\n126:- jusprinv2-mailtest-ob (no cf_product): the Obico email exactly as before.\n128:Proposed server change: proposed-cf-product.patch in this folder (adds cf_product to Customer.create in ensure_customer). Not applied, no test covers ensure_customer.\n130:New test-site leftovers: customer field cf_product, customers jusprinv2-mailtest-jp and -ob (k@thespaghettidetective.com) with active JusPrin Hobby subscriptions and unpaid invoices.\n132:## Logo removed for everyone (Kenneth, 2026-11-10: \"Remove logo for all\") — done on the test site\n134:- The email logo is not part of the master template: it is Brand Styles > Email > Customize layout > logo type (Logo / Icon / Text / None), separate from the invoice and checkout logo. Test site set to None (was Logo, Large, centred).\n135:- Master template notes line (\"Obico was previously known…\") cleared on the test site and moved into the Obico half of the Obico Admin signature:\n139:Which emails need their own text changed: the live site has 19 customer emails on (test site: the same plus a coupon notice). Read on the test site, 17 are brand-neutral apart from the logo and sign-off, now handled site-wide. Obico-specific text remains only in:\n140:- Welcome (done on the test site).\n141:- \"Your subscription is about to expire\": two Detective Hour paragraphs. Its editor opens read-only on the test site (greyed settings, empty version menu, typing does nothing); the \"Payment failed\" email does too, and so does the welcome email since it was published. Cause unknown; Chargebee's banner on every editor: \"You can enable only one notification for an email group on this plan.\" Not resolved.\n144:Each test-site email has \"Push to live site\" (/notifications/<id>/push_to_live_ui); the custom field has \"Publish to Live\".\n146:## 2026-11-10: conditional blocks dropped, test site reverted\n150:blocks tried on the test site\", \"Logo removed for everyone\") are superseded.\n152:Reverted on thespaghettidetective-test (the live site was never touched):\n155:- Master template notes line: back to the italic\n159:- Segment-only welcome notification: already gone.\n169:Test data still on the test site (not deleted, needs Kenneth's yes):\n170:- Customer field cf_product.\n173:- Staging customers jusprinv2-490/491/492 have cf_product=jusprin2 set.\n177:On thespaghettidetective-test:\n180:- Cleared cf_product on staging customers jusprinv2-490, 491 and 492. The\n182:- Archived, then discarded, the customer field \"Product (cf_product)\". The\n183:  Custom Fields page now shows no fields. Nothing was published to live.\n184:A scan of all 54 test-site customers found no other customer with cf_product.\n189:invite accepted. Only the test site exists so far: jusprinv2-test.chargebee.com.\n198:Catalog created on the test site (copied from Obico's test site):\n247:- jusprinv2-test: Payment Preferences › Transaction Descriptor set to \"JUSPRIN\" (test site only).\n256:- Test site webhook whv1_6oqeEVabRMPf1Szz -> https://app-stg.obico.io/ent/jusprin/v2/cb_webhook.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"cb9a71bd-e6d9-4a57-9e7f-6e245ec0b705","timestamp":"2026-11-10T21:16:39.955Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"total 120\ndrwx------   9 kenneth  staff    288 Nov 10 10:35 .\ndrwx------  46 kenneth  staff   1472 Nov  9 20:58 ..\n-rw-r--r--   1 kenneth  staff  22913 Nov 10 12:32 chargebee-jusprin-emails-draft.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 kenneth  staff   5028 Nov  9 18:56 chargebee-readiness-2026-11-09.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 kenneth  staff   5615 Nov 10 10:35 jusprin1-users-and-obico-discount-report.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 kenneth  staff   6622 Nov  9 21:49 jusprinv2-prod-rollout-state.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 kenneth  staff   2331 Nov  9 18:53 prod-ingress-kubectl-diff.txt\n-rw-r--r--   1 kenneth  staff   2350 Nov  9 18:56 proposed-billing-fix.patch\n-rw-r--r--   1 kenneth  staff    770 Nov  9 22:05 proposed-cf-product.patch\n5:are switched on, whether the \"Print Smart, - The Obico team\" lines live in each template or in the\n7:template can pick its own sender profile.\n32:- Proposed instead: a customer custom field on both Chargebee sites, `cf_product`, which the server\n35:  receipt included. Tested on the test site 2026-11-10: a customer create carrying `cf_product`\n40:- Not yet confirmed: the exact merge-field name Chargebee gives a customer custom field\n41:  (expected `{{customer.cf_product}}`; to check in the template editor's field list).\n46:   the segment `cf_product = jusprin2`, with its own subject and body, and possibly its own sender\n49:2. **Conditional blocks** (works on any plan): in each existing template, the JusPrin text inside\n50:   `{{#customer.cf_product = jusprin2}} … {{/customer.cf_product = jusprin2}}` and the current Obico\n51:   text inside `{{^customer.cf_product = jusprin2}} … {{/customer.cf_product = jusprin2}}`. Sender,\n98:1. Create the `cf_product` customer field on the test site; add the conditional blocks (or segments) there; send Chargebee's test mail for each and read them.\n99:2. Server: set `cf_product` in `ensure_customer`; deploy to staging; one staging checkout to see the field arrive.\n100:3. Live site, with Kenneth's yes: the same field, the same template edits, and (with segments) the sender profile. This has to happen before the JusPrin 2 plans and pack go on sale on the live site.\n107:- Segments are saved subscription filters. Test site: created segment \"JusPrin 2 plans\" = plan starts with `jusprin-` AND plan does not contain `unlimited` (matches only JusPrin 2 Hobby/Workshop; plan name filters don't work, ids do).\n108:- Adding a second \"Active subscription is created\" email for that segment shows: \"You can enable only one notification for an email group on this plan. To use more notifications on your Live site, upgrade to higher plan.\" So a JusPrin version beside Obico's needs a Chargebee upgrade on the live site. Public pricing lists segmentation and multiple notifications from the \"Flow\" plan, \"$99 + 0.65%\"; the actual upgrade price is via the account manager.\n109:- Test-site leftovers from this check: segment \"JusPrin 2 plans\"; an unpublished, not-enabled \"Active subscription is created\" email for that segment (notification 7508689). A segment change on the Obico welcome email was discarded.\n111:## Conditional blocks tried on the test site (2026-11-10, Kenneth chose conditional blocks)\n114:- Heading, body and closing paragraph: per email, accept `{{#customer.cf_product = jusprin2}}`. Merge name confirmed in the editor's field list: `customer.cf_product`.\n116:- Obico logo at the top and the italic \"Obico was previously known as…\" line: the master template, shared by every email. The notes line refuses conditionals (\"Mustache not allowed in notes\"); the logo is an image block. Email bodies offer only text, button and section blocks, no image.\n118:Changed on the test site (originals in the session scratchpad, test_site_originals.txt):\n119:- Obico Admin signature: `{{^C}}Print Smart,{{/C}}{{#C}}Happy printing,{{/C}}` / `{{^C}}- The Obico team{{/C}}{{#C}}The JusPrin team{{/C}}` (C = customer.cf_product = jusprin2).\n121:- Master template: unchanged.\n124:Result, read in each customer's Email Logs preview (delivery itself bounced: Gmail rejects admin@obico.io mail from the test site under obico.io's DMARC policy; the live site's copies do arrive):\n125:- jusprinv2-mailtest-jp (cf_product = jusprin2): \"Welcome to JusPrin\", the JusPrin body, the support line, \"Happy printing, / The JusPrin team\". Still Obico's logo at the top and \"Obico was previously known as…\" at the bottom.\n126:- jusprinv2-mailtest-ob (no cf_product): the Obico email exactly as before.\n128:Proposed server change: proposed-cf-product.patch in this folder (adds cf_product to Customer.create in ensure_customer). Not applied, no test covers ensure_customer.\n130:New test-site leftovers: customer field cf_product, customers jusprinv2-mailtest-jp and -ob (k@thespaghettidetective.com) with active JusPrin Hobby subscriptions and unpaid invoices.\n132:## Logo removed for everyone (Kenneth, 2026-11-10: \"Remove logo for all\") — done on the test site\n134:- The email logo is not part of the master template: it is Brand Styles > Email > Customize layout > logo type (Logo / Icon / Text / None), separate from the invoice and checkout logo. Test site set to None (was Logo, Large, centred).\n135:- Master template notes line (\"Obico was previously known…\") cleared on the test site and moved into the Obico half of the Obico Admin signature:\n139:Which emails need their own text changed: the live site has 19 customer emails on (test site: the same plus a coupon notice). Read on the test site, 17 are brand-neutral apart from the logo and sign-off, now handled site-wide. Obico-specific text remains only in:\n140:- Welcome (done on the test site).\n141:- \"Your subscription is about to expire\": two Detective Hour paragraphs. Its editor opens read-only on the test site (greyed settings, empty version menu, typing does nothing); the \"Payment failed\" email does too, and so does the welcome email since it was published. Cause unknown; Chargebee's banner on every editor: \"You can enable only one notification for an email group on this plan.\" Not resolved.\n144:Each test-site email has \"Push to live site\" (/notifications/<id>/push_to_live_ui); the custom field has \"Publish to Live\".\n146:## 2026-11-10: conditional blocks dropped, test site reverted\n150:blocks tried on the test site\", \"Logo removed for everyone\") are superseded.\n152:Reverted on thespaghettidetective-test (the live site was never touched):\n155:- Master template notes line: back to the italic\n159:- Segment-only welcome notification: already gone.\n169:Test data still on the test site (not deleted, needs Kenneth's yes):\n170:- Customer field cf_product.\n173:- Staging customers jusprinv2-490/491/492 have cf_product=jusprin2 set.\n177:On thespaghettidetective-test:\n180:- Cleared cf_product on staging customers jusprinv2-490, 491 and 492. The\n182:- Archived, then discarded, the customer field \"Product (cf_product)\". The\n183:  Custom Fields page now shows no fields. Nothing was published to live.\n184:A scan of all 54 test-site customers found no other customer with cf_product.\n189:invite accepted. Only the test site exists so far: jusprinv2-test.chargebee.com.\n198:Catalog created on the test site (copied from Obico's test site):\n247:- jusprinv2-test: Payment Preferences › Transaction Descriptor set to \"JUSPRIN\" (test site only).\n256:- Test site webhook whv1_6oqeEVabRMPf1Szz -> https://app-stg.obico.io/ent/jusprin/v2/cb_webhook.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3464b35e-cb55-41c2-ae11-0600bace0b99","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-dev","slug":"rosy-bubbling-whisper"}
