:"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-dev","slug":"rosy-bubbling-whisper"}
{"parentUuid":"e832a8df-f5a9-4b57-bab2-f3d36a6e9f78","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d3cef047-f25f-4980-9952-f7c49a687725","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011T5bA7dA1DQnqv5JonYhc1","type":"tool_result","content":"## 2026-11-10: conditional blocks dropped, test site reverted\n\nKenneth chose a separate Chargebee site for JusPrin 2 billing instead of\nJusPrin text inside Obico's emails. The two sections above (\"Conditional\nblocks tried on the test site\", \"Logo removed for everyone\") are superseded.\n\nReverted on thespaghettidetective-test (the live site was never touched):\n- Email logo: back to Logo, Large, centred.\n- Sender signature: back to \"Print Smart, / - The Obico team\".\n- Master template notes line: back to the italic\n  'Obico was previously known as \"The Spaghetti Detective\".'\n- Welcome email for Active subscriptions: heading, body and closing paragraph\n  back to the original text, published.\n- Segment-only welcome notification: already gone.\n- Subscription filter \"JusPrin 2 plans\": deleted.\n\nChecked with a real event: a new subscription (6oqeEVaaXFuwbzn, invoice 1072)\non customer jusprinv2-mailtest-ob produced the original Obico welcome email\n(Obico logo, \"Thank you for supporting Obico!\", the Detective Hour note,\n\"Print Smart, - The Obico team\", the \"previously known\" line). Seen in the\ncustomer's Email Logs preview; delivery bounces as usual because test-site\nmail from admin@obico.io fails obico.io's DMARC policy.\n\nTest data still on the test site (not deleted, needs Kenneth's yes):\n- Customer field cf_product.\n- Customers jusprinv2-mailtest-jp and jusprinv2-mailtest-ob (jusprin-hobby-monthly\n  subscriptions; invoices 1070, 1071, 1072 paid offline).\n- Staging customers jusprinv2-490/491/492 have cf_product=jusprin2 set.\n\n## 2026-11-10: test data removed (Kenneth said yes)\n\nOn thespaghettidetective-test:\n- Deleted customers jusprinv2-mailtest-jp and jusprinv2-mailtest-ob. Their five\n  subscriptions and invoices 1068-1072 are gone with them (API returns not found).\n- Cleared cf_product on staging customers jusprinv2-490, 491 and 492. The\n  customers themselves, their subscriptions and invoices are untouched.\n- Archived, then discarded, the customer field \"Product (cf_product)\". The\n  Custom Fields page now shows no fields. Nothing was published to live.\nA scan of all 54 test-site customers found no other customer with cf_product.\n\n## 2026-11-10: separate JusPrin Chargebee site","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"52df28f7-b6e5-4a9e-8a11-a2046bbf68ce","timestamp":"2026-11-10T21:16:42.611Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## 2026-11-10: conditional blocks dropped, test site reverted\n\nKenneth chose a separate Chargebee site for JusPrin 2 billing instead of\nJusPrin text inside Obico's emails. The two sections above (\"Conditional\nblocks tried on the test site\", \"Logo removed for everyone\") are superseded.\n\nReverted on thespaghettidetective-test (the live site was never touched):\n- Email logo: back to Logo, Large, centred.\n- Sender signature: back to \"Print Smart, / - The Obico team\".\n- Master template notes line: back to the italic\n  'Obico was previously known as \"The Spaghetti Detective\".'\n- Welcome email for Active subscriptions: heading, body and closing paragraph\n  back to the original text, published.\n- Segment-only welcome notification: already gone.\n- Subscription filter \"JusPrin 2 plans\": deleted.\n\nChecked with a real event: a new subscription (6oqeEVaaXFuwbzn, invoice 1072)\non customer jusprinv2-mailtest-ob produced the original Obico welcome email\n(Obico logo, \"Thank you for supporting Obico!\", the Detective Hour note,\n\"Print Smart, - The Obico team\", the \"previously known\" line). Seen in the\ncustomer's Email Logs preview; delivery bounces as usual because test-site\nmail from admin@obico.io fails obico.io's DMARC policy.\n\nTest data still on the test site (not deleted, needs Kenneth's yes):\n- Customer field cf_product.\n- Customers jusprinv2-mailtest-jp and jusprinv2-mailtest-ob (jusprin-hobby-monthly\n  subscriptions; invoices 1070, 1071, 1072 paid offline).\n- Staging customers jusprinv2-490/491/492 have cf_product=jusprin2 set.\n\n## 2026-11-10: test data removed (Kenneth said yes)\n\nOn thespaghettidetective-test:\n- Deleted customers jusprinv2-mailtest-jp and jusprinv2-mailtest-ob. Their five\n  subscriptions and invoices 1068-1072 are gone with them (API returns not found).\n- Cleared cf_product on staging customers jusprinv2-490, 491 and 492. The\n  customers themselves, their subscriptions and invoices are untouched.\n- Archived, then discarded, the customer field \"Product (cf_product)\". The\n  Custom Fields page now shows no fields. Nothing was published to live.\nA scan of all 54 test-site customers found no other customer with cf_product.\n\n## 2026-11-10: separate JusPrin Chargebee site","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e832a8df-f5a9-4b57-bab2-f3d36a6e9f78","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-dev","slug":"rosy-bubbling-whisper"}
