{"parentUuid":"201b47f2-a7f0-49cd-b343-dd6a3735bec7","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6a301c32-76b1-44fc-b776-34066675e090","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"Exit code 1\n# jusprinv2.obico.io production rollout — state (session local_3e38de32 side session)\n\n- gcloud on this Mac fails (Homebrew's /opt/homebrew/opt/openssl@3 link is gone; openssl@4 is linked).\n  Workaround: export CLOUDSDK_PYTHON=$HOME/.local/share/uv/python/cpython-3.12.9-macos-aarch64-none/bin/python3.12\n- Release commit, local only, not pushed: tsd-enterprise worktree ~/Projects/tsd-enterprise-worktrees/release-jusprinv2-prod,\n  commit 1cbd23803e = master 0a75568378 + obi.4096's built bundles (da838aefa1). Differs from obi.4096's release only in\n  web_ent/settings_ent.py and last_ent_commit.txt. Push with: git push -f origin HEAD:release\n- Ops edits, uncommitted: tsd/gcp/jusprin-managed-cert.yaml (gke-managed-cert-jusprinv2-app), tsd/gcp/neg-ingress.yaml\n  (annotation + jusprinv2.obico.io rule). kubectl diff saved in prod-ingress-kubectl-diff.txt here.\n- Prod DB: syndicates base(1), kingroon(2); app_syndicate_id_seq last_value 1, is_called false -> reset needed.\n  Google SocialApp \"Obico Google+\" id 1, client 268097575721-ubm4silcbif4sgsc6qpfuc91403s04o2 (project gettsdapp-843e9).\n- Migration hazard: obico-server 0086_sitesyndicate drops app_syndicate_sites; obi.4088 pods read it for logged-out page loads.\n- Staging test accounts made 2026-11-09: k+rollout-stg-obico-1109@obico.io (app-stg.obico.io), k+rollout-stg-kingroon-1109@obico.io (app-stg.kingroon.com).\n- Gateway gap confirmed 2026-11-09: live ConfigMap jusprin-v2-gateway-prod = old one-alias config (matches repo); Secret\n  jusprin-v2-gateway-prod has only ANTHROPIC and OPENAI keys. Prepared, uncommitted: prod/jusprin-v2-gateway.yaml = staging's\n  config (names only differ); prod/tsdws-prod.yaml gains JUSPRIN_OPENROUTER_API_KEY from that Secret. The Secret key must\n  exist before tsdws-prod is applied, or new ws pods fail to start.\n- 2026-11-10 ~03:00 UTC: Google redirect URI https://jusprinv2.obico.io/accounts/google/login/callback/ saved on client 268097575721-ubm4... (Kenneth asked). Namecheap A record NOT added yet: Namecheap needs Kenneth to sign in (Chrome tab open).\n- Prod Secret jusprin-v2-gateway-prod now has JUSPRIN_OPENROUTER_API_KEY (Kenneth's key from /tmp/openrouter-prod.key; OpenRouter says limit $50, usage 0).\n- Staging migration tests 03:08-03:14 UTC (probe logs in this session's scratchpad stgtest/): obi.4088 on migrated DB: logged-out pages 500 on every brand, /hc/ 200, signed-in API and pages 200; fresh process fails build_full_url_for_syndicate (ProgrammingError). obi.4096 on reverse-migrated DB: every request 500. Rollback that works: undo images first, then `migrate app 0085` from a runner pod (deployment pod template, new image, no service label, sleep). Staging restored to obi.4096, mapping unchanged.\n- Last prod web rollout (obi.4088, 2026-11-08): 06:07:04 first new pod -> 06:10:23 last old pod stopped, + 120 s preStop.\n\n## 2026-11-10 03:57 UTC — rollout finished, smoke test waiting on Kenneth\n- All four prod deployments (web, ws, tasks, rttasks) on obi.4098; tsdbeat-prod unchanged on obi.4036.\n- Mixed-version window on prod: 03:43:14–03:46:11 UTC (Sentry issues 2038 and 2039, 294 events in all, \"relation app_syndicate_sites does not exist\"). Nothing since then. The probe of app.obico.io and app.thespaghettidetective.com returned 656/656 200 since 03:47.\n- Sentry 2040: one scanner hit jusprinv2.obico.io/accounts/login/ at 03:46:15, before the Site row existed. Not a regression.\n- ManagedCertificate gke-managed-cert-jusprinv2-app is Active.\n- jusprinv2.obico.io answers like jusprinv2-stg: login and signup 404, password reset 200, /hc/ 200.\n- tsdws-prod scale-down per prod/release.sh: 12→11 at ~04:16 UTC, 11→10 at ~04:21 (scratchpad/scaledown.sh, pid 63215).\n- migrate-runner-prod pod kept until the smoke test passes.\n- The smoke test needs Kenneth: this Mac caches a \"not found\" DNS answer for jusprinv2.obico.io for ~75 min unless flushed with sudo. He also has to do the two production sign-ups.\n\n## 2026-11-10 ~04:55 UTC — smoke test passed, ops committed (not pushed)\n- Kenneth signed up on production from the test app: user 263740 k+jusprinv2-smoke@obico.io (emailed code) and 263741 k@obico.io (Google). Each got a 500-credit signup grant expiring 2026-12-10.\n- Gateway on production, called with the app's saved key: Standard (responses format, OpenRouter DeepSeek) and Expert (anthropic format, Claude) both answered; charged 1 and 5 credits, 494 left on 263741.\n- Credits and plans and Billing and usage pages open signed in through /ent/jusprin/v2/web_link and show the right balance and usage rows. No checkout attempted.\n- No Sentry issues in obico-server or obico-frontend since 03:47. tsdws-prod scaled 12→10. migrate-runner-prod deleted.\n- ~/Projects/ops commit d9d4cc1; master is 52 commits ahead of origin, push waits on Kenneth.\n\n## 2026-11-10 ~05:00 UTC — chats in the real app\n- ops pushed: GitHub master d9d4cc1 (the \"51 unpushed\" was a stale tracking ref; origin's fetch refspec maps to refs/remotes/git/*).\n- In the test app (signed in as k@obico.io): Expert chat answered with a tool call, 5 credits; Standard chat answered correctly, 1 credit; titles free. 488 credits left.\n- App's Billing and usage sheet opens from Preferences and shows usage.\n- Found: Home's AI card stays at \"500 credits left\" (server 488); first-run JusPrin 1 import page names the previously signed-in account. Standard chat titled with an answer sentence. Follow-up proposed as task_e1be45b4.\n\n## 2026-11-10 — chat capture\n- Kenneth decided \"opt-in first\": production keeps no chats until there's a per-person opt-in (published privacy policy promises opt-in for AI training). JUSPRIN_V2_CAPTURE_CONTAINER stays blank in prod. Opt-in work proposed as task_6ad51eec.\n- Buck