ate_plan","type":"assistant","uuid":"7eb5c3b8-d2ba-475a-9c26-8c754b0e324b","timestamp":"2026-11-10T21:25:10.979Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-dev","slug":"rosy-bubbling-whisper"}
{"parentUuid":"7eb5c3b8-d2ba-475a-9c26-8c754b0e324b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6a301c32-76b1-44fc-b776-34066675e090","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CCJALUxhTjTS6oSkLJatxX","type":"tool_result","content":"## 2026-11-10: separate JusPrin Chargebee site\n\nKenneth signed up the site jusprinv2 and invited k@thespaghettidetective.com;\ninvite accepted. Only the test site exists so far: jusprinv2-test.chargebee.com.\nNo live site until Kenneth activates it.\n\nThe site is on Product Catalog 2.0 (Chargebee's default for sites created since\nMay 2021). billing.py and v2/views.py use 1.0 calls (checkout_new/existing/\none_time with plan_id and addons; subscription.plan_id; invoice line\nentity_type 'addon'), so the server change is a port to the *_for_items\ncalls, not just env=.\n\nCatalog created on the test site (copied from Obico's test site):\n- Product family jusprin.\n- Plan jusprin-hobby, price jusprin-hobby-monthly: USD 10/month flat, forever.\n- Plan jusprin-workshop, price jusprin-workshop-monthly: USD 20/month flat.\n- Charge (one-off) jusprin-credit-pack, price jusprin-credit-pack-USD: USD 10.\n  External name \"JusPrin Credit Pack (500 credits)\".\n- Coupon jusprin2-obico-premium-20: 20% off, forever, each specified item,\n  limited to the two plan prices above.\nThe site also carries Chargebee's sample family \"OmniSupport Solutions\"; left alone.\n\nNot done yet: API key, payment gateway, branding, sender email, emails,\nwebhook, server port.\n\n## Server port to JusPrin's own site (2026-11-10)\n\nWorktree /Users/kenneth/Projects/tsd-enterprise-worktrees/jusprin-v2-own-chargebee, branch jusprin-v2-own-chargebee-site from tsd-enterprise master f9516b3f3e. Uncommitted, not pushed.\n\n- billing.py calls the site in JUSPRIN_V2_CHARGEBEE_SITE / JUSPRIN_V2_CHARGEBEE_API_KEY on every call (chargebee-python env=), using Product Catalog 2.0 calls (checkout_new/existing/one_time_for_items, cancel_for_items). Pack = charge item price jusprin-credit-pack-USD.\n- New webhook /ent/jusprin/v2/cb_webhook: takes only the event id from the post and reads the event back from the JusPrin site. Obico's two webhooks no longer grant JusPrin 2 credits.\n- Tests: 33/33 billing + account-delete tests pass (21 of them fail on master); full jusprin + app_ent suites 281 pass.\n- Real run on jusprinv2-test with the test card (local user 62, customer jusprinv2-62):\n  - Pack: 500 + 500 launch bonus, once on repeat.\n  - Hobby: 750 + 750, once. Card line \"Visa ending 1111\".\n  - Switch to Workshop: same subscription, prorated $10; Hobby lots expired, Workshop 1000 + 1000 once.\n  - Cancel: Chargebee non_renewing, plan expired_at = term end.\n  - Webhook fed the 34 real event ids (each twice) rebuilt identical grants; forged id -> 400.\n  - Account delete endpoint: 204, user gone, subscription cancelled at once.\n- Test-site setting changed: Self-Serve Portal access \"Via Chargebee Login\" -> \"Via Single Sign On API\" (same as Obico's site). Without it the portal link fails with \"Customer portal access via API is disabled\".\n- docs/jusprin2-host-setup.md gained a Chargebee section (env vars, catalog ids, checkout/portal settings, webhook URL, check).\n- Before this deploys to staging: set the two env vars on the staging web pods and add the webhook on jusprinv2-test, or every checkout fails.\n- Left in place on jusprinv2-test: customer jusprinv2-62 with its paid invoices and the cancelled subscription (test data). The site also carries Chargebee's cbdemo_* sample catalog.\n\n## The three billing bugs, fixed (2026-11-10)\n\n- tsd-enterprise 161e2747a2 on jusprin-v2-own-chargebee-site (not pushed): a term is granted only with no unpaid invoice (payment_succeeded re-records it); a switch back reopens that plan's lots and ends the other's; the webhook reads the subscription's current state; /v2/account sends ends_at and renews_at null for a cancelled plan.\n- JusPrin 6f1f03867d on claude/plan-ends-line from jusprin-dev (worktree /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin-worktrees/plan-ends-line, not pushed): Preferences shows \"Ends <day>.\" from ends_at.\n- Each reproduced on jusprinv2-test with real events before, checked after (customers jusprinv2-63..66; 66 has an unpaid Hobby invoice left on purpose). Server suites 287 pass; AgentUI 713 pass.\n- Supersedes proposed-billing-fix.patch (written for Obico's site).\n\n## Payment gateways on jusprinv2-test (2026-11-10)\n\n- Stripe: connected through Stripe Connect to TSD Technology's existing Stripe account (acct_1CrFhqLPS4omY4v8), in test mode. Card checkout tested.\n- PayPal: connected through PayPal Commerce Platform to TSD's existing PayPal developer sandbox (merchant k-facilitator@getanywhere.io); Chargebee gateway gw_16A02yVabCJbx1EDR. Smart Routing sends PayPal payments there and cards to Stripe.\n- PayPal test, local user 67 (k+jp2-paypal-1110@obico.io): Hobby checkout paid by sandbox buyer k-buyer@getanywhere.io. Chargebee: subscription 16BVT5VabCPhi1GNx active, transaction txn_AzZNCSVabEVg2Cjl $10.00 success, PayPal id 4A210709LW2776028, payment source pm_AzZNCSVabEWZlCk0 valid with a billing agreement (auto collection on, so renewals can charge it). Server: finish_checkout gave 750 Hobby + 750 launch bonus to 10 Dec, total 2,000 with the 500 sign-up credits.\n- Trap: Chrome autofills the sandbox login with k-facilitator, and PayPal refuses \"This PayPal account is associated with the merchant\". Sign out at sandbox.paypal.com/signout and use k-buyer.\n- Chargebee's PayPal page warns that \"Reference Transactions\" must be enabled on the PayPal account for recurring charges. The sandbox issued a billing agreement anyway; on the live PayPal business account it must be checked (ask PayPal support if it isn't on).\n- None of this carries to the live site: Chargebee says each gateway must be connected again there.\n\n## Statement text (2026-11-10, Kenneth asked via local_a7a3e9c2)\n- jusprinv2-test: Payment Preferences › Transaction Descriptor set to \"JUSPRIN\" (test site only).\n- Stripe test charge after it (invoice 13, txn_16BVT5VabK91I1Msu, ch_3UaKtqLPS4omY4v81d5L4E7h, tok_visa on jusprinv2-64): statement descriptor \"OBICO* JUSPRIN\". The earlier charge ch_3UaK4TLPS4omY4v80bzVaUPo (before the setting) read \"OBICO/THE SPAGHETTI DE\".\n- PayPal sandbox charge after it (invoice 12, txn_AzZi3mVabK3T51N93, PayPal 48G06919G5813131X, reference transaction on jusprinv2-67's billing agreement): Completed; NVP GetTransactionDetails has no soft-descriptor field, so the PayPal statement line is unverified.\n- Obico live today (read only): no Transaction Descriptor; a real charge from today reads \"OBICO/THE SPAGHETTI DE\". Stripe public name \"Obico/The Spaghetti Detective\", support admin@obico.io, +1 (408) 889-3920. Chargebee business profile \"Obico\", 1790 Willow Lake Ln, San Jose CA 95131, +1 (404) 565-4264. Emails from \"Obico Admin <admin@obico.io>\". PayPal gateway: PayPal Express Checkout. Live PayPal business name/soft descriptor not read: paypal.com asks for sign-in.\n- jusprinv2-test: no organization address; invoice PDF has no business name, logo or address.\n\n## Staging on JusPrin's own Chargebee site (2026-11-10 ~20:35 UTC)\n- tsd-enterprise master: 77fd19cadb (port), 2d97f4b1c7 (billing fixes), a72b271f7e (JUSPRIN_V2_CHARGEBEE_CUSTOMER_PREFIX). Release 66519ff80f = obi.4104 (bundles reused from 1cbd23803e). Old local branch jusprin-v2-own-chargebee-site kept; its rebased copy is jusprin-v2-own-chargebee-on-master.\n- Staging (all four deployments) on obi.4104; tsdweb-stg has REDACTED, the staging key Kenneth made, REDACTED. ops commit 1e6caf7, not pushed (on top of another session's unpushed 3f5e1b7).\n- Test site webhook whv1_6oqeEVabRMPf1Szz -> https://app-stg.obico.io/ent/jusprin/v2/cb_webhook.\n- Checked on jusprinv2-stg.obico.io in Chrome: pack (user 497) 500+500 once, invoice 14; Hobby (498) 750+750, plan recorded; Premium (499) prices page and cart show $8 with the coupon (not paid); cancel (498): non_renewing, /v2/account renews_at null, ends_at 10 Dec. Customers jusprinv2-stg-497/498/499.\n- One webhook delivery got 400 because Chargebee's event lookup lagged the post; Chargebee retried ~80 s later and it succeeded.\n- Production is on obi.4098. Releasing master to production before the live site, its key and webhook exist breaks JusPrin 2 checkout there.\n\n#####\n# JusPrin 2 Chargebee and production readiness, checked 2026-11-09\n\n## Chargebee objects (read-only API, both sites on Product Catalog 1.0, USD only)\n\n| Object | Test site (thespaghettidetective-test) | Live site (thespaghettidetective) |\n|---|---|---|\n| plan jusprin-hobby-monthly | exists, $10/month, invoice name \"JusPrin Hobby\" | missing |\n| plan jusprin-workshop-monthly | exists, $20/month, \"JusPrin Workshop\" | missing |\n| addon jusprin-credit-pack | was missing; created by this session 2026-11-09: $10, non_recurring, invoice name \"JusPrin Credit Pack (500 credits)\" | missing |\n| coupon jusprin2-obico-premium-20 | exists, 20%, forever, only the two plans | missing |\n| One-time checkout setting | OFF: hosted_pages/checkout_one_time answers \"One time checkout is not enabled under Checkout & Self-Serve Portal\" | not checked (no read-only way); assume off |\n| Webhook endpoint | app-stg.obico.io/ent/cb_webhook/ (delivers; JusPrin 2 handler runs first) | app.thespaghettidetective.com/ent/cb_webhook/ reaches prod; nothing new needed |\n\nPrices in GET /v2/account match: pack 1000 cents/500 credits, Hobby 1000/750, Workshop 2000/1000.\nNo yearly JusPrin 2 price ids in the code. Customer ids jusprinv2-<user id> are created on first checkout.\nLocal docker stack and staging share the test site, so jusprinv2-<id> can collide between them (test-only nuisance).\n\n## Staging runs (accounts k+cb1109-{pack,plan,prem,fail}@obico.io, users 490-493; Obico base user 494 with a fake paid Subscription)\n\nNo card was entered anywhere. Payments were simulated with offline payments recorded on the Chargebee test site.\n\n- Guest prices page (?guest=1): right prices, \"Sign up to buy\".\n- Signed-in prices page: right; Premium address shows $10→$8, $20→$16.\n- Plan checkout for the Premium address: Chargebee page shows \"JusPrin Hobby $10.00 / Obico Premium 20% off -$2.00 / $8.00\", Obico logo, a \"Remove\" link on the coupon.\n- Pack checkout: fails (\"Checkout couldn't start. Nothing was charged\") because of the one-time checkout setting.\n- Pack via webhook (invoice 1064 paid): pack 500 + launch_bonus 500, source_ref invoice:1064, once.\n- Hobby subscription: 750 + 750 granted at subscription_created **while invoice 1065 was still unpaid** (due_invoices_count 1).\n- Hobby→Workshop: Hobby lots expired, Workshop 1000+1000 granted once. Correct.\n- Workshop→Hobby same term: Hobby lots stay expired, Workshop's 2000 stay live. Bug.\n- Cancel from server billing page: Chargebee non_renewing, billing page \"Ends 10 Dec.\", but /v2/account still sends renews_at only, so Preferences.tsx:218 shows \"Renews 10 Dec.\".\n- Portal link: redirects to Chargebee portal session. Card line absent (no card on file, expected).\n- Not tested: entering a test card, the done page after a real hosted checkout, a failed card, the desktop app UI.\n\n## Emails\n- No Chargebee mail reached the k+…@obico.io test addresses. Chargebee docs: a test site mails only the domain it was created with unless support whitelists another.\n- Live site mails (BCC to k@obico.io): from \"Obico Admin <admin@obico.io>\". \"Thanks for subscribing\" says \"THANK YOU FOR SUPPORTING OBICO!\", links Detective Hour docs, signed \"The Obico team\". Failed payment: \"[Important] We couldn't charge your Card\". JusPrin 2 buyers get these as they are unless templates gain plan-conditional blocks ({{#plan.id = jusprin-hobby-monthly}}) or segmentation (plan-tier dependent).\n- \"OctoPrint Anywhere <admin@thespaghettidetective.com>\" mails come from another Chargebee site (getanywhere), unrelated.\n- Live \"[Chargebee] Webhook failure\" mails come from Sentry OBICO-SERVER-AS7 (User.DoesNotExist in Obico's email path, since 2026-08-12), not JusPrin 2.\n- Sentry OBICO-SERVER-B22 (JSONDecodeError at /ent/cb_webhook/, 2026-11-10 02:46 UTC) was this session's HEAD probe of the prod webhook URL. Harmless; resolve it.\n\n## Production settings vs staging\n- tsdweb-prod/tsdws-prod run obi.4088; staging obi.4096. 4088 lacks JUSPRIN_V2_MIN_APP_VERSION, sign-in mail from jusprin-support@obico.io, host-based brands.\n- ConfigMap jusprin-v2-gateway-prod is the old shape: obi.4088 itself rejects it (\"alias is missing ['credits', 'tier']\"). No slicer-basic alias. Staging's has both.\n- tsdws-prod lacks JUSPRIN_OPENROUTER_API_KEY (staging has it; needed by slicer-basic).\n- Prod DB: no jusprinv2 syndicate, no jusprinv2.obico.io Site. DNS for jusprinv2.obico.io does not resolve. No prod managed cert or ingress rule. All covered by ops tsd/RUNBOOK.md \"JusPrin's host\".\n- JUSPRIN_V2_MIN_APP_VERSION blank on both. JUSPRIN_V2_CAPTURE_CONTAINER blank on both (chats are not kept).\n- Other web env names identical between stg and prod.\n\n## Proposed server fix (not applied, not tested)\nproposed-billing-fix.patch in this folder: grant a term only when the subscription has no unpaid invoices, grant it on payment_succeeded otherwise, and reopen a plan's lots on a switch back. Separately /v2/account needs an \"ends\" signal (plan.expired_at) and Preferences.tsx needs \"Ends <day>.\" when set.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"3b6ee93a-d12f-41e5-a679-f38c67969f11","timestamp":"2026-11-10T21:25:11.360Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## 2026-11-10: separate JusPrin Chargebee site\n\nKenneth signed up the site jusprinv2 and invited k@thespaghettidetective.com;\ninvite accepted. Only the test site exists so far: jusprinv2-test.chargebee.com.\nNo live site until Kenneth activates it.\n\nThe site is on Product Catalog 2.0 (Chargebee's default for sites created since\nMay 2021). billing.py and v2/views.py use 1.0 calls (checkout_new/existing/\none_time with plan_id and addons; subscription.plan_id; invoice line\nentity_type 'addon'), so the server change is a port to the *_for_items\ncalls, not just env=.\n\nCatalog created on the test site (copied from Obico's test site):\n- Product family jusprin.\n- Plan jusprin-hobby, price jusprin-hobby-monthly: USD 10/month flat, forever.\n- Plan jusprin-workshop, price jusprin-workshop-monthly: USD 20/month flat.\n- Charge (one-off) jusprin-credit-pack, price jusprin-credit-pack-USD: USD 10.\n  External name \"JusPrin Credit Pack (500 credits)\".\n- Coupon jusprin2-obico-premium-20: 20% off, forever, each specified item,\n  limited to the two plan prices above.\nThe site also carries Chargebee's sample family \"OmniSupport Solutions\"; left alone.\n\nNot done yet: API key, payment gateway, branding, sender email, emails,\nwebhook, server port.\n\n## Server port to JusPrin's own site (2026-11-10)\n\nWorktree /Users/kenneth/Projects/tsd-enterprise-worktrees/jusprin-v2-own-chargebee, branch jusprin-v2-own-chargebee-site from tsd-enterprise master f9516b3f3e. Uncommitted, not pushed.\n\n- billing.py calls the site in JUSPRIN_V2_CHARGEBEE_SITE / JUSPRIN_V2_CHARGEBEE_API_KEY on every call (chargebee-python env=), using Product Catalog 2.0 calls (checkout_new/existing/one_time_for_items, cancel_for_items). Pack = charge item price jusprin-credit-pack-USD.\n- New webhook /ent/jusprin/v2/cb_webhook: takes only the event id from the post and reads the event back from the JusPrin site. Obico's two webhooks no longer grant JusPrin 2 credits.\n- Tests: 33/33 billing + account-delete tests pass (21 of them fail on master); full jusprin + app_ent suites 281 pass.\n- Real run on jusprinv2-test with the test card (local user 62, customer jusprinv2-62):\n  - Pack: 500 + 500 launch bonus, once on repeat.\n  - Hobby: 750 + 750, once. Card line \"Visa ending 1111\".\n  - Switch to Workshop: same subscription, prorated $10; Hobby lots expired, Workshop 1000 + 1000 once.\n  - Cancel: Chargebee non_renewing, plan expired_at = term end.\n  - Webhook fed the 34 real event ids (each twice) rebuilt identical grants; forged id -> 400.\n  - Account delete endpoint: 204, user gone, subscription cancelled at once.\n- Test-site setting changed: Self-Serve Portal access \"Via Chargebee Login\" -> \"Via Single Sign On API\" (same as Obico's site). Without it the portal link fails with \"Customer portal access via API is disabled\".\n- docs/jusprin2-host-setup.md gained a Chargebee section (env vars, catalog ids, checkout/portal settings, webhook URL, check).\n- Before this deploys to staging: set the two env vars on the staging web pods and add the webhook on jusprinv2-test, or every checkout fails.\n- Left in place on jusprinv2-test: customer jusprinv2-62 with its paid invoices and the cancelled subscription (test data). The site also carries Chargebee's cbdemo_* sample catalog.\n\n## The three billing bugs, fixed (2026-11-10)\n\n- tsd-enterprise 161e2747a2 on jusprin-v2-own-chargebee-site (not pushed): a term is granted only with no unpaid invoice (payment_succeeded re-records it); a switch back reopens that plan's lots and ends the other's; the webhook reads the subscription's current state; /v2/account sends ends_at and renews_at null for a cancelled plan.\n- JusPrin 6f1f03867d on claude/plan-ends-line from jusprin-dev (worktree /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin-worktrees/plan-ends-line, not pushed): Preferences shows \"Ends <day>.\" from ends_at.\n- Each reproduced on jusprinv2-test with real events before, checked after (customers jusprinv2-63..66; 66 has an unpaid Hobby invoice left on purpose). Server suites 287 pass; AgentUI 713 pass.\n- Supersedes proposed-billing-fix.patch (written for Obico's site).\n\n## Payment gateways on jusprinv2-test (2026-11-10)\n\n- Stripe: connected through Stripe Connect to TSD Technology's existing Stripe account (acct_1CrFhqLPS4omY4v8), in test mode. Card checkout tested.\n- PayPal: connected through PayPal Commerce Platform to TSD's existing PayPal developer sandbox (merchant k-facilitator@getanywhere.io); Chargebee gateway gw_16A02yVabCJbx1EDR. Smart Routing sends PayPal payments there and cards to Stripe.\n- PayPal test, local user 67 (k+jp2-paypal-1110@obico.io): Hobby checkout paid by sandbox buyer k-buyer@getanywhere.io. Chargebee: subscription 16BVT5VabCPhi1GNx active, transaction txn_AzZNCSVabEVg2Cjl $10.00 success, PayPal id 4A210709LW2776028, payment source pm_AzZNCSVabEWZlCk0 valid with a billing agreement (auto collection on, so renewals can charge it). Server: finish_checkout gave 750 Hobby + 750 launch bonus to 10 Dec, total 2,000 with the 500 sign-up credits.\n- Trap: Chrome autofills the sandbox login with k-facilitator, and PayPal refuses \"This PayPal account is associated with the merchant\". Sign out at sandbox.paypal.com/signout and use k-buyer.\n- Chargebee's PayPal page warns that \"Reference Transactions\" must be enabled on the PayPal account for recurring charges. The sandbox issued a billing agreement anyway; on the live PayPal business account it must be checked (ask PayPal support if it isn't on).\n- None of this carries to the live site: Chargebee says each gateway must be connected again there.\n\n## Statement text (2026-11-10, Kenneth asked via local_a7a3e9c2)\n- jusprinv2-test: Payment Preferences › Transaction Descriptor set to \"JUSPRIN\" (test site only).\n- Stripe test charge after it (invoice 13, txn_16BVT5VabK91I1Msu, ch_3UaKtqLPS4omY4v81d5L4E7h, tok_visa on jusprinv2-64): statement descriptor \"OBICO* JUSPRIN\". The earlier charge ch_3UaK4TLPS4omY4v80bzVaUPo (before the setting) read \"OBICO/THE SPAGHETTI DE\".\n- PayPal sandbox charge after it (invoice 12, txn_AzZi3mVabK3T51N93, PayPal 48G06919G5813131X, reference transaction on jusprinv2-67's billing agreement): Completed; NVP GetTransactionDetails has no soft-descriptor field, so the PayPal statement line is unverified.\n- Obico live today (read only): no Transaction Descriptor; a real charge from today reads \"OBICO/THE SPAGHETTI DE\". Stripe public name \"Obico/The Spaghetti Detective\", support admin@obico.io, +1 (408) 889-3920. Chargebee business profile \"Obico\", 1790 Willow Lake Ln, San Jose CA 95131, +1 (404) 565-4264. Emails from \"Obico Admin <admin@obico.io>\". PayPal gateway: PayPal Express Checkout. Live PayPal business name/soft descriptor not read: paypal.com asks for sign-in.\n- jusprinv2-test: no organization address; invoice PDF has no business name, logo or address.\n\n## Staging on JusPrin's own Chargebee site (2026-11-10 ~20:35 UTC)\n- tsd-enterprise master: 77fd19cadb (port), 2d97f4b1c7 (billing fixes), a72b271f7e (JUSPRIN_V2_CHARGEBEE_CUSTOMER_PREFIX). Release 66519ff80f = obi.4104 (bundles reused from 1cbd23803e). Old local branch jusprin-v2-own-chargebee-site kept; its rebased copy is jusprin-v2-own-chargebee-on-master.\n- Staging (all four deployments) on obi.4104; tsdweb-stg has REDACTED, the staging key Kenneth made, REDACTED. ops commit 1e6caf7, not pushed (on top of another session's unpushed 3f5e1b7).\n- Test site webhook whv1_6oqeEVabRMPf1Szz -> https://app-stg.obico.io/ent/jusprin/v2/cb_webhook.\n- Checked on jusprinv2-stg.obico.io in Chrome: pack (user 497) 500+500 once, invoice 14; Hobby (498) 750+750, plan recorded; Premium (499) prices page and cart show $8 with the coupon (not paid); cancel (498): non_renewing, /v2/account renews_at null, ends_at 10 Dec. Customers jusprinv2-stg-497/498/499.\n- One webhook delivery got 400 because Chargebee's event lookup lagged the post; Chargebee retried ~80 s later and it succeeded.\n- Production is on obi.4098. Releasing master to production before the live site, its key and webhook exist breaks JusPrin 2 checkout there.\n\n#####\n# JusPrin 2 Chargebee and production readiness, checked 2026-11-09\n\n## Chargebee objects (read-only API, both sites on Product Catalog 1.0, USD only)\n\n| Object | Test site (thespaghettidetective-test) | Live site (thespaghettidetective) |\n|---|---|---|\n| plan jusprin-hobby-monthly | exists, $10/month, invoice name \"JusPrin Hobby\" | missing |\n| plan jusprin-workshop-monthly | exists, $20/month, \"JusPrin Workshop\" | missing |\n| addon jusprin-credit-pack | was missing; created by this session 2026-11-09: $10, non_recurring, invoice name \"JusPrin Credit Pack (500 credits)\" | missing |\n| coupon jusprin2-obico-premium-20 | exists, 20%, forever, only the two plans | missing |\n| One-time checkout setting | OFF: hosted_pages/checkout_one_time answers \"One time checkout is not enabled under Checkout & Self-Serve Portal\" | not checked (no read-only way); assume off |\n| Webhook endpoint | app-stg.obico.io/ent/cb_webhook/ (delivers; JusPrin 2 handler runs first) | app.thespaghettidetective.com/ent/cb_webhook/ reaches prod; nothing new needed |\n\nPrices in GET /v2/account match: pack 1000 cents/500 credits, Hobby 1000/750, Workshop 2000/1000.\nNo yearly JusPrin 2 price ids in the code. Customer ids jusprinv2-<user id> are created on first checkout.\nLocal docker stack and staging share the test site, so jusprinv2-<id> can collide between them (test-only nuisance).\n\n## Staging runs (accounts k+cb1109-{pack,plan,prem,fail}@obico.io, users 490-493; Obico base user 494 with a fake paid Subscription)\n\nNo card was entered anywhere. Payments were simulated with offline payments recorded on the Chargebee test site.\n\n- Guest prices page (?guest=1): right prices, \"Sign up to buy\".\n- Signed-in prices page: right; Premium address shows $10→$8, $20→$16.\n- Plan checkout for the Premium address: Chargebee page shows \"JusPrin Hobby $10.00 / Obico Premium 20% off -$2.00 / $8.00\", Obico logo, a \"Remove\" link on the coupon.\n- Pack checkout: fails (\"Checkout couldn't start. Nothing was charged\") because of the one-time checkout setting.\n- Pack via webhook (invoice 1064 paid): pack 500 + launch_bonus 500, source_ref invoice:1064, once.\n- Hobby subscription: 750 + 750 granted at subscription_created **while invoice 1065 was still unpaid** (due_invoices_count 1).\n- Hobby→Workshop: Hobby lots expired, Workshop 1000+1000 granted once. Correct.\n- Workshop→Hobby same term: Hobby lots stay expired, Workshop's 2000 stay live. Bug.\n- Cancel from server billing page: Chargebee non_renewing, billing page \"Ends 10 Dec.\", but /v2/account still sends renews_at only, so Preferences.tsx:218 shows \"Renews 10 Dec.\".\n- Portal link: redirects to Chargebee portal session. Card line absent (no card on file, expected).\n- Not tested: entering a test card, the done page after a real hosted checkout, a failed card, the desktop app UI.\n\n## Emails\n- No Chargebee mail reached the k+…@obico.io test addresses. Chargebee docs: a test site mails only the domain it was created with unless support whitelists another.\n- Live site mails (BCC to k@obico.io): from \"Obico Admin <admin@obico.io>\". \"Thanks for subscribing\" says \"THANK YOU FOR SUPPORTING OBICO!\", links Detective Hour docs, signed \"The Obico team\". Failed payment: \"[Important] We couldn't charge your Card\". JusPrin 2 buyers get these as they are unless templates gain plan-conditional blocks ({{#plan.id = jusprin-hobby-monthly}}) or segmentation (plan-tier dependent).\n- \"OctoPrint Anywhere <admin@thespaghettidetective.com>\" mails come from another Chargebee site (getanywhere), unrelated.\n- Live \"[Chargebee] Webhook failure\" mails come from Sentry OBICO-SERVER-AS7 (User.DoesNotExist in Obico's email path, since 2026-08-12), not JusPrin 2.\n- Sentry OBICO-SERVER-B22 (JSONDecodeError at /ent/cb_webhook/, 2026-11-10 02:46 UTC) was this session's HEAD probe of the prod webhook URL. Harmless; resolve it.\n\n## Production settings vs staging\n- tsdweb-prod/tsdws-prod run obi.4088; staging obi.4096. 4088 lacks JUSPRIN_V2_MIN_APP_VERSION, sign-in mail from jusprin-support@obico.io, host-based brands.\n- ConfigMap jusprin-v2-gateway-prod is the old shape: obi.4088 itself rejects it (\"alias is missing ['credits', 'tier']\"). No slicer-basic alias. Staging's has both.\n- tsdws-prod lacks JUSPRIN_OPENROUTER_API_KEY (staging has it; needed by slicer-basic).\n- Prod DB: no jusprinv2 syndicate, no jusprinv2.obico.io Site. DNS for jusprinv2.obico.io does not resolve. No prod managed cert or ingress rule. All covered by ops tsd/RUNBOOK.md \"JusPrin's host\".\n- JUSPRIN_V2_MIN_APP_VERSION blank on both. JUSPRIN_V2_CAPTURE_CONTAINER blank on both (chats are not kept).\n- Other web env names identical between stg and prod.\n\n## Proposed server fix (not applied, not tested)\nproposed-billing-fix.patch in this folder: grant a term only when the subscription has no unpaid invoices, grant it on payment_succeeded otherwise, and reopen a plan's lots on a switch back. Separately /v2/account needs an \"ends\" signal (plan.expired_at) and Preferences.tsx needs \"Ends <day>.\" when set.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7eb5c3b8-d2ba-475a-9c26-8c754b0e324b","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-dev","slug":"rosy-bubbling-whisper"}
