{"parentUuid":"426e606f-6f35-4056-ac44-349cb6af1e63","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6a301c32-76b1-44fc-b776-34066675e090","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011AcG5pbRAgv1DV133UejdX","type":"tool_result","content":"commit f6242452582e156dabeef0c30873b72173506617\nAuthor: Kenneth Jiang <kenneth.jiang@gmail.com>\nDate:   Tue Nov 10 10:12:48 2026 -0800\n\n    JusPrin 2's host: its own Google sign-in app, set up by hand once per server\n    \n    JusPrin 2's host had shared Obico's Google app, so Google's consent screen\n    named Obico and linked Obico's policies. The host now uses a Google app of its\n    own, from the JusPrin Google Cloud project, so the screen says JusPrin.\n    \n    A server's JusPrin 2 host is set up once, by hand: its site in the jusprinv2\n    syndicate from a Django shell, since the admin doesn't edit syndicates, and\n    its Google app in the admin. docs/jusprin2-host-setup.md has the steps;\n    production will need them for jusprinv2.obico.io. The management command that\n    did this was used only by the tests, so it is gone, and the tests build the\n    same rows with set_up_jusprin_host() in jusprin/v2/tests/jusprin_host.py.\n\n docs/jusprin2-host-setup.md                        | 58 ++++++++++++++++++++++\n web_ent/jusprin/ledger/billing.py                  |  2 +-\n .../commands/set_up_jusprinv2_syndicate.py         | 45 -----------------","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"b0d02a79-ea5f-4eff-b029-bc1d350491a7","timestamp":"2026-11-10T21:27:05.294Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"commit f6242452582e156dabeef0c30873b72173506617\nAuthor: Kenneth Jiang <kenneth.jiang@gmail.com>\nDate:   Tue Nov 10 10:12:48 2026 -0800\n\n    JusPrin 2's host: its own Google sign-in app, set up by hand once per server\n    \n    JusPrin 2's host had shared Obico's Google app, so Google's consent screen\n    named Obico and linked Obico's policies. The host now uses a Google app of its\n    own, from the JusPrin Google Cloud project, so the screen says JusPrin.\n    \n    A server's JusPrin 2 host is set up once, by hand: its site in the jusprinv2\n    syndicate from a Django shell, since the admin doesn't edit syndicates, and\n    its Google app in the admin. docs/jusprin2-host-setup.md has the steps;\n    production will need them for jusprinv2.obico.io. The management command that\n    did this was used only by the tests, so it is gone, and the tests build the\n    same rows with set_up_jusprin_host() in jusprin/v2/tests/jusprin_host.py.\n\n docs/jusprin2-host-setup.md                        | 58 ++++++++++++++++++++++\n web_ent/jusprin/ledger/billing.py                  |  2 +-\n .../commands/set_up_jusprinv2_syndicate.py         | 45 -----------------","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"426e606f-6f35-4056-ac44-349cb6af1e63","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/tsd-enterprise-worktrees/jusprin-v2-own-chargebee","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-dev","slug":"rosy-bubbling-whisper"}
