{"parentUuid":"262ad066-1cee-461d-b818-774ec6e5335f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CguxTvMtvn4XbTNcUkmhH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2582,"cache_read_input_tokens":263298,"output_tokens":1156,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":17},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2582,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1156,"cache_read_input_tokens":263298,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2582,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2582},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":6595,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CguxTv7mVi9ypiCNBojFe","requestRef":"7b9dbfaf-a93c-4600-b977-f6b90fd50792","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"86f485e1-7d99-41f3-ad84-22d5be46f058","timestamp":"2026-11-10T21:28:15.869Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-dev","slug":"rosy-bubbling-whisper"}
{"parentUuid":"86f485e1-7d99-41f3-ad84-22d5be46f058","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CguxTvMtvn4XbTNcUkmhH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"We're not ready for production yet. The server code is ready, but JusPrin's Chargebee account still has only its test site. The site picker shows \"jusprinv2 – TEST Site\" and no live site. Until a live site exists with its catalog, payment gateways and webhook, production has nowhere to sell. I changed nothing during this check.\n\n**What's ready**\n- **Server code:** master holds the move to JusPrin's own Chargebee site, the billing fixes, the customer-name prefix and the setup doc. Staging ran it end to end: a credit pack, a Hobby plan, the Premium discount in the cart, a cancel, and a pack with no billing form. PayPal was tested on a local server.\n- **What master adds over production:** six commits and no database migrations. Production runs image obi.4098, built from master commit 0a75568378.\n- **Production matches the ops files.** The only differences are web-socket replicas scaled down on purpose and env lines in a different order.\n- **Low risk to customers:** production has one JusPrin 2 account, yours (k@obico.io). Buying there already fails today: as of the 9 Nov check, the JusPrin 2 plans did not exist on Obico's live site. Deploying won't break anything that works now.\n- **Sentry:** no errors in the billing code. The one hit on `/ent/cb_webhook/` is the old Obico email bug from August.\n\n**What blocks the rollout**\n1. **The live site.** You have to activate it; Chargebee will ask for business details. Then it needs everything the test site has:\n   - the three prices and the Premium coupon;\n   - Stripe connected to TSD's live account, and PayPal connected to TSD's live account. On PayPal, \"Reference Transactions\" has to be on, or renewals can't be charged.\n   - the checkout settings (one-time payments on, plan quantity off, coupons on, portal by single sign-on) and the field settings;\n   - the logo and colors;\n   - the \"JUSPRIN\" statement name;\n   - a business name and address for invoices (the test site has none);\n   - the email sender.\n\n   I can do all of that once the site exists and you say yes. You create the live API key, as you did for staging, and I add the webhook pointing at production.\n2. **Deploy.** Build a release from master and add two settings to production's web pods: the live site name `jusprinv2` and its API key. The customer-name prefix stays at its default.\n3. **Ops push.** Two ops commits aren't pushed. One is mine, for staging. The other is another session's chat-keeping change, which is already running in production. Pushing waits on you.\n\n**Not blocking, but open**\n- **Google sign-in on production:** sign-in on jusprinv2.obico.io still uses Obico's Google app, so Google's consent screen names Obico. Switching to JusPrin's Google app is a manual admin step, and you'd paste in the client secret. It can happen before or after the deploy.\n- **Email sign-off:** the test site's emails are signed \"Jusprin-support\", with a lowercase p.\n- **The app's plan line:** the change that makes the app say \"Ends <day>\" for a cancelled plan is only on branch `claude/plan-ends-line`, not on `jusprin-dev`. It should land before the app release.\n- **Staging leftover:** staging test user 491 still points at a subscription I deleted from Obico's test site. It ends 10 Dec and only affects that test account.\n\nThe question below the recap asks whether you'll activate the live site."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2582,"cache_read_input_tokens":263298,"output_tokens":1156,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":17},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2582,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1156,"cache_read_input_tokens":263298,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2582,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2582},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CguxTv7mVi9ypiCNBojFe","requestRef":"7b9dbfaf-a93c-4600-b977-f6b90fd50792","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"b9dc2998-f293-4418-b458-51df1ec17acc","timestamp":"2026-11-10T21:28:20.174Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-dev","slug":"rosy-bubbling-whisper"}
