{"parentUuid":"dd063375-b09a-4561-9847-dc73fa67ca62","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CguycsrT9BhbymP9zsJ4L","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You activate it from the test site, signed in to Chargebee as the site's owner. On jusprinv2 the owner is **jusprin-support@obico.io**. The login I use, k@thespaghettidetective.com, is only an Admin there, and Chargebee doesn't show it the activation button. Activating starts a paid Chargebee subscription for this site, separate from Obico's, so it needs a card.\n\n**Steps** (from Chargebee's activation guide; I couldn't see the screens myself)\n1. Sign in to app.chargebee.com as jusprin-support@obico.io and open the jusprinv2 test site. Click **Select Plan**. Chargebee says the button is next to the test site in the site list, or at the top left above the menu, or on your profile at the bottom left.\n2. Pick a plan. The Flow plan is the self-serve one, with a choice of **Pay as you go** or **Commit monthly**. Click **Activate now**.\n3. Choose USD as the billing currency, then **Activate now**.\n4. **Contact for Technical/Billing Issues:** enter the company name, then **Save and Proceed**. TSD's Stripe account is named \"TSD Technology, LLC\".\n5. **Billing Information:** organization, phone and address. Obico's Chargebee profile uses 1790 Willow Lake Ln, San Jose CA 95131. Then **Save and Proceed**.\n6. **Payment Information:** your card, then **Save and Proceed**.\n7. **Summary:** agree to the terms and click **Pay & Get Started**. Your bank may ask for a 3-D Secure check.\n\nChargebee then opens the live site. The site switcher at the top left now offers both Test and Live.\n\n**Decision needed: which plan variant.** Chargebee's fee is paid out of what JusPrin bills, and only you can pick how much to commit. The options, using third-party trackers' numbers (I couldn't open Chargebee's own pricing page, so check it on the plan screen):\n- **Pay as you go:** 0.80% of each month's billing, with no monthly fee.\n- **Commit monthly:** $99 a month plus 0.65%.\n\nCommit only becomes cheaper once JusPrin bills more than about $66,000 a month. My pick is Pay as you go. The old free tier, which covered the first $250K, appears to be gone. Do you want Pay as you go? The question below the recap asks it too.\n\n**After it's activated, four things only you can do:**\n1. **Invite me:** on the live site, invite k@thespaghettidetective.com as Admin under Team Members. Each site keeps its own team, so the test-site invite doesn't carry over.\n2. **Create a key:** under Settings › Configure Chargebee › API Keys and Events, add a full-access key. Save it to `~/.config/jusprin/chargebee-jusprinv2-live.env`, as you did for staging.\n3. **Connect Stripe:** sign in to TSD's live Stripe account when the connect window asks.\n4. **Connect PayPal:** sign in to TSD's live PayPal business account when it asks. Make sure \"Reference Transactions\" is turned on for that PayPal account, or plan renewals can't be charged; PayPal support turns it on if it's off.\n\nEverything else I copy from the test site: the catalog, checkout and field settings, branding, statement name and emails. Then I add the production webhook, run one small real-card purchase, and deploy.\n\nSources:\n- [Chargebee: Activate your Live site](https://www.chargebee.com/docs/billing/2.0/implementing-chargebee/activate-live-site)\n- [Chargebee: Go-live checklist](https://chargebee.com/docs/billing/2.0/implementing-chargebee/checklist)\n- [Chargebee Flow plan consolidation (usagepricing.com)](https://www.usagepricing.com/blueprint/activity/chargebee-2026-08-11-flow-plan-consolidation)\n- [Chargebee pricing history (PricingSaaS)](https://pricingsaas.com/companies/chargebee)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":924,"cache_read_input_tokens":282363,"output_tokens":1354,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":924,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1354,"cache_read_input_tokens":282363,"cache_creation_input_tokens":924,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":924},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CguycsbKZuT6rUfMUQ4sX","requestRef":"3c0f07a9-58fe-4d55-80fa-8be751a0472e","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"dddfc0b8-e9bb-41b0-bb25-09976ce9ec05","timestamp":"2026-11-10T21:43:27.525Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-dev","slug":"rosy-bubbling-whisper"}
