{"parentUuid":"f9b49077-4e05-4cca-bf3b-ebbe2d82f842","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvBVerocX5Sxsg9CdVH1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"JusPrin's live Chargebee site is active, and the API key you saved works against it. It now has the same catalog as the test site, which I created through its API:\n- **Plans:** Hobby at $10 a month and Workshop at $20 a month.\n- **Credit pack:** $10 for 500 credits.\n- **Coupon:** 20% off forever for Obico Premium users, on the two plans only.\n\nThe ids, names and prices match the test site exactly, which is what the server expects.\n\nThen I tried to open the live site's checkout settings in your Chrome. The permission check stopped me, because those changes affect what real customers see. So I'm asking for an explicit yes before I touch them. Here is what I'd change, all copied from the test site:\n- **Checkout options:** one-time payments on, so the credit pack can be bought. Plan quantity editing off, coupons allowed, and the self-serve portal reached by single sign-on (Chargebee's \"Single Sign On API\" setting).\n- **Checkout fields:** billing and shipping off; the card asks only for an optional zip and country.\n- **Branding:** the JusPrin logo, icon and favicon; brand and accent color #3A2D64; page and header color #F6F2F7.\n- **Statement name:** \"JUSPRIN\", so card statements read \"OBICO* JUSPRIN\".\n- **Email sender:** \"JusPrin Support <jusprin-support@obico.io>\". I'd also fix the sign-off's spelling to \"JusPrin Support\"; the test site's reads \"Jusprin-support\".\n- **Invoice business name and address:** the test site has none. I'd use TSD Technology, LLC at 1790 Willow Lake Ln, San Jose CA 95131, the address Obico's Chargebee profile uses, unless you want a different one.\n\nThree things stay apart from this yes:\n- **Stripe and PayPal:** connecting them needs you to sign in to TSD's live accounts. I'll open those pages for you when we get there.\n- **Production webhook:** I'd add it only right before the deploy.\n- **The deploy:** that gets its own question."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":564,"cache_read_input_tokens":301543,"output_tokens":690,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":564,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":690,"cache_read_input_tokens":301543,"cache_creation_input_tokens":564,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":564},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgvBVedRCRiQBUp7YKNKw","requestRef":"97763d68-d5a9-4567-b3e7-85cbbc785275","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"7ca07d90-25b1-455c-a415-e8c1e017163b","timestamp":"2026-11-11T00:19:05.886Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79/scratchpad","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-dev","slug":"rosy-bubbling-whisper"}
