{"parentUuid":"1f200fc5-5e47-441c-93dc-ec8f99a67cbf","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"1878ed12-3b45-49de-a8a9-e4ddee9fabce","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>Bash, Edit, Read, SendMessage, Skill, ToolSearch, WebFetch, WebSearch, Write, mcp__Claude_Browser__computer, mcp__Claude_Browser__get_page_text, mcp__Claude_Browser__navigate, mcp__Claude_Browser__preview_list, mcp__Claude_Browser__preview_start, mcp__Claude_Browser__preview_stop, mcp__Claude_Browser__tabs_context, mcp__ccd_turn__update_plan, mcp__ccd_turn__wrap_up, mcp__claude-in-chrome__browser_batch, mcp__claude-in-chrome__computer, mcp__claude-in-chrome__file_upload, mcp__claude-in-chrome__find, mcp__claude-in-chrome__get_page_text, mcp__claude-in-chrome__javascript_tool, mcp__claude-in-chrome__navigate, mcp__claude-in-chrome__read_console_messages, mcp__claude-in-chrome__read_page, mcp__claude-in-chrome__tabs_close_mcp, mcp__claude-in-chrome__tabs_context_mcp, mcp__claude-in-chrome__tabs_create_mcp</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n\n   **Constraints in force (verbatim or near-verbatim):**\n   - \"Don't change anything in production, and don't change Chargebee's live site without Kenneth's explicit yes.\" Kenneth has now given an explicit yes to copy the test site's settings to JusPrin's live site, jusprinv2. Asked: \"May I change the live site's settings to match the test site?\" Answer: \"Yes, go ahead\".\n   - Ask Kenneth before any production change, including the deploy and the production webhook.\n   - Never commit submodule pointer changes.\n   - Use the service account ai-agent@tsdtechnology.iam.gserviceaccount.com for gcloud and kubectl. On this Mac: `export CLOUDSDK_PYTHON=$HOME/.local/share/uv/python/cpython-3.12.9-macos-aarch64-none/bin/python3.12`.\n   - Don't start a second docker stack.\n   - Server code goes to tsd-enterprise master.\n   - The ops repo push waits on Kenneth.\n   - I may not type passwords, government IDs or API keys; Kenneth does those himself. Never print API keys.\n   - Key files:\n     - ~/.config/jusprin/chargebee-jusprinv2-test.env (test site)\n     - ~/.config/jusprin/chargebee-jusprinv2-stg.env (staging)\n     - ~/.config/jusprin/chargebee-jusprinv2-live.env (live; variable CHARGEBEE_API_KEY, chmod 600 applied)\n   - Fix any bug without asking.\n   - Reuse existing Stripe and PayPal accounts.\n   - Read-only on Obico's live Chargebee site and on TSD's Stripe and PayPal accounts.\n\n   **Requests this stretch, in order:**\n   1. Style the jusprinv2 Chargebee site in JusPrin's branding.\n   2. Fix the blank band above \"Back to cart\", and question whether the billing address is needed. Kenneth then said \"Yes, turn it off\".\n   3. Clean up the old plans etc. from the tsd/obico Chargebee test site.\n   4. Check readiness for production.\n   5. Explain how to activate the live site. Kenneth chose \"Pay as you go\".\n   6. Open the page in Kenneth's own Chrome.\n   7. Kenneth said \"done\" (activated, invited, key saved).\n   8. Kenneth said \"Yes, go ahead\": copy the test site's settings to the live site.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n\n   **Chargebee sites:**\n   - jusprinv2-test (test) and jusprinv2 (live, newly activated on the Flow plan, Pay as you go). Both are on Product Catalog 2.0.\n   - Live site owner: jusprin-support@obico.io. k@thespaghettidetective.com is an Admin on the test site.\n   - Chrome is now signed in to Chargebee as JusPrin Support.\n   - Obico's sites, thespaghettidetective-test and thespaghettidetective live, are on Product Catalog 1.0 (plans and addons).\n\n   **Production:**\n   - All five deployments (web, ws, tasks, rttasks, beat) run kennethjiang/web_ent:obi.4098, built from master 0a75568378.\n   - Staging runs obi.4104.\n   - Master adds six commits over production, none with migrations: f624245258, d984c46317, 77fd19cadb, 2d97f4b1c7, a72b271f7e, 52d1bd7974.\n   - Production has no JUSPRIN_V2_CHARGEBEE_* env vars.\n   - Production JusPrin host jusprinv2.obico.io (Site 5, syndicate jusprinv2) still uses Obico's Google SocialApp 1 \"Obico Google+\". It has one jusprinv2 user, k@obico.io.\n\n   **Ops repo (~/Projects/ops):** two unpushed commits, both waiting on Kenneth.\n   - 1e6caf7: mine, for staging.\n   - 3f5e1b7: another session's chat-capture change, already applied to production.\n   - `kubectl diff` shows production matches the ops files, apart from tsdws replicas scaled down to 10 on purpose.\n\n   **Brand tokens:** action-primary #3A2D64, surface-subtle #F6F2F7.\n\n   **Chargebee checkout customizer:** native `type=color` inputs with ids COLOR_ACCENT, COLOR_HEADER, COLOR_HIGHLIGHT_PANEL, COLOR_CHECKOUT_PAGE, COLOR_ORDER_CARDS, COLOR_INPUT_COMPONENTS.\n   - The advanced inputs only exist in the page once \"Advanced colors\" is expanded.\n   - Set them with the HTMLInputElement value setter plus input and change events.\n   - The brand color field drops uppercase letters when typed; type lowercase \"3a2d64\".\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   **tsd-enterprise worktree** /Users/kenneth/Projects/tsd-enterprise-worktrees/jusprin-v2-own-chargebee (branch jusprin-v2-own-chargebee-on-master):\n   - docs/jusprin2-host-setup.md, section 3. Committed as 52d1bd7974 \"JusPrin 2 host setup: checkout asks no billing address and wears JusPrin's brand\" and pushed to origin master. Added text:\n     ```\n     Under Fields on the same page, disable the Billing and Shipping sections, and\n     under Payments turn on the card's Address Fields with only Zip and Country.\n     No tax is set up, so nothing needs a billing address; Obico's site asks the\n     same. Turn billing back on, with at least the country, if the site ever\n     collects tax.\n\n     Under Settings › Configure Chargebee › Brand Styles, upload JusPrin's logo\n     (the app's `resources/jusprin/overlay/images/OrcaSlicer_horizontal_light.svg`\n     as a PNG), the mark as the icon, and `jusprin/static/jusprinv2/img/favicon.png`\n     as the favicon, and set the brand color to `#3A2D64`. Under Checkout\n     (Customize Checkout), set the accent color to `#3A2D64` and the header and\n     page colors to `#F6F2F7`, JusPrin's page background. Without a logo the\n     checkout shows an empty band above \"Back to cart\".\n     ```\n   - web_ent/app_ent/cb_views.py: read only. Obico's cb_webhook ignores deletion events; it handles only SUBSCRIPTION_EVENTS and invoice_generated.\n\n   **Scratchpad** /private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79/scratchpad/:\n   - jusprin-logo-light.png: 720×256, rendered from the JusPrin lockup with `rsvg-convert -h 256`.\n   - jusprin-mark.png and jusprin-icon.png: 512×512, from resources/jusprin/branding/jusprin-mark.svg.\n   - Favicon source: …/web_ent/jusprin/static/jusprinv2/img/favicon.png (192×192).\n   - obico-test.env: Obico's test-site key as OBT. Never print it.\n   - cbl.sh: live-site API helper.\n     ```\n     #!/bin/zsh\n     source ~/.config/jusprin/chargebee-jusprinv2-live.env\n     M=$1; P=$2; shift 2\n     if [ \"$M\" = GET ]; then curl -s -G -u REDACTED \"https://jusprinv2.chargebee.com/api/v2/$P\" \"$@\"; else curl -s -u REDACTED -X $M \"https://jusprinv2.chargebee.com/api/v2/$P\" \"$@\"; fi\n     ```\n   - cbj.sh: test-site API helper.\n   - checkout.sh `<user> <what>`: starts a staging checkout and prints the hosted page URL; `what` is pack, etc.\n   - web.sh\n   - stg_users.json: users 497 pack, 498 plan, 499 prem, 500 fail, 501.\n   - stg_lots.py: run as `kubectl --context=tsd exec -i <pod> -c tsdweb-stg -- env UIDS=500 python - < stg_lots.py`.\n   - prod_read.py: read-only query of production SocialApps and Sites.\n\n   **Shared notes** /Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_3e38de32-e8df-4f8c-b26d-1a20db4c0aca/chargebee-jusprin-emails-draft.md:\n   - Appended \"Production readiness check (2026-11-10, late)\".\n   - Appended a line recording the Pay as you go choice and the activation steps.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - Chargebee color fields didn't take typed values. Fixed by setting the value through the JS value setter and dispatching input and change events.\n   - The brand color field dropped \"A\" and \"D\" when typed. Fixed by typing lowercase.\n   - On the live site, a VWO script threw \"Illegal invocation\" during the JS set. The accent and header colors had taken; the page color input wasn't in the page yet. Expanded \"Advanced colors\", then set COLOR_CHECKOUT_PAGE.\n   - Disabling the test billing address was first refused by the permission check as an account-settings change. I asked Kenneth; he said \"Yes, turn it off\".\n   - The permission check refused navigating to the live site's settings (\"Modify Shared Resources\"). I asked Kenneth; he said \"Yes, go ahead\".\n   - The coupon create failed with \"name : cannot be blank\" because of the \"%\" in the name. Fixed with `--data-urlencode`.\n   - preview_stop needed the process serverId from preview_list (browser-preview-1794347333914-66), not the previewId.\n   - Live /r/payment_preferences loads blank; /email_notifications is a 404; the test site's /notifications gives no page text.\n   - zsh glob errors with unquoted `?` and `[]` in URLs and kubectl custom-columns. Fixed by quoting.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n\n   **Test site jusprinv2-test:**\n   - Checkout colors: accent #3a2d64, header and page #f6f2f7, cards, highlight panel and inputs white.\n   - Logo, icon, favicon uploaded; brand color #3A2D64.\n   - Billing and shipping off; card asks Zip and Country, both optional.\n   - Staging purchase without billing fields: user 500 got 500 + 500 credits from invoice 16.\n\n   **Obico test site cleanup:**\n   - Deleted plans jusprin-hobby-monthly and jusprin-workshop-monthly, addon jusprin-credit-pack, coupon jusprin2-obico-premium-20.\n   - Deleted customers jusprinv2-57, jusprinv2-59, jusprinv2-490, jusprinv2-491, jusprinv2-492; subscription AzZd1kVaXEUIX4Ti3 went with them.\n   - Kept: JusPrin 1's jusprin-unlimited-* plans and all of Obico's own plans and addons.\n   - Leftover: staging user 491 has a JusPrinPlan row pointing at the deleted subscription; it expires 10 Dec.\n\n   **Live site jusprinv2 (business profile \"TSD Technology, LLC\", San Jose CA 95131, phone +14045654264, as set by Kenneth):**\n   - Catalog created via API, matching the test site:\n     - Family jusprin.\n     - Items jusprin-hobby and jusprin-workshop (plans), jusprin-credit-pack (charge).\n     - Prices jusprin-hobby-monthly $10/month, jusprin-workshop-monthly $20/month, jusprin-credit-pack-USD $10.\n     - Coupon jusprin2-obico-premium-20: 20%, forever, limited to the two plan prices.\n   - Checkout configuration, published:\n     - Plan quantity editing off; coupons on (multiple coupons off).\n     - One-time payments enabled: API only on, coupons off, edit quantity on, remove products on.\n     - Portal access \"Via Single Sign On API\".\n   - Fields, published: billing and shipping disabled; card address fields Zip and Country only.\n   - Branding applied: logo, icon, favicon, brand color #3A2D64.\n   - Customize Checkout colors saved: accent #3a2d64, header and page #f6f2f7, others white.\n   - Payment gateways: none yet.\n\n   **Activation info:** Chargebee's activation is done by the owner via \"Select Plan\". Pricing came from third-party trackers: Pay as you go 0.80%; Commit $99/month plus 0.65%.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"can we style chargebee jusprinv2 site to be consistent with the branding?\" (with a screenshot)\n   - \"also there is a big blank space above \"back to cart\". I'm not sure billing address is necessary. any point of requiring the user to enter billing address?\" (with a screenshot)\n   - \"Yes, turn it off\"\n   - \"clean up the old plans etc from the tsd/obico chargebee test site first\"\n   - \"Check to see if we're ready to roll out to production.\"\n   - \"Tell me how to activate it.\"\n   - \"Pay as you go\"\n   - \"Open the page for me so that I can do these\"\n   - \"in my own chrome\" / \"Try again\"\n   - \"done\"\n   - \"Yes, go ahead\" (answer to: \"May I change the live site's settings to match the test site?\")\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - **Live site emails:** set the sender to \"JusPrin Support <jusprin-support@obico.io>\" and copy the test site's master template (JusPrin logo). Fix the sign-off \"Jusprin-support\" to \"JusPrin Support\". The sender may need verification on the live site.\n   - **Gateways:** connect Stripe (TSD's live account) and PayPal (TSD's live business account, with Reference Transactions on) to the live site. Kenneth must sign in; open the pages for him in his Chrome. Set up Smart Routing like the test site: PayPal to PayPal, cards to Stripe.\n   - **Statement name:** set the Transaction Descriptor \"JUSPRIN\" under Payment Preferences once a gateway exists. The page loads blank by direct URL; try from the payment gateways page.\n   - **Before the deploy:** add the live webhook to https://<production host>/ent/jusprin/v2/cb_webhook. The production web host is likely app.obico.io or app.thespaghettidetective.com; check which. Then ask Kenneth before deploying.\n   - **Deploy (needs Kenneth's yes):**\n     - Build a release from master (release branch = master plus built bundles, force-pushed; CircleCI builds obi.<n>).\n     - Add REDACTED and JUSPRIN_V2_CHARGEBEE_API_KEY (live key) to tsd/prod/tsdweb-prod.yaml; the prefix stays at its default.\n     - Run one small real-card purchase.\n     - Ops push waits on Kenneth.\n   - **Open items to report:**\n     - Production Google sign-in still uses Obico's Google app: a manual SocialApp switch, with Kenneth pasting the client secret.\n     - The app's \"Ends <day>\" change 6f1f03867d is only on claude/plan-ends-line, not on jusprin-dev.\n     - Staging user 491 leftover.\n   - **Task list on screen:**\n     1. Check live site access and API key: completed.\n     2. Copy catalog and coupon to live site: completed.\n     3. Copy checkout, fields, branding, descriptor: completed, except the descriptor.\n     4. Copy email sender and templates: in progress.\n     5. Connect Stripe and PayPal with Kenneth: pending.\n     6. Report and ask to deploy: pending.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I was copying the email settings from the test site to the live site. I tried to read the test site's email notification list: https://jusprinv2-test.chargebee.com/email_notifications was a 404, and https://jusprinv2-test.chargebee.com/notifications returned no page text. A screenshot or wait was needed.\n\n   Known from earlier: the test site's /notifications/settings opens \"Customize Master Template\" with From \"JusPrin Support jusprin-support@obico.io\", the JusPrin logo, and the signature \"Regards, Jusprin-support\".\n\n   Chrome tabs:\n   - 268836873: live site, signed in as JusPrin Support.\n   - 268836818: test site.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Continue Kenneth's \"Yes, go ahead\" (copy the test site's settings to the live site), starting with emails:\n   1. Screenshot https://jusprinv2-test.chargebee.com/notifications/settings and the notifications list to read the sender profile and template.\n   2. Open https://jusprinv2.chargebee.com/notifications/settings and set the same sender (\"JusPrin Support\", jusprin-support@obico.io), the logo, and the corrected sign-off \"JusPrin Support\".\n   3. Open the live payment gateways page (https://jusprinv2.chargebee.com/payment_gateways) for Stripe and PayPal. Ask Kenneth to sign in for each connection.\n   4. Set the Transaction Descriptor \"JUSPRIN\".\n   5. Report and ask before adding the production webhook and deploying.\n\n   Earlier promise, verbatim: \"Stripe and PayPal: connecting them needs you to sign in to TSD's live accounts. I'll open those pages for you when we get there.\" and \"Production webhook: I'd add it only right before the deploy.\" and \"The deploy: that gets its own question.\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"8502fb8e-9a41-4794-9a5a-2a959d5e243e","timestamp":"2026-11-11T00:31:08.118Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":34,"turnIndex":39},"turnOrigin":"human","summarizedTurnPromptUuids":["14c1c0f3-a73a-48d8-b40a-c7fb27b518f5"],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79/scratchpad","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-dev","slug":"rosy-bubbling-whisper"}
{"parentUuid":"8502fb8e-9a41-4794-9a5a-2a959d5e243e","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/tsd-enterprise-worktrees/jusprin-v2-own-chargebee/docs/jusprin2-host-setup.md","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/tsd-enterprise-worktrees/jusprin-v2-own-chargebee/docs/jusprin2-host-setup.md","content":"# Setting up JusPrin 2's host on a server\n\nJusPrin 2 signs in on a host of its own, such as `jusprinv2-stg.obico.io` on\nstaging. Accounts made through that host belong to the `jusprinv2` syndicate,\napart from any Obico account with the same email: the request's host picks the\nsyndicate (`obico-server/backend/lib/syndicate.py`). Google sign-in on that host\nuses JusPrin's own Google client, so Google's sign-in screens are JusPrin's,\nnot Obico's. Each server needs this set up once, by hand.\n`web_ent/jusprin/v2/tests/jusprin_host.py` builds the same rows for the tests.\n\nStaging was set up on 2026-11-10. Production has no JusPrin 2 host yet; its\nhost will be `jusprinv2.obico.io`, which the Google client already accepts as\na redirect address. Neither server has JusPrin 2's own Chargebee site\n(section 3) yet.\n\n## 1. The syndicate and the site\n\nThe Django admin doesn't edit syndicates, so run this in a Django shell on the\nweb pod (`python manage.py shell`), with the host's name:\n\n```python\nfrom django.contrib.sites.models import Site\nfrom app.models import SiteSyndicate, Syndicate\n\ndomain = 'jusprinv2.obico.io'\nsyndicate, _ = Syndicate.objects.get_or_create(name='jusprinv2')\nsite, _ = Site.objects.get_or_create(domain=domain, defaults={'name': 'JusPrin'})\nSiteSyndicate.objects.update_or_create(site=site, defaults={'syndicate': syndicate})\n```\n\nIt changes nothing when run again.\n\n## 2. Google sign-in\n\nThe Google client is \"JusPrin 2 server\", a Web application client in the\nGoogle Cloud project `jusprin`:\n\n- Client ID: `477983024689-h769gibj38tbs3smov9mci575t0khkbf.apps.googleusercontent.com`\n- Redirect addresses: `https://jusprinv2-stg.obico.io/accounts/google/login/callback/`\n  and `https://jusprinv2.obico.io/accounts/google/login/callback/`\n\nIn the admin, under Social applications, add one:\n\n- Provider: Google\n- Name: `JusPrin Google`\n- Client id: the client ID above\n- Secret key: the client's secret. Google shows a secret only when it is made,\n  so take it from wherever it was stored then, or add a new secret on the\n  client's page in the Google Cloud console.\n- Sites: only JusPrin 2's host.\n\nallauth refuses a site that two Google apps serve, so if another Google app\n(Obico's) has JusPrin 2's host ticked, untick it there.\n\n## 3. Chargebee\n\nJusPrin 2 sells credit packs and plans on a Chargebee site of its own,\n`jusprinv2`, not on Obico's. Its test site is `jusprinv2-test`, which local\nservers and staging use. Both sites use Chargebee's Product Catalog 2.0\n(`web_ent/jusprin/ledger/billing.py` says what that changes).\n\nSet these on the web pods:\n\n- `JUSPRIN_V2_CHARGEBEE_SITE`: `jusprinv2-test` on staging, `jusprinv2` on\n  production.\n- `JUSPRIN_V2_CHARGEBEE_API_KEY`: a full-access API key of that site.\n- `JUSPRIN_V2_CHARGEBEE_CUSTOMER_PREFIX`: `jusprinv2-stg-` on staging; leave\n  it unset elsewhere (`jusprinv2-`). An account's Chargebee customer is this\n  prefix and its user id. Staging and local servers share the test site, and\n  user ids repeat across servers, so without its own prefix staging would take\n  a local server's customers and events as its own.\n\nThe site's product catalog needs these ids, which the server names in\n`settings_ent.py`:\n\n- Plan item prices `jusprin-hobby-monthly` ($10 a month) and\n  `jusprin-workshop-monthly` ($20 a month).\n- Charge item price `jusprin-credit-pack-USD` ($10), the credit pack.\n- Coupon `jusprin2-obico-premium-20`, 20% off forever, for the two plans only.\n\nUnder Settings › Configure Chargebee › Checkout & Self-Serve Portal ›\nConfiguration:\n\n- Checkout: turn off \"Allow customers to edit quantity for plans\", and turn on\n  \"Allow customers to add/remove coupons\".\n- Checkout: One time payments: leave it enabled; the credit pack is bought\n  through it.\n- Self-Serve Portal: set \"Customers can access the self-serve portal\" to\n  \"Via Single Sign On API\". Otherwise Chargebee refuses the server's portal\n  link with \"Customer portal access via API is disabled\".\n\nUnder Fields on the same page, disable the Billing and Shipping sections, and\nunder Payments turn on the card's Address Fields with only Zip and Country.\nNo tax is set up, so nothing needs a billing address; Obico's site asks the\nsame. Turn billing back on, with at least the country, if the site ever\ncollects tax.\n\nUnder Settings › Configure Chargebee › Brand Styles, upload JusPrin's logo\n(the app's `resources/jusprin/overlay/images/OrcaSlicer_horizontal_light.svg`\nas a PNG), the mark as the icon, and `jusprin/static/jusprinv2/img/favicon.png`\nas the favicon, and set the brand color to `#3A2D64`. Under Checkout\n(Customize Checkout), set the accent color to `#3A2D64` and the header and\npage colors to `#F6F2F7`, JusPrin's page background. Without a logo the\ncheckout shows an empty band above \"Back to cart\".\n\nUnder Settings › Configure Chargebee › Webhooks, add\n`https://<server>/ent/jusprin/v2/cb_webhook`, where `<server>` is the server's\nown host (`app-stg.obico.io` on staging). The server trusts a post only for\nthe event's id and reads the event back from the site with its key, so the\nwebhook needs no password.\n\n## 4. Check it\n\nOpen `https://<host>/accounts/google/login/?process=login`. It should redirect\nto `accounts.google.com` with the client ID above and\n`redirect_uri=https://<host>/accounts/google/login/callback/`.\n\nSigned in on the host, open `https://<host>/ent/jusprin/v2/web/prices` and\nstart a credit-pack checkout. It should open a `jusprinv2` (or\n`jusprinv2-test`) checkout page for $10. On the test site, pay with\nChargebee's test card 4111 1111 1111 1111; the account should gain 500\ncredits, plus the launch bonus while that offer runs.\n","numLines":123,"startLine":1,"totalLines":123}},"displayPath":"../../../../../../../Users/kenneth/Projects/tsd-enterprise-worktrees/jusprin-v2-own-chargebee/docs/jusprin2-host-setup.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"f4f31cbd-5dc6-469b-bc13-56589aae4075","timestamp":"2026-11-11T00:31:08.334Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Users/kenneth/Projects/tsd-enterprise-worktrees/jusprin-v2-own-chargebee/docs/jusprin2-host-setup.md\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t# Setting up JusPrin 2's host on a server\n2\t\n3\tJusPrin 2 signs in on a host of its own, such as `jusprinv2-stg.obico.io` on\n4\tstaging. Accounts made through that host belong to the `jusprinv2` syndicate,\n5\tapart from any Obico account with the same email: the request's host picks the\n6\tsyndicate (`obico-server/backend/lib/syndicate.py`). Google sign-in on that host\n7\tuses JusPrin's own Google client, so Google's sign-in screens are JusPrin's,\n8\tnot Obico's. Each server needs this set up once, by hand.\n9\t`web_ent/jusprin/v2/tests/jusprin_host.py` builds the same rows for the tests.\n10\t\n11\tStaging was set up on 2026-11-10. Production has no JusPrin 2 host yet; its\n12\thost will be `jusprinv2.obico.io`, which the Google client already accepts as\n13\ta redirect address. Neither server has JusPrin 2's own Chargebee site\n14\t(section 3) yet.\n15\t\n16\t## 1. The syndicate and the site\n17\t\n18\tThe Django admin doesn't edit syndicates, so run this in a Django shell on the\n19\tweb pod (`python manage.py shell`), with the host's name:\n20\t\n21\t```python\n22\tfrom django.contrib.sites.models import Site\n23\tfrom app.models import SiteSyndicate, Syndicate\n24\t\n25\tdomain = 'jusprinv2.obico.io'\n26\tsyndicate, _ = Syndicate.objects.get_or_create(name='jusprinv2')\n27\tsite, _ = Site.objects.get_or_create(domain=domain, defaults={'name': 'JusPrin'})\n28\tSiteSyndicate.objects.update_or_create(site=site, defaults={'syndicate': syndicate})\n29\t```\n30\t\n31\tIt changes nothing when run again.\n32\t\n33\t## 2. Google sign-in\n34\t\n35\tThe Google client is \"JusPrin 2 server\", a Web application client in the\n36\tGoogle Cloud project `jusprin`:\n37\t\n38\t- Client ID: `477983024689-h769gibj38tbs3smov9mci575t0khkbf.apps.googleusercontent.com`\n39\t- Redirect addresses: `https://jusprinv2-stg.obico.io/accounts/google/login/callback/`\n40\t  and `https://jusprinv2.obico.io/accounts/google/login/callback/`\n41\t\n42\tIn the admin, under Social applications, add one:\n43\t\n44\t- Provider: Google\n45\t- Name: `JusPrin Google`\n46\t- Client id: the client ID above\n47\t- Secret key: the client's secret. Google shows a secret only when it is made,\n48\t  so take it from wherever it was stored then, or add a new secret on the\n49\t  client's page in the Google Cloud console.\n50\t- Sites: only JusPrin 2's host.\n51\t\n52\tallauth refuses a site that two Google apps serve, so if another Google app\n53\t(Obico's) has JusPrin 2's host ticked, untick it there.\n54\t\n55\t## 3. Chargebee\n56\t\n57\tJusPrin 2 sells credit packs and plans on a Chargebee site of its own,\n58\t`jusprinv2`, not on Obico's. Its test site is `jusprinv2-test`, which local\n59\tservers and staging use. Both sites use Chargebee's Product Catalog 2.0\n60\t(`web_ent/jusprin/ledger/billing.py` says what that changes).\n61\t\n62\tSet these on the web pods:\n63\t\n64\t- `JUSPRIN_V2_CHARGEBEE_SITE`: `jusprinv2-test` on staging, `jusprinv2` on\n65\t  production.\n66\t- `JUSPRIN_V2_CHARGEBEE_API_KEY`: a full-access API key of that site.\n67\t- `JUSPRIN_V2_CHARGEBEE_CUSTOMER_PREFIX`: `jusprinv2-stg-` on staging; leave\n68\t  it unset elsewhere (`jusprinv2-`). An account's Chargebee customer is this\n69\t  prefix and its user id. Staging and local servers share the test site, and\n70\t  user ids repeat across servers, so without its own prefix staging would take\n71\t  a local server's customers and events as its own.\n72\t\n73\tThe site's product catalog needs these ids, which the server names in\n74\t`settings_ent.py`:\n75\t\n76\t- Plan item prices `jusprin-hobby-monthly` ($10 a month) and\n77\t  `jusprin-workshop-monthly` ($20 a month).\n78\t- Charge item price `jusprin-credit-pack-USD` ($10), the credit pack.\n79\t- Coupon `jusprin2-obico-premium-20`, 20% off forever, for the two plans only.\n80\t\n81\tUnder Settings › Configure Chargebee › Checkout & Self-Serve Portal ›\n82\tConfiguration:\n83\t\n84\t- Checkout: turn off \"Allow customers to edit quantity for plans\", and turn on\n85\t  \"Allow customers to add/remove coupons\".\n86\t- Checkout: One time payments: leave it enabled; the credit pack is bought\n87\t  through it.\n88\t- Self-Serve Portal: set \"Customers can access the self-serve portal\" to\n89\t  \"Via Single Sign On API\". Otherwise Chargebee refuses the server's portal\n90\t  link with \"Customer portal access via API is disabled\".\n91\t\n92\tUnder Fields on the same page, disable the Billing and Shipping sections, and\n93\tunder Payments turn on the card's Address Fields with only Zip and Country.\n94\tNo tax is set up, so nothing needs a billing address; Obico's site asks the\n95\tsame. Turn billing back on, with at least the country, if the site ever\n96\tcollects tax.\n97\t\n98\tUnder Settings › Configure Chargebee › Brand Styles, upload JusPrin's logo\n99\t(the app's `resources/jusprin/overlay/images/OrcaSlicer_horizontal_light.svg`\n100\tas a PNG), the mark as the icon, and `jusprin/static/jusprinv2/img/favicon.png`\n101\tas the favicon, and set the brand color to `#3A2D64`. Under Checkout\n102\t(Customize Checkout), set the accent color to `#3A2D64` and the header and\n103\tpage colors to `#F6F2F7`, JusPrin's page background. Without a logo the\n104\tcheckout shows an empty band above \"Back to cart\".\n105\t\n106\tUnder Settings › Configure Chargebee › Webhooks, add\n107\t`https://<server>/ent/jusprin/v2/cb_webhook`, where `<server>` is the server's\n108\town host (`app-stg.obico.io` on staging). The server trusts a post only for\n109\tthe event's id and reads the event back from the site with its key, so the\n110\twebhook needs no password.\n111\t\n112\t## 4. Check it\n113\t\n114\tOpen `https://<host>/accounts/google/login/?process=login`. It should redirect\n115\tto `accounts.google.com` with the client ID above and\n116\t`redirect_uri=https://<host>/accounts/google/login/callback/`.\n117\t\n118\tSigned in on the host, open `https://<host>/ent/jusprin/v2/web/prices` and\n119\tstart a credit-pack checkout. It should open a `jusprinv2` (or\n120\t`jusprinv2-test`) checkout page for $10. On the test site, pay with\n121\tChargebee's test card 4111 1111 1111 1111; the account should gain 500\n122\tcredits, plus the launch bonus while that offer runs.\n123\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79/scratchpad","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-dev","slug":"rosy-bubbling-whisper"}
{"parentUuid":"f4f31cbd-5dc6-469b-bc13-56589aae4075","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"invoked_skills","skills":[{"name":"anthropic-skills:chrome-browser","path":"plugin:anthropic-skills:chrome-browser","content":"Base directory for this skill: /Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/local-agent-mode-sessions/skills-plugin/68a648b0-98a4-49c7-902b-ff471f8d1d46/7911d73c-5552-4877-a943-6a0eba3d7c4d/skills/chrome-browser\n\n# Claude in Chrome\n\nClaude in Chrome is a browser extension. Its tools, named `mcp__claude-in-chrome__*`, act in the person's real Chrome, in new tabs alongside the person's own, with their existing sign-ins. Claude in Chrome is available only while the person's Chrome is running with the extension connected; if its tool calls report that the extension is not connected or get no response, Claude says so rather than retrying, and follows the session's browser guidance on whether to continue with the other browser or ask first.\n\nIf the only Claude in Chrome tool present is `enable__mcp__claude-in-chrome`, Claude calls it first: it turns Claude in Chrome on for this conversation, and the `mcp__claude-in-chrome__*` tools appear once it has run.\n\n## Loading the tools\n\nIf the `mcp__claude-in-chrome__*` tools are deferred (meaning they have to be loaded through ToolSearch before use), Claude loads every tool it expects to need in ONE ToolSearch call, because the select query accepts a comma-separated list and each extra ToolSearch call costs a full round trip. The core set to start with:\n\n```\nToolSearch with query \"select:mcp__claude-in-chrome__tabs_context_mcp,mcp__claude-in-chrome__navigate,mcp__claude-in-chrome__computer,mcp__claude-in-chrome__read_page,mcp__claude-in-chrome__tabs_create_mcp,mcp__claude-in-chrome__tabs_close_mcp\"\n```\n\nClaude adds task-specific tools to that same call when the task obviously needs them: `read_console_messages` and `read_network_requests` for debugging, `form_input` for forms, `gif_creator` for recordings, `javascript_tool` for page scripting. A second ToolSearch is only for a tool the task turned out to need later.\n\n## Starting a session: tab context first, then a new tab\n\nAt the start of each browser session Claude calls `mcp__claude-in-chrome__tabs_context_mcp` first, to see the person's current tabs and understand what they may want to work with. Then:\n\n1. Claude reuses an existing tab only when the person explicitly asks to work with it.\n2. Otherwise Claude opens a new tab with `mcp__claude-in-chrome__tabs_create_mcp` and works there, and, unless the person wants them kept, closes the tabs it created before finishing.\n3. Claude never reuses tab IDs remembered from an earlier or different session. If a tool reports that a tab does not exist or is invalid, or the person closes a tab, or a navigation error occurs, Claude calls `tabs_context_mcp` again for fresh tab IDs.\n\n## Site permissions\n\nClaude in Chrome acts on a site only once the person has allowed it; depending on their settings the person may be prompted per site, in the extension or in the app. When a tool call is waiting on or refused that permission, Claude tells the person and waits for them to allow it rather than working around it. A site the person declines is their decision; Claude moves on.\n\n## Recording a GIF\n\nFor multi-step interactions the person may want to review or share, Claude can record them with `mcp__claude-in-chrome__gif_creator`. Claude captures a few extra frames before and after each action so playback is smooth, and gives the file a meaningful name (for example \"login_process.gif\").\n\n## Reading console output\n\n`mcp__claude-in-chrome__read_console_messages` reads the page's console. Console output can be verbose, so when Claude is looking for specific entries it passes the `pattern` parameter (a regular expression), for example pattern \"[MyApp]\" to keep only the application's own logs.\n\n## Alerts and dialogs\n\nClaude does not trigger JavaScript alerts, confirms, prompts, or other browser modal dialogs through its actions. Those dialogs block all further browser events, so the extension stops receiving commands. Instead:\n\n1. Claude avoids clicking elements likely to raise a confirmation dialog (for example a \"Delete\" button) unless necessary.\n2. If it must interact with such an element, Claude warns the person first that this may interrupt the session.\n3. Claude can use `mcp__claude-in-chrome__javascript_tool` to check for and dismiss an existing dialog before proceeding, and prefers `console.log` plus `read_console_messages` over `alert` for debugging.\n\nIf a dialog does get triggered and the browser stops responding, Claude tells the person they need to dismiss it manually in Chrome.\n\n## Staying on task, and when to stop\n\nClaude stays focused on the specific task and does not wander into unrelated pages. Claude stops and asks the person how to proceed, explaining what it tried and what went wrong, when any of these happen:\n\n- browser tool calls fail or return errors after 2 or 3 attempts\n- the extension gives no response\n- page elements do not respond to clicks or input, or pages do not load or time out\n- the task turns out to involve unexpected complexity or tangents\n- several approaches have not completed the task\n\nClaude does not keep retrying the same failing action.\n"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"dcbec4c2-4c45-4bc2-a206-d982ac6a9345","timestamp":"2026-11-11T00:31:08.335Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nThe following skills were invoked EARLIER in this session (before the conversation was compacted), not on the current turn. They are shown here for context only so you remain aware of their guidelines.\n\nIMPORTANT: Do NOT re-execute these skills or perform their one-time setup actions (e.g., scheduling, creating files) again. Any request or argument text embedded in the skill bodies below — for example under a \"## User Request\" or \"## Input\" heading — was captured when that skill was first invoked. It is NOT the user's current message and NOT a new request: do not act on it as if it were live. Only continue to apply ongoing behavioral guidelines from these skills where still relevant.\n\n### Skill: anthropic-skills:chrome-browser\nPath: plugin:anthropic-skills:chrome-browser\n\nBase directory for this skill: /Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/local-agent-mode-sessions/skills-plugin/68a648b0-98a4-49c7-902b-ff471f8d1d46/7911d73c-5552-4877-a943-6a0eba3d7c4d/skills/chrome-browser\n\n# Claude in Chrome\n\nClaude in Chrome is a browser extension. Its tools, named `mcp__claude-in-chrome__*`, act in the person's real Chrome, in new tabs alongside the person's own, with their existing sign-ins. Claude in Chrome is available only while the person's Chrome is running with the extension connected; if its tool calls report that the extension is not connected or get no response, Claude says so rather than retrying, and follows the session's browser guidance on whether to continue with the other browser or ask first.\n\nIf the only Claude in Chrome tool present is `enable__mcp__claude-in-chrome`, Claude calls it first: it turns Claude in Chrome on for this conversation, and the `mcp__claude-in-chrome__*` tools appear once it has run.\n\n## Loading the tools\n\nIf the `mcp__claude-in-chrome__*` tools are deferred (meaning they have to be loaded through ToolSearch before use), Claude loads every tool it expects to need in ONE ToolSearch call, because the select query accepts a comma-separated list and each extra ToolSearch call costs a full round trip. The core set to start with:\n\n```\nToolSearch with query \"select:mcp__claude-in-chrome__tabs_context_mcp,mcp__claude-in-chrome__navigate,mcp__claude-in-chrome__computer,mcp__claude-in-chrome__read_page,mcp__claude-in-chrome__tabs_create_mcp,mcp__claude-in-chrome__tabs_close_mcp\"\n```\n\nClaude adds task-specific tools to that same call when the task obviously needs them: `read_console_messages` and `read_network_requests` for debugging, `form_input` for forms, `gif_creator` for recordings, `javascript_tool` for page scripting. A second ToolSearch is only for a tool the task turned out to need later.\n\n## Starting a session: tab context first, then a new tab\n\nAt the start of each browser session Claude calls `mcp__claude-in-chrome__tabs_context_mcp` first, to see the person's current tabs and understand what they may want to work with. Then:\n\n1. Claude reuses an existing tab only when the person explicitly asks to work with it.\n2. Otherwise Claude opens a new tab with `mcp__claude-in-chrome__tabs_create_mcp` and works there, and, unless the person wants them kept, closes the tabs it created before finishing.\n3. Claude never reuses tab IDs remembered from an earlier or different session. If a tool reports that a tab does not exist or is invalid, or the person closes a tab, or a navigation error occurs, Claude calls `tabs_context_mcp` again for fresh tab IDs.\n\n## Site permissions\n\nClaude in Chrome acts on a site only once the person has allowed it; depending on their settings the person may be prompted per site, in the extension or in the app. When a tool call is waiting on or refused that permission, Claude tells the person and waits for them to allow it rather than working around it. A site the person declines is their decision; Claude moves on.\n\n## Recording a GIF\n\nFor multi-step interactions the person may want to review or share, Claude can record them with `mcp__claude-in-chrome__gif_creator`. Claude captures a few extra frames before and after each action so playback is smooth, and gives the file a meaningful name (for example \"login_process.gif\").\n\n## Reading console output\n\n`mcp__claude-in-chrome__read_console_messages` reads the page's console. Console output can be verbose, so when Claude is looking for specific entries it passes the `pattern` parameter (a regular expression), for example pattern \"[MyApp]\" to keep only the application's own logs.\n\n## Alerts and dialogs\n\nClaude does not trigger JavaScript alerts, confirms, prompts, or other browser modal dialogs through its actions. Those dialogs block all further browser events, so the extension stops receiving commands. Instead:\n\n1. Claude avoids clicking elements likely to raise a confirmation dialog (for example a \"Delete\" button) unless necessary.\n2. If it must interact with such an element, Claude warns the person first that this may interrupt the session.\n3. Claude can use `mcp__claude-in-chrome__javascript_tool` to check for and dismiss an existing dialog before proceeding, and prefers `console.log` plus `read_console_messages` over `alert` for debugging.\n\nIf a dialog does get triggered and the browser stops responding, Claude tells the person they need to dismiss it manually in Chrome.\n\n## Staying on task, and when to stop\n\nClaude stays focused on the specific task and does not wander into unrelated pages. Claude stops and asks the person how to proceed, explaining what it tried and what went wrong, when any of these happen:\n\n- browser tool calls fail or return errors after 2 or 3 attempts\n- the extension gives no response\n- page elements do not respond to clicks or input, or pages do not load or time out\n- the task turns out to involve unexpected complexity or tangents\n- several approaches have not completed the task\n\nClaude does not keep retrying the same failing action.\n\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79/scratchpad","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-dev","slug":"rosy-bubbling-whisper"}
