ea](orca-bed-exclude-area-rule.md) — 4 points per box; [Calibration generators](calibration-generators-replace-project.md) — replace project.\n- Prompt and chat: [Sections](project-prompt-sections.md) — five, policy out of tools; [Rule placement](rule-lives-next-to-what-it-governs.md) — one-tool rules in description; [Channels](prompt-principles-vs-state-channels.md) — principles only; [No forcing field](no-required-field-to-force-a-question.md) — ask via prompt; [History trimming](history-trimming-by-size.md) — 64 KiB; [Tool replay](printer-chat-tool-history-replay.md) — saved callId; [Input tags](workspace-input-tags.md) — message parts; [State guidance](state-driven-guidance-project-chat.md) — plate picture on file open; [Stated facts](state-fact-test-the-turns-after.md) — test later turns; [Normalize](normalize-derive-current-from-relations.md) — store once, derive current; [Model pickers](composer-model-pickers.md) — per chat; [Keeps its model](chat-keeps-its-model.md) — no mid-chat switch; [Turn activity](agent-turn-activity-proposal.md) — one line per turn; [Chat capture](jusprin-chat-capture-design.md) — on in prod 2026-11-10, policy clause not opt-in; [Rebuild a request](rebuild-wire-request-from-saved-chat.md) — current-state.json; [DeepSeek images](live-app-deepseek-drops-images.md) — 404; [Standard titles](standard-title-answers-instead.md) — 4 of 12 refused.\n- Skills: [File-loaded](skill-model-arrived.md); [Slice-failed](skill-slice-failed.md); [Setup-changed](skill-setup-changed.md); [Print-issues](skill-print-issues.md); [Integrated](skills-integrated-branch.md) — 8913319cac.\n- Evals: [Live suite](live-suite-is-part-of-done.md) — part of done; [Eval spend](prompt-eval-spend-budget.md) — ask first; [Measurements](project-prompt-eval-sample-size.md) — stub rates retracted; [Live eval](live-eval-after-only-vs-baseline.md) — after-only vs baseline; [Harness critique](project-prompt-harness-critique.md); [Harness ported](project-prompt-harness-ported.md) — --project-prompt-requests; [Recorder noise](request-recorder-run-to-run-noise.md) — what to normalise; [Reply cut at 160](prompt-runner-truncates-replies.md) — lift before reading replies; slicer-basic = DeepSeek V4 Flash; [Print-setup cases](print-setup-prompt-cases.md).\n- Design process: [Design source](design-source-is-claude-artifacts.md) — Claude artifacts; [Design artifacts](jusprin-claude-design-system-artifact.md) — URLs, re-sync; [Token sync](design-token-sync-decisions.md) — chip 28, rows 36; [Design before code](update-design-before-code.md) — boards first; [Mark old boards](new-board-marks-old-superseded.md) — every page; [Show in screen](show-design-in-the-screen.md) — whole screens; [Canvas boards](canvas-boards-from-bundle-rules.md) — bundle CSS; [Board PNGs](render-canvas-boards-with-render-dc.md) — render_dc.py; [Mockup strings](mockup-strings-from-real-output.md) — real output; [Cold reader](cold-reader-agent-catches-cryptic-ui-text.md) — screenshots only, 14/23; [Unbuilt proposals](sweep-unbuilt-proposals-stay-visible.md) — say what stays.\n- Wording: [Code's own terms](use-the-codes-own-terms.md) — \"syndicate\", never \"pool\"; [No \"arrive\"](no-arrive-jargon-for-files.md) — opened/imported/loaded/added; [AI is the name](ai-is-the-feature-name.md) — not \"the Agent\".\n- Prepare and project UI: [Setup card headline](setup-card-headline-setup-record.md) — setup_record; [Setup card shape](setup-card-two-part-shape.md) — words above, facts below; [Setup-changed entry](setup-changed-entry-point.md) — A+C+D; [All settings](all-settings-panel.md) — settings_catalog; [Filament chip](filament-chip-no-spool-decisions.md) — no saved spools; [Chip statement](chip-states-selection-not-machine.md) — selection, not the machine; [File-printer switch](file-printer-switch-decisions.md) — Option 2; [Print issues](persistent-print-issues-spike.md) — Ask AI / Resolve; [Check print design](check-print-design-decisions.md) — slice_report panel; [Check print built](check-print-implementation.md); [Auto slicing reverted](auto-slice-reverted.md) — locked the UI; [Classic view return](classic-view-return-decisions.md) — banner + View menu; [Calibration](calibration-design-decisions.md) — own project.\n- Saving and menus: [Autosave design](autosave-design-research.md) — two modified trackers; [Autosave cost](autosave-save-cost-results.md) — ~2.3 µs/triangle; [Store format compat](project-store-format-compat-review.md) — StoredFormat rule, 2.0.0 fixture, Home hides unreadable, Get the new version… button; [App menus](app-menu-decisions.md) — same everywhere, grey not hide; [Save As → Export 3MF](save-as-becomes-export-3mf.md) — Cmd/Ctrl+Shift+S; [Settings menu](settings-menu-window-plus-ask-ai.md) — window + Ask AI.\n- Print history: [Screen](print-history-screen-design.md) — one record per G-code; [Report placement](print-report-lives-on-history-entry.md) — on the entry.\n- Credits and pricing: [Chat cost](per-chat-cost-estimate.md) — $0.30-0.56 measured; [Corrections](pricing-brainstorm-corrections.md) — low usage = low stickiness; [Usage vs quota](usage-against-quota-common-shape.md) — copy real screens; [Get more credits](one-action-to-get-more-credits.md) — one action; [v1 subscribers](v1-subscribers-grandfathered.md) — original price; [\"1 credit\"](credit-price-needs-its-unit.md) — needs unit; [One kind](credits-one-kind-no-ceiling.md) — no ceiling; [Credits only](balances-in-credits-only.md) — no message counts; [Boards on flow pages](credits-boards-live-on-flow-pages.md); [Account billing](account-billing-served-by-server.md) — re-asked.\n- First run and import: [Boards](first-run-flow-boards.md) — canvas v93; [Sequence](first-run-flow-sequence.md) — Welcome → Printers → Home; [Proposition](first-run-value-prop-decisions.md) — fixes failed prints; [Old onboarding](old-onboarding-boards-review.md) — email code dropped; [Sign-up reason](sign-up-reason-must-be-prominent.md) — headline; [Import scope](v1-import-scope-origin.md) — no app settings; [v1 only imports](v1-is-only-an-import-source.md) — no v1 account.\n- Accounts and server: [Sign-in form everywhere](sign-in-is-the-in-app-form-everywhere.md) — not the web page; [Full syndicate](jusprin-full-syndicate-decision.md) — jusprinv2; [JusPrin Cloud](jusprin-cloud-provider.md) — live; [Google sign-in client](jusprin2-google-sign-in-client.md) — own project `jusprin`, staging switched, branding verified; [2.0.0 waits for jusprinv2](release-2-0-0-notes-wait-for-jusprinv2.md) — publish only once it resolves; [allauth 65](allauth-65-upgrade.md) — staging; [One local server](one-local-server-no-second-stack.md) — no second stack; [Signed-in tab](signed-in-tab-cannot-self-close.md) — leave it; [Announce hold](announce-hold-forgot-closed-project-call.md) — d354a20687; [Gmail code card](gmail-code-card-undocumented.md) — stopped; [New logo](new-logo-soft-serve.md) — soft serve.\n- Tools: [Chrome extension](claude-in-chrome-lives-in-claude-profile.md) — Profile 20; [CLI WebSearch](claude-cli-websearch-differs-from-app.md) — Sources demand.\n- Retired (Figma gone 2026-10-20, header values superseded): [file](figma-jusprin-v2-file.md), [seats](figma-mcp-view-seat-limit.md), [add printer](add-printer-flow-figma-discrepancy.md), [in-file agent](drive-figma-in-file-agent-via-chrome.md), [parity](figma-dump-then-measure-parity.md), [header values](header-menu-values-kenneth-kept.md).\n- Legal text: [Principles, not specifics](legal-docs-state-principles.md) — Terms/Privacy state lasting commitments; opt-in for new uses.\n</system-reminder>"},{"type":"text","text":"<system-reminder>\nAs you answer the user's questions, you can use the following context:\n# userEmail\nThe user's email address is k@obico.io. Use it only to identify the user, such as for authorship, attribution, or filtering their own work. Never send it to an unrelated service, such as in a request header, URL, or payload, unless the user explicitly asks.\n# gitStatus\nThis is the git status at the start of the conversation. Note that this status is a snapshot in time, and will not update during the conversation.\n\nCurrent branch: jusprin-dev\n\nMain branch (you will usually use this for PRs): main\n\nGit user: Kenneth Jiang\n\nStatus:\n(clean)\n\nRecent commits:\n5eb531f5d0 Navigation: one look for each kind of way back\nf2322b9857 Home's credits: shown only while the sign-in they were read with is saved\n55873a16a6 About window and README: the nozzle prints the name once and stops\n2900b98fc7 Credits: each screen reads the account from the server when it comes on screen\ned7b6810fb Sign-in form: Terms and Privacy Policy open JusPrin's own pages\n\nClaude Code attached this context automatically; it isn't part of the user's message. It describes the user's own account and workspace, so they don't need it reported back.\n</system-reminder>\n"},{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>Bash, Edit, Read, SendMessage, Skill, ToolSearch, WebFetch, WebSearch, Write, mcp__Claude_Browser__computer, mcp__Claude_Browser__get_page_text, mcp__Claude_Browser__navigate, mcp__Claude_Browser__preview_list, mcp__Claude_Browser__preview_start, mcp__Claude_Browser__preview_stop, mcp__Claude_Browser__tabs_context, mcp__ccd_turn__update_plan, mcp__ccd_turn__wrap_up, mcp__claude-in-chrome__browser_batch, mcp__claude-in-chrome__computer, mcp__claude-in-chrome__file_upload, mcp__claude-in-chrome__find, mcp__claude-in-chrome__get_page_text, mcp__claude-in-chrome__javascript_tool, mcp__claude-in-chrome__navigate, mcp__claude-in-chrome__read_console_messages, mcp__claude-in-chrome__read_page, mcp__claude-in-chrome__tabs_close_mcp, mcp__claude-in-chrome__tabs_context_mcp, mcp__claude-in-chrome__tabs_create_mcp</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n\n   **Constraints in force (verbatim or near-verbatim):**\n   - \"Don't change anything in production, and don't change Chargebee's live site without Kenneth's explicit yes.\" Kenneth has now given an explicit yes to copy the test site's settings to JusPrin's live site, jusprinv2. Asked: \"May I change the live site's settings to match the test site?\" Answer: \"Yes, go ahead\".\n   - Ask Kenneth before any production change, including the deploy and the production webhook.\n   - Never commit submodule pointer changes.\n   - Use the service account ai-agent@tsdtechnology.iam.gserviceaccount.com for gcloud and kubectl. On this Mac: `export CLOUDSDK_PYTHON=$HOME/.local/share/uv/python/cpython-3.12.9-macos-aarch64-none/bin/python3.12`.\n   - Don't start a second docker stack.\n   - Server code goes to tsd-enterprise master.\n   - The ops repo push waits on Kenneth.\n   - I may not type passwords, government IDs or API keys; Kenneth does those himself. Never print API keys.\n   - Key files:\n     - ~/.config/jusprin/chargebee-jusprinv2-test.env (test site)\n     - ~/.config/jusprin/chargebee-jusprinv2-stg.env (staging)\n     - ~/.config/jusprin/chargebee-jusprinv2-live.env (live; variable CHARGEBEE_API_KEY, chmod 600 applied)\n   - Fix any bug without asking.\n   - Reuse existing Stripe and PayPal accounts.\n   - Read-only on Obico's live Chargebee site and on TSD's Stripe and PayPal accounts.\n\n   **Requests this stretch, in order:**\n   1. Style the jusprinv2 Chargebee site in JusPrin's branding.\n   2. Fix the blank band above \"Back to cart\", and question whether the billing address is needed. Kenneth then said \"Yes, turn it off\".\n   3. Clean up the old plans etc. from the tsd/obico Chargebee test site.\n   4. Check readiness for production.\n   5. Explain how to activate the live site. Kenneth chose \"Pay as you go\".\n   6. Open the page in Kenneth's own Chrome.\n   7. Kenneth said \"done\" (activated, invited, key saved).\n   8. Kenneth said \"Yes, go ahead\": copy the test site's settings to the live site.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n\n   **Chargebee sites:**\n   - jusprinv2-test (test) and jusprinv2 (live, newly activated on the Flow plan, Pay as you go). Both are on Product Catalog 2.0.\n   - Live site owner: jusprin-support@obico.io. k@thespaghettidetective.com is an Admin on the test site.\n   - Chrome is now signed in to Chargebee as JusPrin Support.\n   - Obico's sites, thespaghettidetective-test and thespaghettidetective live, are on Product Catalog 1.0 (plans and addons).\n\n   **Production:**\n   - All five deployments (web, ws, tasks, rttasks, beat) run kennethjiang/web_ent:obi.4098, built from master 0a75568378.\n   - Staging runs obi.4104.\n   - Master adds six commits over production, none with migrations: f624245258, d984c46317, 77fd19cadb, 2d97f4b1c7, a72b271f7e, 52d1bd7974.\n   - Production has no JUSPRIN_V2_CHARGEBEE_* env vars.\n   - Production JusPrin host jusprinv2.obico.io (Site 5, syndicate jusprinv2) still uses Obico's Google SocialApp 1 \"Obico Google+\". It has one jusprinv2 user, k@obico.io.\n\n   **Ops repo (~/Projects/ops):** two unpushed commits, both waiting on Kenneth.\n   - 1e6caf7: mine, for staging.\n   - 3f5e1b7: another session's chat-capture change, already applied to production.\n   - `kubectl diff` shows production matches the ops files, apart from tsdws replicas scaled down to 10 on purpose.\n\n   **Brand tokens:** action-primary #3A2D64, surface-subtle #F6F2F7.\n\n   **Chargebee checkout customizer:** native `type=color` inputs with ids COLOR_ACCENT, COLOR_HEADER, COLOR_HIGHLIGHT_PANEL, COLOR_CHECKOUT_PAGE, COLOR_ORDER_CARDS, COLOR_INPUT_COMPONENTS.\n   - The advanced inputs only exist in the page once \"Advanced colors\" is expanded.\n   - Set them with the HTMLInputElement value setter plus input and change events.\n   - The brand color field drops uppercase letters when typed; type lowercase \"3a2d64\".\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   **tsd-enterprise worktree** /Users/kenneth/Projects/tsd-enterprise-worktrees/jusprin-v2-own-chargebee (branch jusprin-v2-own-chargebee-on-master):\n   - docs/jusprin2-host-setup.md, section 3. Committed as 52d1bd7974 \"JusPrin 2 host setup: checkout asks no billing address and wears JusPrin's brand\" and pushed to origin master. Added text:\n     ```\n     Under Fields on the same page, disable the Billing and Shipping sections, and\n     under Payments turn on the card's Address Fields with only Zip and Country.\n     No tax is set up, so nothing needs a billing address; Obico's site asks the\n     same. Turn billing back on, with at least the country, if the site ever\n     collects tax.\n\n     Under Settings › Configure Chargebee › Brand Styles, upload JusPrin's logo\n     (the app's `resources/jusprin/overlay/images/OrcaSlicer_horizontal_light.svg`\n     as a PNG), the mark as the icon, and `jusprin/static/jusprinv2/img/favicon.png`\n     as the favicon, and set the brand color to `#3A2D64`. Under Checkout\n     (Customize Checkout), set the accent color to `#3A2D64` and the header and\n     page colors to `#F6F2F7`, JusPrin's page background. Without a logo the\n     checkout shows an empty band above \"Back to cart\".\n     ```\n   - web_ent/app_ent/cb_views.py: read only. Obico's cb_webhook ignores deletion events; it handles only SUBSCRIPTION_EVENTS and invoice_generated.\n\n   **Scratchpad** /private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79/scratchpad/:\n   - jusprin-logo-light.png: 720×256, rendered from the JusPrin lockup with `rsvg-convert -h 256`.\n   - jusprin-mark.png and jusprin-icon.png: 512×512, from resources/jusprin/branding/jusprin-mark.svg.\n   - Favicon source: …/web_ent/jusprin/static/jusprinv2/img/favicon.png (192×192).\n   - obico-test.env: Obico's test-site key as OBT. Never print it.\n   - cbl.sh: live-site API helper.\n     ```\n     #!/bin/zsh\n     source ~/.config/jusprin/chargebee-jusprinv2-live.env\n     M=$1; P=$2; shift 2\n     if [ \"$M\" = GET ]; then curl -s -G -u REDACTED \"https://jusprinv2.chargebee.com/api/v2/$P\" \"$@\"; else curl -s -u REDACTED -X $M \"https://jusprinv2.chargebee.com/api/v2/$P\" \"$@\"; fi\n     ```\n   - cbj.sh: test-site API helper.\n   - checkout.sh `<user> <what>`: starts a staging checkout and prints the hosted page URL; `what` is pack, etc.\n   - web.sh\n   - stg_users.json: users 497 pack, 498 plan, 499 prem, 500 fail, 501.\n   - stg_lots.py: run as `kubectl --context=tsd exec -i <pod> -c tsdweb-stg -- env UIDS=500 python - < stg_lots.py`.\n   - prod_read.py: read-only query of production SocialApps and Sites.\n\n   **Shared notes** /Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_3e38de32-e8df-4f8c-b26d-1a20db4c0aca/chargebee-jusprin-emails-draft.md:\n   - Appended \"Production readiness check (2026-11-10, late)\".\n   - Appended a line recording the Pay as you go choice and the activation steps.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - Chargebee color fields didn't take typed values. Fixed by setting the value through the JS value setter and dispatching input and change events.\n   - The brand color field dropped \"A\" and \"D\" when typed. Fixed by typing lowercase.\n   - On the live site, a VWO script threw \"Illegal invocation\" during the JS set. The accent and header colors had taken; the page color input wasn't in the page yet. Expanded \"Advanced colors\", then set COLOR_CHECKOUT_PAGE.\n   - Disabling the test billing address was first refused by the permission check as an account-settings change. I asked Kenneth; he said \"Yes, turn it off\".\n   - The permission check refused navigating to the live site's settings (\"Modify Shared Resources\"). I asked Kenneth; he said \"Yes, go ahead\".\n   - The coupon create failed with \"name : cannot be blank\" because of the \"%\" in the name. Fixed with `--data-urlencode`.\n   - preview_stop needed the process serverId from preview_list (browser-preview-1794347333914-66), not the previewId.\n   - Live /r/payment_preferences loads blank; /email_notifications is a 404; the test site's /notifications gives no page text.\n   - zsh glob errors with unquoted `?` and `[]` in URLs and kubectl custom-columns. Fixed by quoting.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n\n   **Test site jusprinv2-test:**\n   - Checkout colors: accent #3a2d64, header and page #f6f2f7, cards, highlight panel and inputs white.\n   - Logo, icon, favicon uploaded; brand color #3A2D64.\n   - Billing and shipping off; card asks Zip and Country, both optional.\n   - Staging purchase without billing fields: user 500 got 500 + 500 credits from invoice 16.\n\n   **Obico test site cleanup:**\n   - Deleted plans jusprin-hobby-monthly and jusprin-workshop-monthly, addon jusprin-credit-pack, coupon jusprin2-obico-premium-20.\n   - Deleted customers jusprinv2-57, jusprinv2-59, jusprinv2-490, jusprinv2-491, jusprinv2-492; subscription AzZd1kVaXEUIX4Ti3 went with them.\n   - Kept: JusPrin 1's jusprin-unlimited-* plans and all of Obico's own plans and addons.\n   - Leftover: staging user 491 has a JusPrinPlan row pointing at the deleted subscription; it expires 10 Dec.\n\n   **Live site jusprinv2 (business profile \"TSD Technology, LLC\", San Jose CA 95131, phone +14045654264, as set by Kenneth):**\n   - Catalog created via API, matching the test site:\n     - Family jusprin.\n     - Items jusprin-hobby and jusprin-workshop (plans), jusprin-credit-pack (charge).\n     - Prices jusprin-hobby-monthly $10/month, jusprin-workshop-monthly $20/month, jusprin-credit-pack-USD $10.\n     - Coupon jusprin2-obico-premium-20: 20%, forever, limited to the two plan prices.\n   - Checkout configuration, published:\n     - Plan quantity editing off; coupons on (multiple coupons off).\n     - One-time payments enabled: API only on, coupons off, edit quantity on, remove products on.\n     - Portal access \"Via Single Sign On API\".\n   - Fields, published: billing and shipping disabled; card address fields Zip and Country only.\n   - Branding applied: logo, icon, favicon, brand color #3A2D64.\n   - Customize Checkout colors saved: accent #3a2d64, header and page #f6f2f7, others white.\n   - Payment gateways: none yet.\n\n   **Activation info:** Chargebee's activation is done by the owner via \"Select Plan\". Pricing came from third-party trackers: Pay as you go 0.80%; Commit $99/month plus 0.65%.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"can we style chargebee jusprinv2 site to be consistent with the branding?\" (with a screenshot)\n   - \"also there is a big blank space above \"back to cart\". I'm not sure billing address is necessary. any point of requiring the user to enter billing address?\" (with a screenshot)\n   - \"Yes, turn it off\"\n   - \"clean up the old plans etc from the tsd/obico chargebee test site first\"\n   - \"Check to see if we're ready to roll out to production.\"\n   - \"Tell me how to activate it.\"\n   - \"Pay as you go\"\n   - \"Open the page for me so that I can do these\"\n   - \"in my own chrome\" / \"Try again\"\n   - \"done\"\n   - \"Yes, go ahead\" (answer to: \"May I change the live site's settings to match the test site?\")\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - **Live site emails:** set the sender to \"JusPrin Support <jusprin-support@obico.io>\" and copy the test site's master template (JusPrin logo). Fix the sign-off \"Jusprin-support\" to \"JusPrin Support\". The sender may need verification on the live site.\n   - **Gateways:** connect Stripe (TSD's live account) and PayPal (TSD's live business account, with Reference Transactions on) to the live site. Kenneth must sign in; open the pages for him in his Chrome. Set up Smart Routing like the test site: PayPal to PayPal, cards to Stripe.\n   - **Statement name:** set the Transaction Descriptor \"JUSPRIN\" under Payment Preferences once a gateway exists. The page loads blank by direct URL; try from the payment gateways page.\n   - **Before the deploy:** add the live webhook to https://<production host>/ent/jusprin/v2/cb_webhook. The production web host is likely app.obico.io or app.thespaghettidetective.com; check which. Then ask Kenneth before deploying.\n   - **Deploy (needs Kenneth's yes):**\n     - Build a release from master (release branch = master plus built bundles, force-pushed; CircleCI builds obi.<n>).\n     - Add REDACTED and JUSPRIN_V2_CHARGEBEE_API_KEY (live key) to tsd/prod/tsdweb-prod.yaml; the prefix stays at its default.\n     - Run one small real-card purchase.\n     - Ops push waits on Kenneth.\n   - **Open items to report:**\n     - Production Google sign-in still uses Obico's Google app: a manual SocialApp switch, with Kenneth pasting the client secret.\n     - The app's \"Ends <day>\" change 6f1f03867d is only on claude/plan-ends-line, not on jusprin-dev.\n     - Staging user 491 leftover.\n   - **Task list on screen:**\n     1. Check live site access and API key: completed.\n     2. Copy catalog and coupon to live site: completed.\n     3. Copy checkout, fields, branding, descriptor: completed, except the descriptor.\n     4. Copy email sender and templates: in progress.\n     5. Connect Stripe and PayPal with Kenneth: pending.\n     6. Report and ask to deploy: pending.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I was copying the email settings from the test site to the live site. I tried to read the test site's email notification list: https://jusprinv2-test.chargebee.com/email_notifications was a 404, and https://jusprinv2-test.chargebee.com/notifications returned no page text. A screenshot or wait was needed.\n\n   Known from earlier: the test site's /notifications/settings opens \"Customize Master Template\" with From \"JusPrin Support jusprin-support@obico.io\", the JusPrin logo, and the signature \"Regards, Jusprin-support\".\n\n   Chrome tabs:\n   - 268836873: live site, signed in as JusPrin Support.\n   - 268836818: test site.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Continue Kenneth's \"Yes, go ahead\" (copy the test site's settings to the live site), starting with emails:\n   1. Screenshot https://jusprinv2-test.chargebee.com/notifications/settings and the notifications list to read the sender profile and template.\n   2. Open https://jusprinv2.chargebee.com/notifications/settings and set the same sender (\"JusPrin Support\", jusprin-support@obico.io), the logo, and the corrected sign-off \"JusPrin Support\".\n   3. Open the live payment gateways page (https://jusprinv2.chargebee.com/payment_gateways) for Stripe and PayPal. Ask Kenneth to sign in for each connection.\n   4. Set the Transaction Descriptor \"JUSPRIN\".\n   5. Report and ask before adding the production webhook and deploying.\n\n   Earlier promise, verbatim: \"Stripe and PayPal: connecting them needs you to sign in to TSD's live accounts. I'll open those pages for you when we get there.\" and \"Production webhook: I'd add it only right before the deploy.\" and \"The deploy: that gets its own question.\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."}]}}
