{"parentUuid":"ffa59093-35a8-4ba7-aa2e-e82cd85b95c9","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"38be1999-5af5-4617-9ece-2f6f40a61611","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TYSZzmCYa7CSdhZc1XfWNb","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[navigate] Navigated to https://jusprinv2-test.chargebee.com/payment_gateways"},{"type":"text","text":"[computer:wait] Waited for 3 seconds"},{"type":"text","text":"[computer:screenshot] Successfully captured screenshot (896x487, jpeg) - ID: ss_8438069ib — 0.6-scale view; coordinate frame: 1493x812."},{"type":"image","source":{"type":"base64","media_type":"image/jpeg","data":""}},{"type":"text","text":"[Image: source: /Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79/tool-results/REDACTED.jpg]"},{"type":"text","text":"[get_page_text] Title: Payment Gateways - Chargebee\nURL: https://jusprinv2.chargebee.com/payment_gateways/38/edit?using_stripe=true\nSource element: <body>\n---\nBilling\nTSD Technology, LLC\nLive\njusprinv2.chargebee.com\nGo to\n⌘\nK\nHome\nCustomers\nSubscriptions\nInvoices & Credit Notes\nProduct Catalog\nEntitlements\nLogs\nReceivables\nNEW\nRevenueStory\nClassic Reports\nApps\nSettings\nConfigure Chargebee\nImport & Export Data\nTeam Members\nChargebee Notifications\nSecurity\nWhat's new\nNeed Help?\nJS\nJusPrin Support\njusprin-support@obico.io\nConfigure Chargebee\nPayment Gateways\nConfigure Stripe\nDisplay Name\nStripe-1\nChargebee Gateway Account ID\ngw_16A02yVacYD1N1JCL\nReconnect\nArchive\nPayment methods\nCards\nPrepaid cards: Enabled\nRetain cards in Stripe: Disabled\n3D Secure: Disabled\nManage\ntrue\nTo comply with SCA regulations, you need to enable 3D Secure if you are operating out of Europe or have customers in Europe. To enable 3D Secure, click Manage next to Cards. Learn more\nApple Pay\nAllow your customers to pay with Apple Pay. Learn more\nfalse\nDirect Debit (SEPA)\nAllow your customers to pay via their bank accounts. Learn more.\nfalse\niDEAL (Recurring via SEPA Direct Debit)\nAllow your customers in the Netherlands to pay via iDEAL (SEPA). iDEAL can be used to make payment only once. All subsequent recurring payments will be made via SEPA Direct Debit. Learn more.\nfalse\nBancontact (Recurring via SEPA Direct Debit)\nAllow your customers to pay via Bancontact(SEPA). Bancontact can be used to make payment only once. All subsequent recurring payments will be made via SEPA Direct Debit. Learn more.\nfalse\nDirect Debit (ACH/eCheck)\nAllow your customers to pay via Direct Debit (ACH/eCheck). Learn more.\nfalse\nACH Credit Transfer (For US only)\nA unique virtual bank account will be created for your customers. Payment details will be automatically added to your customers' payment due invoices. Learn more\nfalse\nAmazon Pay\nAllow your customers to pay with Amazon Pay. Learn more\nfalse\nGoogle Pay\nAllow your customers to pay with Google Pay. Learn more\nfalse\nTo avoid checkout failures, ensure Google Pay is enabled in live mode in Stripe (not just test mode). Additionally, verify if your domain is properly registered with Google Pay to avoid payment failures.\n\nLearn more in our article →\nUnified Payments Interface (UPI)\nAllow your customers to pay using UPI. Learn more\nfalse\nBoleto (For BRAZIL region only)\nBoleto is a Brazilian payment method which involves generating a voucher that your customers can use to pay at multiple locations or using secure online services. Learn more\nfalse\nBECS Direct Debit (For AUS region only)\nAllow your customers to pay via their bank accounts. Learn more.\nfalse\nBACS Direct Debit (For UK region only)\nAllow your customers to pay via their bank accounts. Learn more.\nfalse\nKlarna\nAllow your customers to pay with Klarna. Learn more\nfalse\nStablecoin\nAllow your customers to pay using Stablecoins via Stripe. Stablecoin payments can be made one‑time or set up for recurring billing (subject to eligibility and availability). Learn more\nfalse\nAlipay\nAllow your customers to pay with Alipay. Learn more\nfalse\nConfigure and customise the behaviour and features for Stripe. Go to Settings\nRadar Settings\nStripe charges per Radar screening. Skip re-screening once a payment method has a clean track record.\nRadar on customer-initiated transactions (CIT)\nAlways screens customer-present transactions: first payment, checkout, and payment method updates.\ntrue\nSkip Radar on merchant-initiated transactions (MIT)\nScreens recurring charges until they build a clean record, then skips Radar for good.\nfalse\nEnable this only after Skip Radar is turned on in your Stripe account. Turning it on here first can cause MIT payment attempts to fail.\nWebhooks\nChargebee uses the webhook feature of Stripe to listen to events occurring in your Stripe account. Learn more\nNotification URL\nCopy\nHow to configure?\nIn your Stripe account\nDisable View test data .\nGo to Developers > Webhooks > Add endpoint .\nSelect the ‘receive all events’ option to notify Chargebee of all events in Stripe.\nPaste the Notification URL in the field URL to be called.\nPrivacy Terms"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\nTab Context:\n- Executed on tabId: 268836914\n- Available tabs:\n  • tabId 268836914: \"Payment Gateways - Chargebee\" (\"https://jusprinv2.chargebee.com/payment_gateways/38/edit?using_stripe=true\")\n  • tabId 268836915: \"Payment Gateways - Chargebee\" (\"https://jusprinv2-test.chargebee.com/payment_gateways\")"}]}]},"uuid":"b8a907ac-92a6-4215-ac67-408aae880bb1","timestamp":"2026-11-11T00:43:38.976Z","toolUseResult":[{"type":"text","text":"[navigate] Navigated to https://jusprinv2-test.chargebee.com/payment_gateways"},{"type":"text","text":"[computer:wait] Waited for 3 seconds"},{"type":"text","text":"[computer:screenshot] Successfully captured screenshot (896x487, jpeg) - ID: ss_8438069ib — 0.6-scale view; coordinate frame: 1493x812."},{"type":"image","source":{"type":"base64","media_type":"image/jpeg","data":""}},{"type":"text","text":"[Image: source: /Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79/tool-results/REDACTED.jpg]"},{"type":"text","text":"[get_page_text] Title: Payment Gateways - Chargebee\nURL: https://jusprinv2.chargebee.com/payment_gateways/38/edit?using_stripe=true\nSource element: <body>\n---\nBilling\nTSD Technology, LLC\nLive\njusprinv2.chargebee.com\nGo to\n⌘\nK\nHome\nCustomers\nSubscriptions\nInvoices & Credit Notes\nProduct Catalog\nEntitlements\nLogs\nReceivables\nNEW\nRevenueStory\nClassic Reports\nApps\nSettings\nConfigure Chargebee\nImport & Export Data\nTeam Members\nChargebee Notifications\nSecurity\nWhat's new\nNeed Help?\nJS\nJusPrin Support\njusprin-support@obico.io\nConfigure Chargebee\nPayment Gateways\nConfigure Stripe\nDisplay Name\nStripe-1\nChargebee Gateway Account ID\ngw_16A02yVacYD1N1JCL\nReconnect\nArchive\nPayment methods\nCards\nPrepaid cards: Enabled\nRetain cards in Stripe: Disabled\n3D Secure: Disabled\nManage\ntrue\nTo comply with SCA regulations, you need to enable 3D Secure if you are operating out of Europe or have customers in Europe. To enable 3D Secure, click Manage next to Cards. Learn more\nApple Pay\nAllow your customers to pay with Apple Pay. Learn more\nfalse\nDirect Debit (SEPA)\nAllow your customers to pay via their bank accounts. Learn more.\nfalse\niDEAL (Recurring via SEPA Direct Debit)\nAllow your customers in the Netherlands to pay via iDEAL (SEPA). iDEAL can be used to make payment only once. All subsequent recurring payments will be made via SEPA Direct Debit. Learn more.\nfalse\nBancontact (Recurring via SEPA Direct Debit)\nAllow your customers to pay via Bancontact(SEPA). Bancontact can be used to make payment only once. All subsequent recurring payments will be made via SEPA Direct Debit. Learn more.\nfalse\nDirect Debit (ACH/eCheck)\nAllow your customers to pay via Direct Debit (ACH/eCheck). Learn more.\nfalse\nACH Credit Transfer (For US only)\nA unique virtual bank account will be created for your customers. Payment details will be automatically added to your customers' payment due invoices. Learn more\nfalse\nAmazon Pay\nAllow your customers to pay with Amazon Pay. Learn more\nfalse\nGoogle Pay\nAllow your customers to pay with Google Pay. Learn more\nfalse\nTo avoid checkout failures, ensure Google Pay is enabled in live mode in Stripe (not just test mode). Additionally, verify if your domain is properly registered with Google Pay to avoid payment failures.\n\nLearn more in our article →\nUnified Payments Interface (UPI)\nAllow your customers to pay using UPI. Learn more\nfalse\nBoleto (For BRAZIL region only)\nBoleto is a Brazilian payment method which involves generating a voucher that your customers can use to pay at multiple locations or using secure online services. Learn more\nfalse\nBECS Direct Debit (For AUS region only)\nAllow your customers to pay via their bank accounts. Learn more.\nfalse\nBACS Direct Debit (For UK region only)\nAllow your customers to pay via their bank accounts. Learn more.\nfalse\nKlarna\nAllow your customers to pay with Klarna. Learn more\nfalse\nStablecoin\nAllow your customers to pay using Stablecoins via Stripe. Stablecoin payments can be made one‑time or set up for recurring billing (subject to eligibility and availability). Learn more\nfalse\nAlipay\nAllow your customers to pay with Alipay. Learn more\nfalse\nConfigure and customise the behaviour and features for Stripe. Go to Settings\nRadar Settings\nStripe charges per Radar screening. Skip re-screening once a payment method has a clean track record.\nRadar on customer-initiated transactions (CIT)\nAlways screens customer-present transactions: first payment, checkout, and payment method updates.\ntrue\nSkip Radar on merchant-initiated transactions (MIT)\nScreens recurring charges until they build a clean record, then skips Radar for good.\nfalse\nEnable this only after Skip Radar is turned on in your Stripe account. Turning it on here first can cause MIT payment attempts to fail.\nWebhooks\nChargebee uses the webhook feature of Stripe to listen to events occurring in your Stripe account. Learn more\nNotification URL\nCopy\nHow to configure?\nIn your Stripe account\nDisable View test data .\nGo to Developers > Webhooks > Add endpoint .\nSelect the ‘receive all events’ option to notify Chargebee of all events in Stripe.\nPaste the Notification URL in the field URL to be called.\nPrivacy Terms"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\nTab Context:\n- Executed on tabId: 268836914\n- Available tabs:\n  • tabId 268836914: \"Payment Gateways - Chargebee\" (\"https://jusprinv2.chargebee.com/payment_gateways/38/edit?using_stripe=true\")\n  • tabId 268836915: \"Payment Gateways - Chargebee\" (\"https://jusprinv2-test.chargebee.com/payment_gateways\")"}],"classifierBoundary":true,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ffa59093-35a8-4ba7-aa2e-e82cd85b95c9","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/ops","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-dev","slug":"rosy-bubbling-whisper"}
