{"parentUuid":"b8a9cf3b-4c57-4099-89bb-7b80dc84e2e0","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"38be1999-5af5-4617-9ece-2f6f40a61611","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EZaUVPX3AaL7LzDNi7heMX","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Chargebee transaction descriptor setting Stripe statement descriptor where to configure\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Transaction Descriptors - Chargebee Payment Docs\",\"url\":\"https://www.chargebee.com/docs/2.0/transaction_descriptors.html\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding Statement Descriptors in Stripe via ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.chargebee.com/docs/payments/2.0/kb/billing/understanding-statement-descriptors-in-stripe-via-chargebee\"},{\"title\":\"How to use Transaction Descriptors on Payment Gateways in Chargebee?: Chargebee Support Portal\",\"url\":\"https://support.chargebee.com/support/solutions/articles/260535-how-to-use-transaction-descriptors-on-payment-gateways-in-chargebee-\"},{\"title\":\"Stripe - statement descriptors\",\"url\":\"https://www.chargebee.com/docs/payments/2.0/kb/payments/transaction-descriptor-i-want-my-companys-name-to-appear-on-my-customers-bank-statements-how-do-i-set-this-up-on-stripe\"},{\"title\":\"Payment Preferences\",\"url\":\"https://www.chargebee.com/docs/payments/2.0/others/payment-preferences\"},{\"title\":\"PayPay via Stripe - Chargebee Docs\",\"url\":\"https://www.chargebee.com/docs/payments/2.0/payment-gateways-and-configuration/stripe-paypay\"},{\"title\":\"Transactions\",\"url\":\"https://apidocs.chargebee.com/docs/api/transactions\"},{\"title\":\"Pix via dLocal - Chargebee Docs\",\"url\":\"https://www.chargebee.com/docs/payments/2.0/payment-gateways-and-configuration/dlocal-pix\"},{\"title\":\"Chargebee Pay Onboarding - Chargebee Docs\",\"url\":\"https://www.chargebee.com/docs/payments/2.0/payment-gateways-and-configuration/getting-started\"},{\"title\":\"South Korean Cards via Stripe - Chargebee Docs\",\"url\":\"https://www.chargebee.com/docs/payments/2.0/payment-gateways-and-configuration/stripe-south-korean-cards\"}]\n\nChargebee's docs point to two places to configure the descriptor, and the menu paths differ between the older and newer documentation.\n\n- **Chargebee site (older docs and support article):** Navigate to Settings > Configure Chargebee > Payment Gateways > Add a Descriptor. The descriptor applies to every gateway in your Chargebee site.\n- **Chargebee site (newer Payment Preferences docs):** Go to Payments > Payment Gateways, then click Manage Settings from the Payment Preferences block. The Stripe-specific setting there is an option to send the suffix for Apple Pay and Google Pay as well as cards (default off).\n- **Stripe dashboard:** Stripe's own business name is set separately, under Account Settings > Public Information > Statement Descriptor.\n- **Per-transaction override:** Chargebee's API accepts a statement_descriptor parameter, which will override the descriptor you have set on your Chargebee site.\n\nStripe's limits matter here. Chargebee's documentation says Stripe enforces a 22-character limit for card transaction descriptors, including the asterisk * and spaces. In Stripe's format, the part before the asterisk (*) is set directly in the merchant's Stripe dashboard. Chargebee's guide suggests sending only a short suffix, such as \"PRIME\", to avoid truncation.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"8cf1dd3c-a86e-4908-8a2b-33cbdfcf52ae","timestamp":"2026-11-11T00:46:10.219Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"Chargebee transaction descriptor setting Stripe statement descriptor where to configure","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01BcjAF99tpnB17j74PNzKRB","content":[{"title":"Transaction Descriptors - Chargebee Payment Docs","url":"https://www.chargebee.com/docs/2.0/transaction_descriptors.html"},{"title":"Understanding Statement Descriptors in Stripe via ...","url":"https://www.chargebee.com/docs/payments/2.0/kb/billing/understanding-statement-descriptors-in-stripe-via-chargebee"},{"title":"How to use Transaction Descriptors on Payment Gateways in Chargebee?: Chargebee Support Portal","url":"https://support.chargebee.com/support/solutions/articles/260535-how-to-use-transaction-descriptors-on-payment-gateways-in-chargebee-"},{"title":"Stripe - statement descriptors","url":"https://www.chargebee.com/docs/payments/2.0/kb/payments/transaction-descriptor-i-want-my-companys-name-to-appear-on-my-customers-bank-statements-how-do-i-set-this-up-on-stripe"},{"title":"Payment Preferences","url":"https://www.chargebee.com/docs/payments/2.0/others/payment-preferences"},{"title":"PayPay via Stripe - Chargebee Docs","url":"https://www.chargebee.com/docs/payments/2.0/payment-gateways-and-configuration/stripe-paypay"},{"title":"Transactions","url":"https://apidocs.chargebee.com/docs/api/transactions"},{"title":"Pix via dLocal - Chargebee Docs","url":"https://www.chargebee.com/docs/payments/2.0/payment-gateways-and-configuration/dlocal-pix"},{"title":"Chargebee Pay Onboarding - Chargebee Docs","url":"https://www.chargebee.com/docs/payments/2.0/payment-gateways-and-configuration/getting-started"},{"title":"South Korean Cards via Stripe - Chargebee Docs","url":"https://www.chargebee.com/docs/payments/2.0/payment-gateways-and-configuration/stripe-south-korean-cards"}]},"Chargebee's docs point to two places to configure the descriptor, and the menu paths differ between the older and newer documentation.\n\n- **Chargebee site (older docs and support article):** Navigate to Settings > Configure Chargebee > Payment Gateways > Add a Descriptor. The descriptor applies to every gateway in your Chargebee site.\n- **Chargebee site (newer Payment Preferences docs):** Go to Payments > Payment Gateways, then click Manage Settings from the Payment Preferences block. The Stripe-specific setting there is an option to send the suffix for Apple Pay and Google Pay as well as cards (default off).\n- **Stripe dashboard:** Stripe's own business name is set separately, under Account Settings > Public Information > Statement Descriptor.\n- **Per-transaction override:** Chargebee's API accepts a statement_descriptor parameter, which will override the descriptor you have set on your Chargebee site.\n\nStripe's limits matter here. Chargebee's documentation says Stripe enforces a 22-character limit for card transaction descriptors, including the asterisk * and spaces. In Stripe's format, the part before the asterisk (*) is set directly in the merchant's Stripe dashboard. Chargebee's guide suggests sending only a short suffix, such as \"PRIME\", to avoid truncation."],"durationSeconds":5.303789749999996,"searchCount":1},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b8a9cf3b-4c57-4099-89bb-7b80dc84e2e0","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/ops","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-dev","slug":"rosy-bubbling-whisper"}
