{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","id":"6edf276c-3535-4ee6-854e-8b35d917a445","timestamp":"2026-11-11T00:47:22.137Z","version":"2.1.309","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"da73513a254bf836b57e2900c63c230613663d1ee4c9926cb06de70fc600e87a","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"high"}},"base":"7ab68c76-1c38-4ca4-9dfa-8870d498b840","keep":188,"tail":["4b98dc9920a1a589ececcab2938447510cbfa67b8a6242703e13de60e9fce79f","8ece09c40f6c8ca6fdeae4c7cdcf74ba8c61afaf9ebb0884c70ae75b6910e0ba","8d5417819870814c986d7076932ad2dcad28287bdd05a674772b4c6ce5fb42e5"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",190,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"02f3439de95209847c4974ee6afcd68b495761d5c83951d949107bbd20b0cb75"}
{"parentUuid":"0c56aa71-f99c-45d6-8705-7ae0a530d3ac","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvDfCBTScp6dFYE1evvX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stripe is connected correctly. The live Chargebee site now takes cards through TSD Technology's Stripe account, and the PayPal connect window is open in your Chrome for you.\n\n**What I checked on Stripe:**\n- Chargebee shows a gateway named \"Stripe-1\" with cards on and every other payment method off.\n- TSD's Stripe account (acct_1CrFhqLPS4omY4v8) logged \"Your account authorized the Chargebee application\" at 4:42 PM today. Your Stripe sign-in can also reach \"Atlas Account\" and \"GitHub Sponsors\", so this log entry is what shows you picked the right account.\n- A minute later Stripe logged an \"account updated\" event, but it lists no changed fields, so nothing on TSD's account changed.\n- TSD's Stripe account has no webhooks, which means Obico's Chargebee site runs without one too. JusPrin's site can do the same.\n\n**Name on card statements:** I set \"JUSPRIN\" as the descriptor. TSD's Stripe account puts \"OBICO\" in front of it, so a JusPrin charge will read \"OBICO* JUSPRIN\". Without the descriptor it would have read \"OBICO/THE SPAGHETTI DE\".\n\n**I was wrong about one thing:** I said I'd copy the test site's routing, with PayPal payments going to PayPal and cards to Stripe. The test site actually has no gateway connected. Its purchases ran through Chargebee's built-in test gateway, so there is no routing to copy. Chargebee picks the right gateway for each payment method by itself, so nothing needs setting up.\n\n**Your turn: PayPal.** The live site's tab in your Chrome shows the \"Connect with PayPal\" window. Click **Connect to an existing account** and sign in to TSD's PayPal business account. Once it's connected, I'll check it the same way I checked Stripe.\n\nSources: [Transaction Descriptors (Chargebee docs)](https://www.chargebee.com/docs/2.0/transaction_descriptors.html), [Payment Preferences (Chargebee docs)](https://www.chargebee.com/docs/payments/2.0/others/payment-preferences), [Stripe statement descriptors via Chargebee](https://www.chargebee.com/docs/payments/2.0/kb/billing/understanding-statement-descriptors-in-stripe-via-chargebee)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":831,"cache_read_input_tokens":175430,"output_tokens":799,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":831,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":799,"cache_read_input_tokens":175430,"cache_creation_input_tokens":831,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":831},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgvDfBvLUwSzHnq4V43XM","requestRef":"6edf276c-3535-4ee6-854e-8b35d917a445","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"bcd98061-ea55-4d0f-b861-f464da5a8138","timestamp":"2026-11-11T00:47:29.663Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/ops","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-dev","slug":"rosy-bubbling-whisper"}
