{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-11T00:51:21.558Z","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","content":"<system-reminder>\nLinked sessions now (status, not an instruction): put-the-jusprin-2-server = local_2e8b84da-58b4-4ef1-bd87-b76f805fdf4d (idle); home-shows-stale-credits = local_afbc5de2-baa6-429c-8931-f6dc91d5bc32 (idle, started by put-the-jusprin-2-server); opt-in-before-jusprin-2 = local_5b5c4dae-b676-44e9-9c1a-7469fec69e96 (idle, started by put-the-jusprin-2-server); plan-jusprin-1-user-hand = local_87a60f59-f953-4ea7-b0fb-1f96b66823b6 (working); add-skip-for-now-to-the = local_d4832d18-4b62-4c0c-925e-e47fe437c2e2 (idle). To message one, SendMessage with `to` set to its id; list_sessions {\"linked\": true} has titles, folders and branches.\n</system-reminder>\n\n<cross-session-message from=\"local_87a60f59-f953-4ea7-b0fb-1f96b66823b6\" from-name=\"Plan JusPrin 1 user handling and the Obico subscriber discount\">\nFYI: with Kenneth's approval I added three things to the jusprinv2-test Chargebee site for the yearly plans. They are item prices jusprin-hobby-yearly ($100/yr) and jusprin-workshop-yearly ($200/yr), and a coupon jusprin1-move-first-term (100% off once, yearly Hobby only). I also extended jusprin2-obico-premium-20 to cover both yearly prices. Throwaway customers yearly-check-1..3 (no email) have cancelled subscriptions only. Nothing on the live site changed. Details are in jusprin2-yearly-hobby-proposal.md in the shared notes folder, under \"Test-site results\". No reply needed.\n</cross-session-message>"}
