{"parentUuid":"2f483f0c-25fe-4f46-b0e3-3fb78892c2ab","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvEBLPegRwY5hcXHJXqW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"PayPal is connected correctly, so the live Chargebee site is ready to take payments. What's left is production: its server doesn't point at this site yet.\n\n**What I checked on PayPal:**\n- Chargebee lists a gateway named \"Paypal-1\".\n- Only PayPal's own button is on. Cards through PayPal and Venmo are off, so all card payments go through Stripe.\n- The PayPal account you were signed in to while connecting is TSD Technology LLC's business account (merchant ID 5LEKESCBJJP9S).\n- Chargebee's routing sends US-dollar card payments to Stripe and PayPal payments to PayPal.\n\n**One thing I couldn't check:** Chargebee shows a standard reminder that a PayPal plan only renews if \"Reference Transactions\" is on in the PayPal account. I can't see that setting from here. My guess is it's already on, if Obico's Chargebee site renews subscriptions through this same PayPal account, but I haven't checked that either. If it's off, a PayPal plan purchase would go through once and fail at the first renewal. One-time credit packs aren't affected.\n\n**Decision needed: deploy JusPrin 2's purchases to production.** It's yours because it changes production and spends real money on a test purchase. If you say yes, I'll do these in order:\n1. Build a release from master. It adds six commits over what production runs, none of which change the database.\n2. Add the live site's name and API key to `tsd/prod/tsdweb-prod.yaml` in the ops repo and apply them. That repo has two earlier commits still waiting on you to push, and this would be a third.\n3. Add the webhook `https://app.obico.io/ent/jusprin/v2/cb_webhook` on the live Chargebee site, right after the new release is up.\n4. Buy one $10 credit pack with a real card at jusprinv2.obico.io and check that the credits show up. I'd refund it afterwards.\n\nThe other choice is to wait, which costs nothing. Production keeps running as it does now, and nobody can buy from JusPrin 2 there.\n\nOne more thing is still open, whatever you decide: Google sign-in on jusprinv2.obico.io still uses Obico's Google app. Switching it is a manual change in the production admin, and you'd need to paste the client secret.\n\nI recommend deploying now, so the real purchase tests the whole path while the settings are fresh. Should I go ahead with the deploy?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1630,"cache_read_input_tokens":187067,"output_tokens":800,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1630,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":800,"cache_read_input_tokens":187067,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1630,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1630},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgvEBL9XQKnMEhUfwWPyd","requestRef":"9975c156-c7bd-453a-9d01-74c88fb49ed2","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"56da62ad-e631-47e5-8f84-3483e3654b5b","timestamp":"2026-11-11T00:54:21.838Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-dev","slug":"rosy-bubbling-whisper"}
