{"parentUuid":"ed429582-721a-4232-a24b-c9e51b63fd5c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvFpfdvv99uC34WJH8WF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"JusPrin 2 purchases are now live in production. The only check left is a real card purchase, which needs you.\n\n**What's live and checked:**\n- **New version:** all of production's web, background-task and scheduler servers run `obi.4104`. That's the version staging has run all day; it has no database changes.\n- **Live site:** a production web server reads the live site's prices: $10 Hobby, $20 Workshop, $10 credit pack.\n- **Webhook:** `https://app.obico.io/ent/jusprin/v2/cb_webhook` is on the live site. I sent it a made-up event id, and production looked the id up on the live site with the new key and rejected it, which is the expected response. So the address, the code and the key all work together.\n- **Websocket servers:** they finished their last copy while I was checking. They keep their 10 copies.\n- **Ops repo:** the config change is committed but not pushed. The repo now has three commits waiting on your push.\n\n**Your turn: one real purchase.**\n1. In your Chrome, the tab \"Credits and plans · JusPrin\" shows jusprinv2.obico.io's prices page.\n2. Sign in as k@obico.io, then buy one **Credit pack** ($10) with a real card.\n3. That account has 488 credits now. It should go to 1,488: 500 from the pack and 500 from the launch offer. Tell me when you've paid, and I'll check the credits, the Chargebee invoice and the Stripe charge.\n\nI can't issue refunds, because that moves money. To get the $10 back afterwards, refund it in Chargebee yourself, or keep the credits.\n\n**Runbook fix:** I asked the session that wrote the runbook, [Put the JusPrin 2 server host live in production](#local_2e8b84da-58b4-4ef1-bd87-b76f805fdf4d), to fix it, and I'll review the commit when it reports back. The problem is bigger than the Google option: the setup command those runbook steps name no longer exists. Commit f624245258 removed it when JusPrin got its own Google app. So the runbook should send people to the host setup doc for creating the site and connecting Google sign-in. That session is told to commit only that file in the ops repo, not push, and not touch production.\n\n**PayPal, still open:** PayPal turned down TSD's application to save customers' PayPal payment methods. I expect that breaks PayPal for plans; I don't know yet whether one-time credit packs are affected. Once the card purchase checks out, I'll propose whether to test PayPal with one credit pack or turn PayPal off until PayPal approves it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":856,"cache_read_input_tokens":243125,"output_tokens":849,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":856,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":849,"cache_read_input_tokens":243125,"cache_creation_input_tokens":856,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":856},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"4d3c0387-57a7-478c-95b8-b6538d3e3f35","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgvFpfM58puKB61eNHcP7","requestRef":"033107ab-240c-4e71-99e3-732cb1c366fa","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"96a709dd-975f-4fa6-a878-2a18a4cfe854","timestamp":"2026-11-11T01:15:53.556Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/tsd-enterprise-worktrees/jusprin-v2-own-chargebee","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"jusprin-dev","slug":"rosy-bubbling-whisper"}
