{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-11T01:15:58.004Z","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","content":"<cross-session-message from=\"local_2e8b84da-58b4-4ef1-bd87-b76f805fdf4d\" from-name=\"Put the JusPrin 2 server host live in production\">\nThe ops RUNBOOK fix is two local commits on ops master, not pushed: 518f49a and b2beb75. Review them together with `git diff d9d4cc1..b2beb75 -- tsd/RUNBOOK.md`, or `git show 518f49a b2beb75`. Only tsd/RUNBOOK.md changed. Your a0b8fc7 is untouched underneath, so ops master is now 5 ahead of origin.\n\nWhat the new steps 3-4 say:\n- Step 3 keeps the syndicate id sequence reset, with an explanation. Base and kingroon were inserted with explicit ids, so the sequence still points at an id they already use. Section 1's `Syndicate.objects.get_or_create(name='jusprinv2')` would then fail on a duplicate primary key on any new server. The doc's section 1 doesn't mention this, which is a gap in the doc. Fixing the doc is outside your scope (tsd/RUNBOOK.md only), so I didn't touch it.\n- Step 3 then replaces the removed `set_up_jusprinv2_syndicate --google-from` command with a pointer to tsd-enterprise `docs/jusprin2-host-setup.md`:\n  - section 1 creates the syndicate and site in a Django shell;\n  - section 2 adds the \"JusPrin Google\" sign-in app in the admin and unticks the host on Obico's Google app.\n  \n  It notes both servers were done on 2026-11-10.\n- Step 4 now names the \"JusPrin 2 server\" OAuth client in the Google Cloud project `jusprin`: a new host's callback URL must be one of that client's redirect URIs.\n\nProduction itself was switched earlier today with Kenneth's go-ahead. jusprinv2.obico.io's Google sign-in now redirects with the JusPrin client ID 477983024689-h769…, and app.obico.io still uses Obico's client. I also made tsd-enterprise 5715329f4d, local and unpushed, which updates the doc's status line to say production is set up.\n</cross-session-message>"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"dequeue","timestamp":"2026-11-11T01:15:58.087Z","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79"}
