/Users/kenneth/Projects/tsd-enterprise-worktrees/jusprin-v2-own-chargebee","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"jusprin-dev","slug":"rosy-bubbling-whisper"}
{"parentUuid":"54934627-4c86-480d-be6d-4836017f8a5f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b1634dba-da91-421d-a60f-23684f82ecda","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0131zKLyopZNPpKCcb3jNi6v","type":"tool_result","content":"b2beb75 RUNBOOK: say what the JusPrin host setup doc's two sections do\n518f49a RUNBOOK: JusPrin's host is set up by hand with JusPrin's own Google app\na0b8fc7 Production: obi.4104, JusPrin 2 sells on its own live Chargebee site (jusprinv2)\n1e6caf7 Staging: obi.4104, JusPrin 2 sells on its own Chargebee test site (jusprinv2-test) with its own customer prefix\n3f5e1b7 Keep JusPrin 2 chats in staging and production; production beat on obi.4098\nd9d4cc1 Release obi.4098; jusprinv2.obico.io live in production\ndiff --git a/tsd/RUNBOOK.md b/tsd/RUNBOOK.md\nindex a6e8d06..cb0cdfb 100644\n--- a/tsd/RUNBOOK.md\n+++ b/tsd/RUNBOOK.md\n@@ -106,14 +106,15 @@ Rolling it out, staging first:\n    `python manage.py shell` on a web pod:\n    `from django.core.management.color import no_style; from django.db import connection; from app.models import Syndicate; [connection.cursor().execute(s) for s in connection.ops.sequence_reset_sql(no_style(), [Syndicate])]`\n    (done on staging 2026-11-04 and production 2026-11-10). Without it the\n-   next step fails and rolls back. Then:\n-   `run_django_mgmt_cmd.sh set_up_jusprinv2_syndicate jusprinv2-stg.obico.io --google-from app-stg.obico.io`\n-   (production: `jusprinv2.obico.io --google-from app.obico.io`). It makes the\n-   `jusprinv2` syndicate and the site for the host, takes the site out of the\n-   base syndicate that a new site joins automatically, and puts Obico's Google\n-   sign-in app on it. Safe to run again.\n-4. Google Cloud console, the OAuth client of that Google sign-in app: add\n-   `https://<host>/accounts/google/login/callback/` as a redirect URI.\n+   next step's new `jusprinv2` syndicate row fails on a duplicate id. Then\n+   set up the host by hand, as tsd-enterprise `docs/jusprin2-host-setup.md`\n+   describes (done on staging and production 2026-11-10): section 1 makes the\n+   `jusprinv2` syndicate and the host's site in a Django shell, and section 2\n+   adds the \"JusPrin Google\" sign-in app for the host in the admin and unticks\n+   the host on Obico's Google app.\n+4. Google Cloud console, the `jusprin` project's \"JusPrin 2 server\" OAuth\n+   client: a new host's `https://<host>/accounts/google/login/callback/` must\n+   be one of its redirect URIs.\n 5. The desktop app's default gateway (`ProviderProfile.hpp` in JusPrin, the\n    \"jusprin\" row) is `https://jusprinv2.obico.io/ent/jusprin/v2/responses`. To\n    test against staging, set `jusprin_server/base_url` to\n tsd/RUNBOOK.md | 17 +++++++++--------\n 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"c7691ccc-bf38-4a05-93e4-38cd35d5c5da","timestamp":"2026-11-11T01:16:02.542Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"b2beb75 RUNBOOK: say what the JusPrin host setup doc's two sections do\n518f49a RUNBOOK: JusPrin's host is set up by hand with JusPrin's own Google app\na0b8fc7 Production: obi.4104, JusPrin 2 sells on its own live Chargebee site (jusprinv2)\n1e6caf7 Staging: obi.4104, JusPrin 2 sells on its own Chargebee test site (jusprinv2-test) with its own customer prefix\n3f5e1b7 Keep JusPrin 2 chats in staging and production; production beat on obi.4098\nd9d4cc1 Release obi.4098; jusprinv2.obico.io live in production\ndiff --git a/tsd/RUNBOOK.md b/tsd/RUNBOOK.md\nindex a6e8d06..cb0cdfb 100644\n--- a/tsd/RUNBOOK.md\n+++ b/tsd/RUNBOOK.md\n@@ -106,14 +106,15 @@ Rolling it out, staging first:\n    `python manage.py shell` on a web pod:\n    `from django.core.management.color import no_style; from django.db import connection; from app.models import Syndicate; [connection.cursor().execute(s) for s in connection.ops.sequence_reset_sql(no_style(), [Syndicate])]`\n    (done on staging 2026-11-04 and production 2026-11-10). Without it the\n-   next step fails and rolls back. Then:\n-   `run_django_mgmt_cmd.sh set_up_jusprinv2_syndicate jusprinv2-stg.obico.io --google-from app-stg.obico.io`\n-   (production: `jusprinv2.obico.io --google-from app.obico.io`). It makes the\n-   `jusprinv2` syndicate and the site for the host, takes the site out of the\n-   base syndicate that a new site joins automatically, and puts Obico's Google\n-   sign-in app on it. Safe to run again.\n-4. Google Cloud console, the OAuth client of that Google sign-in app: add\n-   `https://<host>/accounts/google/login/callback/` as a redirect URI.\n+   next step's new `jusprinv2` syndicate row fails on a duplicate id. Then\n+   set up the host by hand, as tsd-enterprise `docs/jusprin2-host-setup.md`\n+   describes (done on staging and production 2026-11-10): section 1 makes the\n+   `jusprinv2` syndicate and the host's site in a Django shell, and section 2\n+   adds the \"JusPrin Google\" sign-in app for the host in the admin and unticks\n+   the host on Obico's Google app.\n+4. Google Cloud console, the `jusprin` project's \"JusPrin 2 server\" OAuth\n+   client: a new host's `https://<host>/accounts/google/login/callback/` must\n+   be one of its redirect URIs.\n 5. The desktop app's default gateway (`ProviderProfile.hpp` in JusPrin, the\n    \"jusprin\" row) is `https://jusprinv2.obico.io/ent/jusprin/v2/responses`. To\n    test against staging, set `jusprin_server/base_url` to\n tsd/RUNBOOK.md | 17 +++++++++--------\n 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"54934627-4c86-480d-be6d-4836017f8a5f","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/ops","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"jusprin-dev","slug":"rosy-bubbling-whisper"}
