apps"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"613e3006-abfd-4472-b652-b56740453827","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgvG9WsrvCFzjQNEtVnV7","requestRef":"1aae8cb1-8c85-41d2-a085-bd2c0f4399e6","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"8f40b61a-b0d5-4012-a8cf-ed18763aefa6","timestamp":"2026-11-11T01:20:07.847Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"jusprin-dev","slug":"rosy-bubbling-whisper"}
{"parentUuid":"8f40b61a-b0d5-4012-a8cf-ed18763aefa6","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"16ae14a2-1e99-4738-9d6f-53e28aadea9d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PV9dGDM6vozxSRVNH3kW6t","type":"tool_result","content":"---\nname: ux-walkthrough-real-app-recipe\ndescription: \"How to drive the real built JusPrin app for a screenshot-per-step UX walkthrough (2026-10-28): scratch copies, the empty local_machines loop with the fake printer, why background app_* tools fail on Orca dialogs, and where screenshots land.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 33551592-d22c-4161-9a14-9a22ef798541\n  modified: 2026-10-28T13:12:42.393Z\n---\n\nOn 2026-10-28 I walked six scenarios (open-and-print, fix-a-problem) through the real app with Opus 5.5 and published the critique at https://claude.ai/artifact/XyVvteGiKhiJ6apUx8rcmR (34 frames, scratch copy at scratchpad/ux/ of that session). Kenneth's steer: start from files people actually download (MakerWorld 3MFs carry a full Bambu profile: printer, print preset, filaments, colours, bed type, designer, licence), not from generated STLs. `~/Downloads` has Tape_4_3MF.3mf (A1 mini profile), find_my_hollow.3mf (P1S, 3 colours, 233 mm wide, too big for an A1 mini), arrow_headband.3mf (P1S), general_purpose_hook.STL (bare).\n\n**Recipe that worked**\n- `ditto` the built .app out of `build/arm64/src/RelWithDebInfo/` into the scratchpad before launching (another session's ninja can relink it underneath you); the bundle id is already unique (`io.jusprin.JusPrin`), no re-sign needed.\n- `ditto` `~/Library/Application Support/JusPrin2` to a scratch `--datadir`; set `jusprin.fake_printer=true`, `presets.machine` to the saved \"Bambu Lab A1 mini 2\", write `jusprin/fake_printer.json`, delete `jusprin/mcp.json.lock`.\n- **Clear `local_machines`.** Kenneth's conf carries a `local_machines` entry keyed by the empty string (old Moonraker experiment). With the fake Bambu agent on, `init_networking_callbacks`' connect callback calls `DeviceManager::set_selected_machine(\"\")` in a loop (\"same lan machine, dev_id =, disconnect and reconnect\"), the main window disappears and the log grew 700 MB in two minutes. Clearing the map fixed it. The loop has no guard; see [[fake-bambu-printer-sim]] and [[harness-fake-printer-cleanup]].\n- Background `app_*` tools cannot press OrcaSlicer's custom `Button`s (no AX action) and the hit test at the dialog's screen position reports \"belongs to a different process\". `request_full_control` + `computer_batch` works for everything, including the Agent web view and the macOS file chooser (`cmd+shift+g`, type the path, Return, Return). Re-front the app with `open_application` when another session's harness steals focus.\n- Every `app_screenshot`/`computer_batch` screenshot is written as a JPEG under `~/.claude/projects/<project>/<session>/tool-results/mcp-computer-use-blob-*.jpg`; copy those for a report instead of fighting `screencapture`.\n- The dev build (-O0) slices a 38 mm part in over a minute; wait 45–60 s before judging a slice.\n\n**Why:** the first launch attempt looked like an app bug (blank window, title \"Couldn't save\") and cost ten minutes; the dialog-click refusals cost another ten.\n**How to apply:** reuse this for any \"walk through the app as a user\" request; keep scenarios on downloaded files; write the critique per step as what the person knows / sees / finds confusing. Related: [[live-test-built-app-on-mac]], [[drive-app-with-posted-key-events]].\n---\nname: scratch-app-driving-traps\ndescription: \"Seven traps met driving a scratch copy of the built app without screen control (2026-11-04): in-place binary copy gets SIGKILL, Home drops bridge messages while hidden, header popups need a posted NSEvent, lldb std::string args, wx Wrap reuse.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: reference\n  originSessionId: dea8379c-b02c-43a2-a254-4c2259672439\n  modified: 2026-11-04T18:59:38.548Z\n---\n\nMet while verifying print-host printer window fixes on the scratch `.app` (see [[live-test-built-app-on-mac]], [[open-file-in-app-without-screen-control]]).\n\n- **Copy a new build into a `.app` with `rm` then `cp`.** `cp` over the existing signed binary keeps the inode; the kernel kills the launch at once (exit 137, nothing logged).\n- **A launch from a plain Bash call dies when the call ends.** Start the app with `run_in_background: true` and `exec`.\n- **Home ignores bridge messages while the main window shows a project.** A queued `launch_monitor` through `JUSPRIN_HOME_DEV_URL` is sent by the page and silently dropped; switch to Home first (`m_tabpanel->SetSelection(0)` via lldb).\n- **Background `app_click` does not reach the header's popup menus** (they are not listed as windows). Post the click into the app's queue with lldb: `expr -l objc -- @import AppKit`, then `NSEvent mouseEventWithType:NSEventTypeLeftMouseDown/Up location:NSMakePoint(x, y-from-popup-bottom) ... windowNumber:[popup windowNumber]` and `[NSApp postEvent:atStart:NO]`. Render the popup with `cacheDisplayInRect:` on its contentView ([[capture-mac-popups-for-platform-diff]]).\n- **lldb cannot build `std::string` args.** This libc++ uses the alternate short-string layout: a 24-byte char array with the text at offset 0 and its length in byte 23 (≤ 22 chars), passed as `*(std::string*)buf`.\n- **wx `wxStaticText::Wrap()` (Orca's wx) skips a width it already wrapped at and keeps the first text it wrapped**, so SetLabel + Wrap on a reused label comes back unwrapped. Use a fresh label.\n- **With the screen locked, an instrumented dev page stops polling** (WebKit throttles the hidden page's timers; `document.visibilityState` is \"hidden\"). Run JS in it through lldb instead: walk `[NSApp windows]` → subviews to the `WKWebView` (match its title or `URL`), then `[webview evaluateJavaScript:@\"…\" completionHandler:nil]`; the page can `fetch()` results to the dev server. A menu item without a shortcut: `[[item target] performSelector:[item action] withObject:item afterDelay:0.5]` from lldb, so the modal it opens runs after detach.\n- **A locked screen slows the whole app 2-4×** (2026-11-05: the same first-launch OrcaSlicer import took 46 s unlocked at 15:48, 226 s locked at 19:22, same build and folder). Compare timings only between back-to-back runs under the same conditions, old and new builds side by side.\n---\nname: live-test-built-app-on-mac\ndescription: \"How to launch, see, and drive the locally built JusPrin app on the Mac: the shared bundle id binds tools to the wrong instance, and \\\"on another Space\\\" usually means the window is on the second monitor, not that the user is in full screen.\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: fa2d66ed-e217-440b-aae0-da4164953edc\n  modified: 2026-11-01T19:29:08.107Z\n---\n\nEvery build of the fork (and /Applications/OrcaSlicer.app) shares bundle id `com.softfever3d.orca-slicer`. The desktop-control tools resolve an app by bundle id and bind to whichever instance comes first, so `app_list_windows` returns `[]` and filtered screenshots hide the window you actually launched.\n\n**Working recipe (2026-09-05):** `ditto` the built .app into the scratchpad, `plutil -replace CFBundleIdentifier -string com.jusprin.worktree-test`, `codesign --force --deep -s -`, then `open -n <copy>.app --args <model>` and `request_access` for the new id. `app_screenshot`/`app_click` then work and include popup menus. A display-scope `left_click` on the header did NOT open the fork's PopupWindow menus, but a background `app_click` did; take the pixel-level `zoom` with the display tools afterwards (call `app_release` first). Display-scope `Escape` does not close those popups; a click elsewhere does.\n\nThe MCP discovery file `~/Library/Application Support/JusPrin2/jusprin/mcp.json` points at the newest instance's `http://127.0.0.1:<port>/mcp`; `tests/mcp/probe.py`'s `call()` can drive real tools (e.g. `workspace_inspect`, then `report_slice_review` with sessionId/plateId/sliceResultId) to put the header into the Check-print state without lldb. lldb `expr` cannot call inline accessors like `status_row()`.\n\n**Why:** On 2026-09-01 a verification pass screenshotted the stock app instead of the build; on 2026-09-05 the tools bound to another session's main-repo build.\n\n**How to apply:** Confirm the pid with `pgrep -fl OrcaSlicer.app/Contents/MacOS`; never kill an instance you did not launch. `osascript` System Events by unix id still works to set `frontmost`. See [[jusprin-shell-phase-1-design]] and [[orca-inherited-teardown-crash]].\n\n**\"On another Space\" usually means \"on the other monitor.\"** Cost about ten turns on\n2026-09-09 and produced a wrong report to Kenneth. `app_list_windows` returns\n`is_off_space: true` and clicks are refused with \"this window is on another Space\";\n`app_bring_to_current_space` then fails with \"the user's current Space is a full-screen\napp.\" Both messages are about Spaces, so the natural read is that the user is sitting in\na full-screen app — but with *Displays have separate Spaces* on, a window merely sitting\non the second monitor produces exactly the same symptoms. Kenneth was not in full screen;\nthe harness had opened on the Acer.\n\nTell them apart before saying anything to the user: take a **display-scope** screenshot\n(`app_release`, then `computer_batch` screenshot). Its header names the monitor it\ncaptured and lists the others — if the window shows up there, it is a monitor problem,\nnot a Space problem, and the display-scope tools can drive it immediately. Never conclude\n\"the user is in a full-screen app\" from the background tools' error text alone.\n\nThe same flag also flaps: a window can read `is_off_space: false` and click fine, then\nread `true` a minute later. Clicks delivered while it is true report `ok ... unverified`\nand silently do nothing. **A click that reports \"unverified\" and changes nothing is not\n57003 /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/build/arm64/src/RelWithDebInfo/OrcaSlicer.app/Contents/MacOS/jusprin-mcp --discovery /Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/JusPrin2/jusprin/mcp.json\n57165 /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/build/arm64/src/RelWithDebInfo/OrcaSlicer.app/Contents/MacOS/jusprin-mcp --discovery /Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/JusPrin2/jusprin/mcp.json\n57166 /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/build/arm64/src/RelWithDebInfo/OrcaSlicer.app/Contents/MacOS/jusprin-mcp --discovery /Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/JusPrin2/jusprin/mcp.json\n57677 /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/build/arm64/src/RelWithDebInfo/OrcaSlicer.app/Contents/MacOS/jusprin-mcp --discovery /Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/JusPrin2/jusprin/mcp.json\n57833 /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/build/arm64/src/RelWithDebInfo/OrcaSlicer.app/Contents/MacOS/jusprin-mcp --discovery /Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/JusPrin2/jusprin/mcp.json\n57987 /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/build/arm64/src/RelWithDebInfo/OrcaSlicer.app/Contents/MacOS/jusprin-mcp --discovery /Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/JusPrin2/jusprin/mcp.json\n58092 /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/build/arm64/src/RelWithDebInfo/OrcaSlicer.app/Contents/MacOS/jusprin-mcp --discovery /Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/JusPrin2/jusprin/mcp.json\n58199 /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/build/arm64/src/RelWithDebInfo/OrcaSlicer.app/Contents/MacOS/jusprin-mcp --discovery /Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/JusPrin2/jusprin/mcp.json\n58316 /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/build/arm64/src/RelWithDebInfo/OrcaSlicer.app/Contents/MacOS/jusprin-mcp --discovery /Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/JusPrin2/jusprin/mcp.json\n59138 /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/build/arm64/src/RelWithDebInfo/OrcaSlicer.app/Contents/MacOS/jusprin-mcp --discovery /Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/JusPrin2/jusprin/mcp.json","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"b6a4993a-4f55-411b-9851-822acbf386f2","timestamp":"2026-11-11T01:20:07.940Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"---\nname: ux-walkthrough-real-app-recipe\ndescription: \"How to drive the real built JusPrin app for a screenshot-per-step UX walkthrough (2026-10-28): scratch copies, the empty local_machines loop with the fake printer, why background app_* tools fail on Orca dialogs, and where screenshots land.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 33551592-d22c-4161-9a14-9a22ef798541\n  modified: 2026-10-28T13:12:42.393Z\n---\n\nOn 2026-10-28 I walked six scenarios (open-and-print, fix-a-problem) through the real app with Opus 5.5 and published the critique at https://claude.ai/artifact/XyVvteGiKhiJ6apUx8rcmR (34 frames, scratch copy at scratchpad/ux/ of that session). Kenneth's steer: start from files people actually download (MakerWorld 3MFs carry a full Bambu profile: printer, print preset, filaments, colours, bed type, designer, licence), not from generated STLs. `~/Downloads` has Tape_4_3MF.3mf (A1 mini profile), find_my_hollow.3mf (P1S, 3 colours, 233 mm wide, too big for an A1 mini), arrow_headband.3mf (P1S), general_purpose_hook.STL (bare).\n\n**Recipe that worked**\n- `ditto` the built .app out of `build/arm64/src/RelWithDebInfo/` into the scratchpad before launching (another session's ninja can relink it underneath you); the bundle id is already unique (`io.jusprin.JusPrin`), no re-sign needed.\n- `ditto` `~/Library/Application Support/JusPrin2` to a scratch `--datadir`; set `jusprin.fake_printer=true`, `presets.machine` to the saved \"Bambu Lab A1 mini 2\", write `jusprin/fake_printer.json`, delete `jusprin/mcp.json.lock`.\n- **Clear `local_machines`.** Kenneth's conf carries a `local_machines` entry keyed by the empty string (old Moonraker experiment). With the fake Bambu agent on, `init_networking_callbacks`' connect callback calls `DeviceManager::set_selected_machine(\"\")` in a loop (\"same lan machine, dev_id =, disconnect and reconnect\"), the main window disappears and the log grew 700 MB in two minutes. Clearing the map fixed it. The loop has no guard; see [[fake-bambu-printer-sim]] and [[harness-fake-printer-cleanup]].\n- Background `app_*` tools cannot press OrcaSlicer's custom `Button`s (no AX action) and the hit test at the dialog's screen position reports \"belongs to a different process\". `request_full_control` + `computer_batch` works for everything, including the Agent web view and the macOS file chooser (`cmd+shift+g`, type the path, Return, Return). Re-front the app with `open_application` when another session's harness steals focus.\n- Every `app_screenshot`/`computer_batch` screenshot is written as a JPEG under `~/.claude/projects/<project>/<session>/tool-results/mcp-computer-use-blob-*.jpg`; copy those for a report instead of fighting `screencapture`.\n- The dev build (-O0) slices a 38 mm part in over a minute; wait 45–60 s before judging a slice.\n\n**Why:** the first launch attempt looked like an app bug (blank window, title \"Couldn't save\") and cost ten minutes; the dialog-click refusals cost another ten.\n**How to apply:** reuse this for any \"walk through the app as a user\" request; keep scenarios on downloaded files; write the critique per step as what the person knows / sees / finds confusing. Related: [[live-test-built-app-on-mac]], [[drive-app-with-posted-key-events]].\n---\nname: scratch-app-driving-traps\ndescription: \"Seven traps met driving a scratch copy of the built app without screen control (2026-11-04): in-place binary copy gets SIGKILL, Home drops bridge messages while hidden, header popups need a posted NSEvent, lldb std::string args, wx Wrap reuse.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: reference\n  originSessionId: dea8379c-b02c-43a2-a254-4c2259672439\n  modified: 2026-11-04T18:59:38.548Z\n---\n\nMet while verifying print-host printer window fixes on the scratch `.app` (see [[live-test-built-app-on-mac]], [[open-file-in-app-without-screen-control]]).\n\n- **Copy a new build into a `.app` with `rm` then `cp`.** `cp` over the existing signed binary keeps the inode; the kernel kills the launch at once (exit 137, nothing logged).\n- **A launch from a plain Bash call dies when the call ends.** Start the app with `run_in_background: true` and `exec`.\n- **Home ignores bridge messages while the main window shows a project.** A queued `launch_monitor` through `JUSPRIN_HOME_DEV_URL` is sent by the page and silently dropped; switch to Home first (`m_tabpanel->SetSelection(0)` via lldb).\n- **Background `app_click` does not reach the header's popup menus** (they are not listed as windows). Post the click into the app's queue with lldb: `expr -l objc -- @import AppKit`, then `NSEvent mouseEventWithType:NSEventTypeLeftMouseDown/Up location:NSMakePoint(x, y-from-popup-bottom) ... windowNumber:[popup windowNumber]` and `[NSApp postEvent:atStart:NO]`. Render the popup with `cacheDisplayInRect:` on its contentView ([[capture-mac-popups-for-platform-diff]]).\n- **lldb cannot build `std::string` args.** This libc++ uses the alternate short-string layout: a 24-byte char array with the text at offset 0 and its length in byte 23 (≤ 22 chars), passed as `*(std::string*)buf`.\n- **wx `wxStaticText::Wrap()` (Orca's wx) skips a width it already wrapped at and keeps the first text it wrapped**, so SetLabel + Wrap on a reused label comes back unwrapped. Use a fresh label.\n- **With the screen locked, an instrumented dev page stops polling** (WebKit throttles the hidden page's timers; `document.visibilityState` is \"hidden\"). Run JS in it through lldb instead: walk `[NSApp windows]` → subviews to the `WKWebView` (match its title or `URL`), then `[webview evaluateJavaScript:@\"…\" completionHandler:nil]`; the page can `fetch()` results to the dev server. A menu item without a shortcut: `[[item target] performSelector:[item action] withObject:item afterDelay:0.5]` from lldb, so the modal it opens runs after detach.\n- **A locked screen slows the whole app 2-4×** (2026-11-05: the same first-launch OrcaSlicer import took 46 s unlocked at 15:48, 226 s locked at 19:22, same build and folder). Compare timings only between back-to-back runs under the same conditions, old and new builds side by side.\n---\nname: live-test-built-app-on-mac\ndescription: \"How to launch, see, and drive the locally built JusPrin app on the Mac: the shared bundle id binds tools to the wrong instance, and \\\"on another Space\\\" usually means the window is on the second monitor, not that the user is in full screen.\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: fa2d66ed-e217-440b-aae0-da4164953edc\n  modified: 2026-11-01T19:29:08.107Z\n---\n\nEvery build of the fork (and /Applications/OrcaSlicer.app) shares bundle id `com.softfever3d.orca-slicer`. The desktop-control tools resolve an app by bundle id and bind to whichever instance comes first, so `app_list_windows` returns `[]` and filtered screenshots hide the window you actually launched.\n\n**Working recipe (2026-09-05):** `ditto` the built .app into the scratchpad, `plutil -replace CFBundleIdentifier -string com.jusprin.worktree-test`, `codesign --force --deep -s -`, then `open -n <copy>.app --args <model>` and `request_access` for the new id. `app_screenshot`/`app_click` then work and include popup menus. A display-scope `left_click` on the header did NOT open the fork's PopupWindow menus, but a background `app_click` did; take the pixel-level `zoom` with the display tools afterwards (call `app_release` first). Display-scope `Escape` does not close those popups; a click elsewhere does.\n\nThe MCP discovery file `~/Library/Application Support/JusPrin2/jusprin/mcp.json` points at the newest instance's `http://127.0.0.1:<port>/mcp`; `tests/mcp/probe.py`'s `call()` can drive real tools (e.g. `workspace_inspect`, then `report_slice_review` with sessionId/plateId/sliceResultId) to put the header into the Check-print state without lldb. lldb `expr` cannot call inline accessors like `status_row()`.\n\n**Why:** On 2026-09-01 a verification pass screenshotted the stock app instead of the build; on 2026-09-05 the tools bound to another session's main-repo build.\n\n**How to apply:** Confirm the pid with `pgrep -fl OrcaSlicer.app/Contents/MacOS`; never kill an instance you did not launch. `osascript` System Events by unix id still works to set `frontmost`. See [[jusprin-shell-phase-1-design]] and [[orca-inherited-teardown-crash]].\n\n**\"On another Space\" usually means \"on the other monitor.\"** Cost about ten turns on\n2026-09-09 and produced a wrong report to Kenneth. `app_list_windows` returns\n`is_off_space: true` and clicks are refused with \"this window is on another Space\";\n`app_bring_to_current_space` then fails with \"the user's current Space is a full-screen\napp.\" Both messages are about Spaces, so the natural read is that the user is sitting in\na full-screen app — but with *Displays have separate Spaces* on, a window merely sitting\non the second monitor produces exactly the same symptoms. Kenneth was not in full screen;\nthe harness had opened on the Acer.\n\nTell them apart before saying anything to the user: take a **display-scope** screenshot\n(`app_release`, then `computer_batch` screenshot). Its header names the monitor it\ncaptured and lists the others — if the window shows up there, it is a monitor problem,\nnot a Space problem, and the display-scope tools can drive it immediately. Never conclude\n\"the user is in a full-screen app\" from the background tools' error text alone.\n\nThe same flag also flaps: a window can read `is_off_space: false` and click fine, then\nread `true` a minute later. Clicks delivered while it is true report `ok ... unverified`\nand silently do nothing. **A click that reports \"unverified\" and changes nothing is not\n57003 /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/build/arm64/src/RelWithDebInfo/OrcaSlicer.app/Contents/MacOS/jusprin-mcp --discovery /Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/JusPrin2/jusprin/mcp.