{"parentUuid":"c6ed6a96-32bb-49b5-8649-64c73b8589ea","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvGDL6L6MzFUN93XUbwJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Nothing was charged. The page you landed on is the server working as designed, because the purchase has to start from inside the JusPrin app.\n\n**What happened:** the prices page in your Chrome was signed out, which is why the buttons said \"Sign up to buy\". The server only lets someone buy after the app has signed them in and opened the page in its own window. Signed out, every button goes to the page you saw, \"You're all set. You can close this tab and go back to JusPrin.\" That page is meant to close the app's window, so in a plain browser it just sits there. I checked production: no Chargebee customer was created, and your account still has 488 credits.\n\n**Doing it from the app:** your usual app points at staging or your local server. So I started a copy of today's app (built at 4:59 PM from the development branch) with an empty settings folder. It talks to production and doesn't touch your own app's settings. It should be open on your screen as a new JusPrin window showing the first-run screens.\n1. Go through the first-run screens and sign in as k@obico.io. Google sign-in now uses JusPrin's own Google app.\n2. Open Credits and plans, for example from the \"Get more credits\" link next to the message box.\n3. Buy the **Credit pack** ($10) with a real card.\n\nAfter that, your account should show 1,488 credits. Tell me when you've paid, and I'll check the credits, the Chargebee invoice and the Stripe charge."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":640,"cache_read_input_tokens":274211,"output_tokens":453,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cach