{"parentUuid":"5a628f8c-78e7-4efa-a00b-21bf531d5560","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[{"name":"mcp__ccd_session__start_session","description":"Start a separate Claude Code session for a task while you stay with the user (when: see \"Starting other sessions\"). `initiation` says who wants it: \"user_asked\" starts it now and returns its id; \"offer\" is for a task the user named in their latest message (new work here, or \"suggest / split off / make a task or session for X\"): called with a title alone, it shows a \"New session\" / \"Do it here\" card and WAITS for their answer, so it must be the only call in that message (no update_plan, no other tool); the result then tells you to carry on here, or to send the brief with proposal_id so the session starts; \"own_initiative\" is for work you propose yourself that the user has not told you to do — something you noticed, or the follow-up your own answer or work turned up (when your reply calls work a follow-up or a separate PR, propose it here rather than only saying so, unless it acts on what this session just found and so stays here), never what \"Starting other sessions\" keeps here or gives to a subagent; the user sees a card and nothing runs until they start it, by clicking it or by telling you (then call this again with just proposal_id; for the cloud, see proposal_id).\n\"user_asked\" and \"own_initiative\" both need a `prompt` — the brief: the task, the files or area, what done looks like — and the call is refused without it; `background` does not stand in for it. Only an \"offer\" is a title alone.\ncontext: \"fork\" = this whole conversation + your `prompt`. \"fresh\" (default) = your `prompt` + `background` only, so `background` is required too, at least 80 characters.\nCheckout here (\"fresh\" only): use_worktree false = shares this checkout and can edit it (in a worktree session its branch and PR too: never for work that ends in a branch or PR of its own or belongs in another repository); true = its own worktree (the default when this session is in one).\nElsewhere (\"fresh\", user_asked only, when the user named the place): `cwd`, `target` \"ssh\" + `host`, `environment` or `preset`; list_start_targets lists the valid names.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"initiation":{"type":"string","enum":["user_asked","own_initiative","offer"],"description":"\"user_asked\": the user asked in words for separate, parallel or background work, or told you to start this piece — it starts now (not for a piece \"Starting other sessions\" gives to a subagent). \"offer\": a task the user named in their latest message (new work for this session, or one they asked you to suggest, split off or make a session for) — the user is asked first and the call waits for their answer; send only title with it (the brief follows, with proposal_id, if they choose New session). \"own_initiative\": work you propose yourself that the user has not told you to do — something you noticed, or the follow-up your own answer or work turned up; it waits as a proposal card until the user starts it; never for a task the user's message tells you to do, nor for the one piece of work \"Starting other sessions\" keeps here, nor for what it gives to a subagent. Required unless proposal_id is set."},"proposal_id":{"description":"Start a proposal the user told you to start, exactly as proposed: its task_id and nothing else (wake_when_done may accompany a local one). To change it, or if you proposed it for the cloud, dismiss_task it and start a new session.","type":"string"},"title":{"description":"Under 60 chars; names the task. Shown on the row or card. Required unless proposal_id is set.","type":"string"},"prompt":{"description":"The brief: the task, the files or area, what done looks like. Required for \"user_asked\" and \"own_initiative\" — the call is refused without it, and `background` does not stand in for it; an \"offer\" leaves it out (the card shows the user's own message) and you send it with proposal_id once they choose New session. Here and in `background`, put file paths and code identifiers in backticks.","type":"string"},"context":{"type":"string","enum":["fresh","fork"],"description":"\"fresh\" (default) or \"fork\" — see the tool description. A \"fork\" from a worktree session gets a fresh worktree, normally cut from your branch tip (commit first; uncommitted edits stay here); from a plain checkout it shares the folder."},"background":{"description":"Required with \"fresh\", besides `prompt`: at least 80 characters of overall goal, decisions and constraints so far, how this piece fits — for someone who has not seen this conversation. Ignored for \"fork\".","type":"string"},"wake_when_done":{"description":"Once this session (and any sibling still working) ends its turn, or fails to start (unless it waits at a prompt the user answers there, its folder was never opened in Claude Desktop, or the user started, stopped or archived it), and you are idle, the app continues you, whether or not this is set. true also continues you if this session never gets its task some other way, such as a brief that is not sent; default false; not with own_initiative; ignored with target \"cloud\", which never continues you.","type":"boolean"},"name":{"description":"Optional short handle for the session ([a-z0-9-], ≤24), e.g. \"cli-cleanup\". Linked sessions and plan steps refer to it by this name; derived from the title when omitted.","type":"string"},"use_worktree":{"description":"\"fresh\" only (rejected with \"fork\"). false = shares this session's checkout and can edit it (in a worktree session: its worktree, branch and PR, so never for work that ends in a branch or PR of its own or belongs in another repository); not accepted from a session set up to move from the user's checkout into a worktree with EnterWorktree (before or after it moves), a fork of a session working in a worktree on an SSH host, or one whose worktree was given back. At another place named by `cwd`, `host` or `preset`, false = that folder as it is. true = its own git worktree. Omitted: the same folder when this session works in a plain folder and has never had a worktree (its own, a shared one, or one it will enter later); otherwise its own worktree. Omitted with `preset` or `host`, or with `cwd` from a session on an SSH host: the default set on that preset or SSH connection instead.","type":"boolean"},"model":{"description":"\"fresh\" only, optional: a cheaper model id for mechanical or read-only pieces (e.g. a Sonnet or Haiku id). Same family or cheaper than yours; anything higher is ignored. Omit to inherit yours.","type":"string"},"target":{"type":"string","enum":["local","cloud","ssh"],"description":"\"fresh\" only. \"local\" (default) = where this session runs. \"cloud\" = run it as a cloud session (keeps going when this computer sleeps). Needs the repository on GitHub and a cloud environment — the app checks and tells the user if it cannot, and the task then stays as a card for them to start. model/effort/use_worktree/cwd/source_branch do not apply. Only when the user asks for the cloud. \"ssh\" = on the SSH connection named by host (or by a preset)."},"host":{"description":"With target \"ssh\": the name of one of the user's saved SSH connections (as list_start_targets reports it) — never a raw hostname, user or key. The app connects as the user configured it and may ask them to sign in.","type":"string"},"cwd":{"description":"The folder the session works in, when it is not this project: an absolute (or ~/) path on the host it will run on — this computer, this session's host, or the SSH connection named by host (default there: the connection's folder). \"fresh\" only.","type":"string"},"environment":{"description":"With target \"cloud\": the name or id of one of the user's cloud environments (list_start_targets lists them); omitted = the default one.","type":"string"},"repository":{"description":"With target \"cloud\", only when the user named a repository other than this project's: \"owner/name\" on github.com, which the cloud session clones at its default branch. Take the exact owner/name from the user's words or a listing that shows it; if you are not sure of it, ask them. A bypass or auto permission mode may not carry over: the session then starts in the cloud's default mode. If the call is refused, do not run or propose the other repository's work in this project.","type":"string"},"source_branch":{"description":"The existing local branch the new worktree is cut from. Default in this project: this session's base branch (the one picked when it started, or the one its worktree was cut from). If the session has none and either it runs on an SSH host or its project folder is itself a git worktree or submodule, the folder's current commit. Otherwise, the repository's default branch, or the folder's current commit if that is unknown. Only for a session that gets its own worktree (use_worktree true, or the place's default); not with target \"cloud\".","type":"string"},"branch_name":{"description":"A short slug for the new worktree's branch (the app adds the user's branch prefix and a suffix). Only with a worktree.","type":"string"},"preset":{"description":"The name of one of the user's saved session presets on this computer: it names the place itself (a folder here or an SSH connection and folder — do not pass host or cwd with it) and brings model, effort and worktree defaults plus its saved environment variables; use_worktree/model/effort override those. Cloud and Remote Control presets are not available here.","type":"string"},"effort":{"type":"string","enum":["low","medium","high","xhigh","max"],"description":"\"fresh\" only, optional: reasoning effort at or below yours. Omit to inherit."},"permission_mode":{"type":"string","enum":["default","acceptEdits","plan","auto","bypassPermissions"],"description":"Optional, local starts only: the permission mode it starts in — this session's own or a lower one (omit to inherit it). A higher mode, or one the app does not offer here, is refused; raising a session is set_session_permission_mode's card to show."}},"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#"},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"df82be44-1809-43a1-abb6-bcf2a0c6dbd4","timestamp":"2026-11-11T01:32:27.999Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"jusprin-dev","slug":"rosy-bubbling-whisper"}
{"type":"tools-used","tools":["Bash","Edit","Read","SendMessage","Skill","ToolSearch","WebFetch","WebSearch","Write","mcp__Claude_Browser__computer","mcp__Claude_Browser__get_page_text","mcp__Claude_Browser__navigate","mcp__Claude_Browser__preview_list","mcp__Claude_Browser__preview_start","mcp__Claude_Browser__preview_stop","mcp__Claude_Browser__tabs_context","mcp__ccd_turn__update_plan","mcp__ccd_turn__wrap_up","mcp__claude-in-chrome__browser_batch","mcp__claude-in-chrome__computer","mcp__claude-in-chrome__file_upload","mcp__claude-in-chrome__find","mcp__claude-in-chrome__get_page_text","mcp__claude-in-chrome__javascript_tool","mcp__claude-in-chrome__navigate","mcp__claude-in-chrome__read_console_messages","mcp__claude-in-chrome__read_page","mcp__claude-in-chrome__tabs_close_mcp","mcp__claude-in-chrome__tabs_context_mcp","mcp__claude-in-chrome__tabs_create_mcp","mcp__ccd_session_mgmt__list_sessions","mcp__ccd_session_mgmt__send_message","CrossSessionMessage","mcp__ccd_session__start_session"],"sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79"}
{"parentUuid":"df82be44-1809-43a1-abb6-bcf2a0c6dbd4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvH5qDBjAVtgd4RRni2s","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018utoSHYkZ8UfKDGnWiTpyp","name":"mcp__ccd_session__start_session","input":{"initiation":"own_initiative","title":"PayPal checkout fails inside the app's Credits sheet","name":"paypal-in-server-sheet","context":"fresh","use_worktree":true,"prompt":"Fix PayPal in the JusPrin app's server sheet (Credits and plans). Reproduced live by Kenneth on 2026-11-10 against production: in the sheet, Chargebee's hosted checkout for the $10 credit pack, choosing PayPal and pressing the PayPal button shows Chargebee's overlay \"Complete your payment in the open PayPal window, or close PayPal to continue paying another way\", and the payment can't be finished in the app. Cause (from code, verify): `src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Shell/ServerSheet.cpp` binds `wxEVT_WEBVIEW_NEWWINDOW` to `wxLaunchDefaultBrowser(event.GetURL())`, so PayPal's popup opens in the person's browser with no `window.opener` link back to the checkout page, and the checkout never hears that PayPal approved. The bundled wx (deps/build/arm64/.../include/wx/webview.h) has `wxWebViewWindowFeatures` and `wxEVT_WEBVIEW_NEWWINDOW_FEATURES`, so a popup can be hosted in a child web view that keeps the opener. Likely fix: for pop-ups the checkout opens (PayPal), host them in a small app-owned window with a child web view instead of the browser; keep plain links going to the browser. Check behaviour on macOS, Windows (WebView2) and Linux (WebKitGTK) per AGENTS.md cross-platform rule; read `agent-docs/jusprin/design-system.md` before any UI. Reproduce first (Bug Fix Policy): the staging Chargebee test site jusprinv2-test has no PayPal gateway, so reproduce against production with Kenneth, or connect PayPal sandbox to the test site if Kenneth agrees. Done = PayPal checkout completes inside the sheet on macOS, verified, with a PR to jusprin-dev.","background":"JusPrin 2 sells credit packs and plans through Chargebee hosted checkout pages, shown inside the app's ServerSheet (a wxWebView sheet over the main window) which the server signs in through POST /ent/jusprin/v2/web_link. The live Chargebee site jusprinv2 went live on production 2026-11-10 with Stripe for cards and PayPal (TSD Technology LLC's account) for PayPal. The sheet's 'Open in browser' header button already opens the same page in the person's browser as a workaround. Separately, PayPal declined TSD's application to save PayPal payment methods, so PayPal plans (recurring) may not work regardless; one-time packs are the case to fix here."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3790,"cache_read_input_tokens":282388,"output_tokens":1371,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3790,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1371,"cache_read_input_tokens":282388,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3790,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3790},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":10125,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_018utoSHYkZ8UfKDGnWiTpyp":{"initiation":"own_initiative","title":"PayPal checkout fails inside the app's Credits sheet","name":"paypal-in-server-sheet","context":"fresh","use_worktree":true,"prompt":"Fix PayPal in the JusPrin app's server sheet (Credits and plans). Reproduced live by Kenneth on 2026-11-10 against production: in the sheet, Chargebee's hosted checkout for the $10 credit pack, choosing PayPal and pressing the PayPal button shows Chargebee's overlay \"Complete your payment in the open PayPal window, or close PayPal to continue paying another way\", and the payment can't be finished in the app. Cause (from code, verify): `src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Shell/ServerSheet.cpp` binds `wxEVT_WEBVIEW_NEWWINDOW` to `wxLaunchDefaultBrowser(event.GetURL())`, so PayPal's popup opens in the person's browser with no `window.opener` link back to the checkout page, and the checkout never hears that PayPal approved. The bundled wx (deps/build/arm64/.../include/wx/webview.h) has `wxWebViewWindowFeatures` and `wxEVT_WEBVIEW_NEWWINDOW_FEATURES`, so a popup can be hosted in a child web view that keeps the opener. Likely fix: for pop-ups the checkout opens (PayPal), host them in a small app-owned window with a child web view instead of the browser; keep plain links going to the browser. Check behaviour on macOS, Windows (WebView2) and Linux (WebKitGTK) per AGENTS.md cross-platform rule; read `agent-docs/jusprin/design-system.md` before any UI. Reproduce first (Bug Fix Policy): the staging Chargebee test site jusprinv2-test has no PayPal gateway, so reproduce against production with Kenneth, or connect PayPal sandbox to the test site if Kenneth agrees. Done = PayPal checkout completes inside the sheet on macOS, verified, with a PR to jusprin-dev.","background":"JusPrin 2 sells credit packs and plans through Chargebee hosted checkout pages, shown inside the app's ServerSheet (a wxWebView sheet over the main window) which the server signs in through POST /ent/jusprin/v2/web_link. The live Chargebee site jusprinv2 went live on production 2026-11-10 with Stripe for cards and PayPal (TSD Technology LLC's account) for PayPal. The sheet's 'Open in browser' header button already opens the same page in the person's browser as a workaround. Separately, PayPal declined TSD's application to save PayPal payment methods, so PayPal plans (recurring) may not work regardless; one-time packs are the case to fix here."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"a739824c-bb0e-4ec3-ab86-428cfb07be30","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgvH5pHsXtABndUGBDABm","requestRef":"09ecf2e1-26b9-45ca-b982-429073d3852b","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"11774b0d-854e-4468-ab6c-6ca116d415a7","timestamp":"2026-11-11T01:32:27.998Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"jusprin-dev","slug":"rosy-bubbling-whisper"}
{"parentUuid":"11774b0d-854e-4468-ab6c-6ca116d415a7","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"f659d12d-d392-458d-ba29-d2e7fca4a105","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018utoSHYkZ8UfKDGnWiTpyp","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Proposed \"PayPal checkout fails inside the app's Credits sheet\" (task_id: task_b17907ff). The user sees a card and nothing runs until they start it — with a click, or by telling you (then call start_session with proposal_id task_b17907ff and nothing else). It expires in 7 days unless started; dismiss_task withdraws it sooner if it goes stale. Don't wait for it and don't repeat the introduction; carry on with what you were doing."}]}]},"uuid":"8edfee0f-84cd-4693-9d69-50ef4b84e0d8","timestamp":"2026-11-11T01:32:28.048Z","toolUseResult":[{"type":"text","text":"Proposed \"PayPal checkout fails inside the app's Credits sheet\" (task_id: task_b17907ff). The user sees a card and nothing runs until they start it — with a click, or by telling you (then call start_session with proposal_id task_b17907ff and nothing else). It expires in 7 days unless started; dismiss_task withdraws it sooner if it goes stale. Don't wait for it and don't repeat the introduction; carry on with what you were doing."}],"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"11774b0d-854e-4468-ab6c-6ca116d415a7","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_temporary","ruleSource":"mcpServerPolicy","grantScope":"once","reasonCode":"rule:mcpServerPolicy"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"jusprin-dev","slug":"rosy-bubbling-whisper"}
{"parentUuid":"8edfee0f-84cd-4693-9d69-50ef4b84e0d8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvH5qDBjAVtgd4RRni2s","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018ViT3eRN8DHuGodehk7jLz","name":"mcp__ccd_turn__wrap_up","input":{"recap":"PayPal can't finish inside the app's Credits sheet: the app sends PayPal's pop-up to your browser, where it loses its link back to the checkout. Nothing was charged. A fix is proposed as its own task; the purchase can go ahead through the sheet's \"Open in browser\" button.","ask":"Have you bought the credit pack after clicking \"Open in browser\"?","actions":[{"label":"Bought it"},{"label":"Something went wrong"}],"blocked":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3790,"cache_read_input_tokens":282388,"output_tokens":1371,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3790,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1371,"cache_read_input_tokens":282388,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3790,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3790},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":1626,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_018ViT3eRN8DHuGodehk7jLz":{"recap":"PayPal can't finish inside the app's Credits sheet: the app sends PayPal's pop-up to your browser, where it loses its link back to the checkout. Nothing was charged. A fix is proposed as its own task; the purchase can go ahead through the sheet's \"Open in browser\" button.","ask":"Have you bought the credit pack after clicking \"Open in browser\"?","actions":[{"label":"Bought it"},{"label":"Something went wrong"}],"blocked":true}},"serverClassifierRequest":"a739824c-bb0e-4ec3-ab86-428cfb07be30","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgvH5pHsXtABndUGBDABm","requestRef":"09ecf2e1-26b9-45ca-b982-429073d3852b","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"6200f7d2-7e85-4acc-bce3-b18d21789597","timestamp":"2026-11-11T01:32:29.631Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"jusprin-dev","slug":"rosy-bubbling-whisper"}
{"parentUuid":"6200f7d2-7e85-4acc-bce3-b18d21789597","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"f659d12d-d392-458d-ba29-d2e7fca4a105","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018ViT3eRN8DHuGodehk7jLz","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Shown in the next-step box. Your closing message is your answer to the user: write it now, in full, as the last thing you say this turn. The box asks your question, so do not ask it again."}]}]},"uuid":"0cc799c5-883d-4980-800a-a2c6f3115e65","timestamp":"2026-11-11T01:32:29.655Z","toolUseResult":[{"type":"text","text":"Shown in the next-step box. Your closing message is your answer to the user: write it now, in full, as the last thing you say this turn. The box asks your question, so do not ask it again."}],"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6200f7d2-7e85-4acc-bce3-b18d21789597","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"jusprin-dev","slug":"rosy-bubbling-whisper"}
{"parentUuid":"0cc799c5-883d-4980-800a-a2c6f3115e65","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"silent_turn_reminder","text":"The user hasn't heard from you in a while — say in a few words what you're doing, then continue."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d884f7e5-6f97-4a7f-b4cd-c6f9b6fc31d3","timestamp":"2026-11-11T01:32:29.659Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nThe user hasn't heard from you in a while — say in a few words what you're doing, then continue.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"jusprin-dev","slug":"rosy-bubbling-whisper"}
{"parentUuid":"d884f7e5-6f97-4a7f-b4cd-c6f9b6fc31d3","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"output_style","style":"Plain"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"6dc448d0-97c3-4bd0-9475-d8b51aa3bc33","timestamp":"2026-11-11T01:32:29.659Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nPlain output style is active. Remember to follow the specific guidelines for this style.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"jusprin-dev","slug":"rosy-bubbling-whisper"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","hash":"0960a262cdf091b4a2edacd770190e342c09a47b61877f344e6821e68daef241","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018utoSHYkZ8UfKDGnWiTpyp","name":"mcp__ccd_session__start_session","input":{"initiation":"own_initiative","title":"PayPal checkout fails inside the app's Credits sheet","name":"paypal-in-server-sheet","context":"fresh","use_worktree":true,"prompt":"Fix PayPal in the JusPrin app's server sheet (Credits and plans). Reproduced live by Kenneth on 2026-11-10 against production: in the sheet, Chargebee's hosted checkout for the $10 credit pack, choosing PayPal and pressing the PayPal button shows Chargebee's overlay \"Complete your payment in the open PayPal window, or close PayPal to continue paying another way\", and the payment can't be finished in the app. Cause (from code, verify): `src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Shell/ServerSheet.cpp` binds `wxEVT_WEBVIEW_NEWWINDOW` to `wxLaunchDefaultBrowser(event.GetURL())`, so PayPal's popup opens in the person's browser with no `window.opener` link back to the checkout page, and the checkout never hears that PayPal approved. The bundled wx (deps/build/arm64/.../include/wx/webview.h) has `wxWebViewWindowFeatures` and `wxEVT_WEBVIEW_NEWWINDOW_FEATURES`, so a popup can be hosted in a child web view that keeps the opener. Likely fix: for pop-ups the checkout opens (PayPal), host them in a small app-owned window with a child web view instead of the browser; keep plain links going to the browser. Check behaviour on macOS, Windows (WebView2) and Linux (WebKitGTK) per AGENTS.md cross-platform rule; read `agent-docs/jusprin/design-system.md` before any UI. Reproduce first (Bug Fix Policy): the staging Chargebee test site jusprinv2-test has no PayPal gateway, so reproduce against production with Kenneth, or connect PayPal sandbox to the test site if Kenneth agrees. Done = PayPal checkout completes inside the sheet on macOS, verified, with a PR to jusprin-dev.","background":"JusPrin 2 sells credit packs and plans through Chargebee hosted checkout pages, shown inside the app's ServerSheet (a wxWebView sheet over the main window) which the server signs in through POST /ent/jusprin/v2/web_link. The live Chargebee site jusprinv2 went live on production 2026-11-10 with Stripe for cards and PayPal (TSD Technology LLC's account) for PayPal. The sheet's 'Open in browser' header button already opens the same page in the person's browser as a workaround. Separately, PayPal declined TSD's application to save PayPal payment methods, so PayPal plans (recurring) may not work regardless; one-time packs are the case to fix here."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018ViT3eRN8DHuGodehk7jLz","name":"mcp__ccd_turn__wrap_up","input":{"recap":"PayPal can't finish inside the app's Credits sheet: the app sends PayPal's pop-up to your browser, where it loses its link back to the checkout. Nothing was charged. A fix is proposed as its own task; the purchase can go ahead through the sheet's \"Open in browser\" button.","ask":"Have you bought the credit pack after clicking \"Open in browser\"?","actions":[{"label":"Bought it"},{"label":"Something went wrong"}],"blocked":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","hash":"5eeca060b4052b309bac5688ccfbd95b318faf6aad36cc2615d8e4efedf5c5de","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018utoSHYkZ8UfKDGnWiTpyp","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Proposed \"PayPal checkout fails inside the app's Credits sheet\" (task_id: task_b17907ff). The user sees a card and nothing runs until they start it — with a click, or by telling you (then call start_session with proposal_id task_b17907ff and nothing else). It expires in 7 days unless started; dismiss_task withdraws it sooner if it goes stale. Don't wait for it and don't repeat the introduction; carry on with what you were doing."}]},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018ViT3eRN8DHuGodehk7jLz","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Shown in the next-step box. Your closing message is your answer to the user: write it now, in full, as the last thing you say this turn. The box asks your question, so do not ask it again."}]}]}}
