{"parentUuid":"a3a2ecad-3ffd-418d-811b-320ec26bdcac","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvHxySxmgvn3M4a1iK7r","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Kepacpf4cgxP7uXtpWRgAi","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"local_3e38de32-e8df-4f8c-b26d-1a20db4c0aca","summary":"Answer release-coordination questions","message":"Release coordination for tsd-enterprise master (43840b75e3 yearly plans + a6745635ed moved-customer warning): nothing blocks it from my side.\n1. Live jusprinv2 already has them, read just now by API: jusprin-hobby-yearly $100/1 year, jusprin-workshop-yearly $200/1 year, coupon jusprin1-move-first-term (100% one_time, hobby-yearly only), and jusprin2-obico-premium-20 covers all four plan prices. All were created 2026-11-10 17:29 Pacific, not by me (likely the JusPrin 1 users session); confirm with it that Kenneth's yes covered the live site. Nothing missing that master's settings_ent.py names.\n2. Nothing of mine is unreleased or uncommitted in tsd-enterprise: my only commit since obi.4104's source is 52d1bd7974 (docs only); my worktree is clean. Ops: 5 local unpushed commits on master, all already applied to the cluster except none pending; a0b8fc7 is production obi.4104 + JUSPRIN_V2_CHARGEBEE_SITE/API_KEY (applied). For the next release: tsdweb-prod's initContainer runs migrate (so migration 0004 runs there); roll tsdws-prod with `kubectl set image`, not apply, because the file says 12 replicas and production runs 10 on purpose. Env vars and the live webhook (https://app.obico.io/ent/jusprin/v2/cb_webhook, checked) are already in place; a release needs only the image tag.\n3. Live Chargebee still open, none blocking the release: (a) the real-money purchase test is in progress with Kenneth right now; (b) PayPal declined TSD's \"save PayPal payment methods\" application, so PayPal for plans (monthly or yearly) likely fails, untested; one-time packs expected to work; (c) PayPal can't complete inside the app's Credits sheet because ServerSheet sends the pop-up to the browser (proposed as its own task; \"Open in browser\" works around it); (d) all automatic Chargebee emails, receipts included, are off on live and test; Kenneth hasn't decided whether to turn receipts on.","type":"message","recipient":"local_3e38de32-e8df-4f8c-b26d-1a20db4c0aca","recipient_kind":"session","content":"Release coordination for tsd-enterprise master (4…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":657,"cache_read_input_tokens":299353,"output_tokens":1472,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":364},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":657,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1472,"cache_read_input_tokens":299353,"cache_creation_input_tokens":657,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":657},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":8412,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Kepacpf4cgxP7uXtpWRgAi":{"to":"local_3e38de32-e8df-4f8c-b26d-1a20db4c0aca","summary":"Answer release-coordination questions","message":"Release coordination for tsd-enterprise master (43840b75e3 yearly plans + a6745635ed moved-customer warning): nothing blocks it from my side.\n1. Live jusprinv2 already has them, read just now by API: jusprin-hobby-yearly $100/1 year, jusprin-workshop-yearly $200/1 year, coupon jusprin1-move-first-term (100% one_time, hobby-yearly only), and jusprin2-obico-premium-20 covers all four plan prices. All were created 2026-11-10 17:29 Pacific, not by me (likely the JusPrin 1 users session); confirm with it that Kenneth's yes covered the live site. Nothing missing that master's settings_ent.py names.\n2. Nothing of mine is unreleased or uncommitted in tsd-enterprise: my only commit since obi.4104's source is 52d1bd7974 (docs only); my worktree is clean. Ops: 5 local unpushed commits on master, all already applied to the cluster except none pending; a0b8fc7 is production obi.4104 + JUSPRIN_V2_CHARGEBEE_SITE/API_KEY (applied). For the next release: tsdweb-prod's initContainer runs migrate (so migration 0004 runs there); roll tsdws-prod with `kubectl set image`, not apply, because the file says 12 replicas and production runs 10 on purpose. Env vars and the live webhook (https://app.obico.io/ent/jusprin/v2/cb_webhook, checked) are already in place; a release needs only the image tag.\n3. Live Chargebee still open, none blocking the release: (a) the real-money purchase test is in progress with Kenneth right now; (b) PayPal declined TSD's \"save PayPal payment methods\" application, so PayPal for plans (monthly or yearly) likely fails, untested; one-time packs expected to work; (c) PayPal can't complete inside the app's Credits sheet because ServerSheet sends the pop-up to the browser (proposed as its own task; \"Open in browser\" works around it); (d) all automatic Chargebee emails, receipts included, are off on live and test; Kenneth hasn't decided whether to turn receipts on."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"1b9920aa-950b-4eb4-b5c9-a8f18faab8fe","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgvHxyCZq2LcpSBDH2Z1q","requestRef":"dabd0942-a2f8-4903-b03b-0b9fb5458367","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"047624b2-73bc-498a-8029-24b8b8b484fb","timestamp":"2026-11-11T01:44:04.525Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/tsd-enterprise-worktrees/jusprin-v2-own-chargebee","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"jusprin-