{"parentUuid":"bd3af1d2-c083-45fc-ad63-e8f8d970527c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvHz7mnugAh4YPJKGeuc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1799,"cache_read_input_tokens":300010,"output_tokens":701,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":110},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1799,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":701,"cache_read_input_tokens":300010,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1799,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1799},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":7142,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"a1cb1bf2-0737-4ddf-98f0-cd94c9764b7f","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgvHz7WRSTxsfrHtFhxC7","requestRef":"10fd00f0-c31b-4c8f-b20c-9f808dfb48da","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"0322cc76-26d4-4f7d-867a-1d728689b666","timestamp":"2026-11-11T01:44:16.128Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/tsd-enterprise-worktrees/jusprin-v2-own-chargebee","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"jusprin-dev","slug":"rosy-bubbling-whisper"}
{"parentUuid":"0322cc76-26d4-4f7d-867a-1d728689b666","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvHz7mnugAh4YPJKGeuc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Nothing on my side needs coordinating for the next production release. I've answered the rollout session, [Just Print V2 rollout plan](#local_3e38de32-e8df-4f8c-b26d-1a20db4c0aca), which asked on your behalf.\n\n**Prices for the next release:** the live Chargebee site already has everything it needs, which I checked through its API. That's the yearly Hobby ($100) and Workshop ($200) prices, the first-year coupon for people moving from JusPrin 1, and the 20% Obico Premium discount extended to the yearly prices. They were added at 5:29 PM today, not by me. Most likely the session planning JusPrin 1 users' move added them. The rollout session should confirm your yes covered the live site, since that session earlier said it had changed only the test site.\n\n**My code:** none of it is waiting. My only commit since the deployed version only changes a doc, and my working folder has no uncommitted changes. The production settings and the live webhook are already in place, so the next release only needs the new version number.\n\n**Two notes I passed on for whoever deploys it:**\n- The next release includes a database change. Production runs database changes automatically when the web servers update, so nothing extra is needed.\n- The websocket servers should be updated with the command that changes only their version (`kubectl set image`). Applying their ops file would raise them from 10 copies back to 12.\n\n**Still open on the live Chargebee site, none of it blocking the release:**\n- Your test purchase.\n- PayPal plans probably won't work, because PayPal turned down saving customers' PayPal accounts. I haven't tested it.\n- PayPal can't finish inside the app's Credits window. That's the separate task I proposed.\n- All automatic Chargebee emails are off, receipts included. You haven't said whether to turn receipts on."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1799,"cache_read_input_tokens":300010,"output_tokens":701,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":110},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1799,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":701,"cache_read_input_tokens":300010,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1799,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1799},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"a1cb1bf2-0737-4ddf-98f0-cd94c9764b7f","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgvHz7WRSTxsfrHtFhxC7","requestRef":"10fd00f0-c31b-4c8f-b20c-9f808dfb48da","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"77c23742-d525-4c8d-8153-84e55f65ab0f","timestamp":"2026-11-11T01:44:16.138Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/tsd-enterprise-worktrees/jusprin-v2-own-chargebee","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"jusprin-dev","slug":"rosy-bubbling-whisper"}
{"parentUuid":"77c23742-d525-4c8d-8153-84e55f65ab0f","isSidechain":false,"type":"system","subtype":"stop_hook_summary","hookCount":4,"hookInfos":[{"command":"sh -c 'if ! command -v entire >/dev/null 2>&1; then exit 0; fi; exec entire hooks claude-code stop'","durationMs":64},{"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-stop.sh","durationMs":16},{"command":"callback"},{"command":"callback"}],"hookErrors":[],"hookAdditionalContext":[],"preventedContinuation":false,"stopReason":"","hasOutput":false,"level":"suggestion","timestamp":"2026-11-11T01:44:18.744Z","uuid":"c529dfd2-3df5-48a8-b4bb-451b0c7a4204","toolUseID":"d16fd5e7-9fdc-4dd0-b3ae-4a62315fcb90","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/tsd-enterprise-worktrees/jusprin-v2-own-chargebee","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"jusprin-dev","slug":"rosy-bubbling-whisper"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-11T01:44:18.794Z","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","content":"<cross-session-message from=\"local_92607d89-53ce-49de-b66c-6c7f1e5b7f3f\" from-name=\"PayPal checkout fails inside the app's Credits sheet\">\nPayPal fix: to reproduce and verify on production I need Kenneth for about 10 minutes, once my build finishes (roughly 45 min). Please ask him two things. (1) I'll launch a test copy of the app with its own data folder; only he can sign it in to production (Google sign-in as k@obico.io), since I can't enter passwords. Is he willing? (2) Pressing PayPal in the $10 pack checkout costs nothing; it shows whether PayPal's window opens inside the app. Should the check stop when PayPal's login page shows in the app's window (no money moves), or go on to a real $10 PayPal payment that he approves himself and refunds afterwards in Chargebee, which is the only way to prove the checkout finishes? My pick: go all the way, since \"checkout completes\" is the done criterion. Meanwhile I'm verifying the mechanism with an automated test against a local stand-in checkout page.\n</cross-session-message>"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"dequeue","timestamp":"2026-11-11T01:44:18.795Z","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79"}
