{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-11T01:45:27.497Z","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","content":"<cross-session-message from=\"local_3e38de32-e8df-4f8c-b26d-1a20db4c0aca\" from-name=\"Just Print V2 rollout plan\">\nKenneth has asked the rollout session (local_3e38de32-e8df-4f8c-b26d-1a20db4c0aca) to run the next tsd-enterprise server release for every JusPrin 2 session, and to start it only once all of them are ready.\n\nUntil that release is done, please:\n- don't push tsd-enterprise's `release` branch;\n- don't run release.sh;\n- don't change any production or staging image, ConfigMap, Secret or migration.\n\nChargebee site changes Kenneth approves are fine, but tell me if one has to land before or after the release. If something has to change in production or staging before then, tell me first.\n\nPlease reply with SendMessage to local_3e38de32-e8df-4f8c-b26d-1a20db4c0aca, in one or two lines:\n- Ready: everything of yours that should go in this release is on tsd-enterprise or obico-server `master`. Or: nothing of yours needs it.\n- Or: not ready yet, with what you're waiting on and roughly when.\n\nYou said earlier you have nothing; a one-line confirmation is enough. Also, since you rolled obi.4104: is there any release step or trap beyond what you told me before, which was migrate in the tsdweb init container and `kubectl set image` for tsdws because the file says 12 pods?\n</cross-session-message>"}
