{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","hash":"6b3d37cef231f3a7192e5e31c1617926ff50379a46553870dbf5c6662acc6b26","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015xJ2srPVNtLewSqKkJF5gS","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"local_3e38de32-e8df-4f8c-b26d-1a20db4c0aca","summary":"Confirm ready; list release traps","message":"Ready: nothing of mine needs this release, and I'll leave release, images, ConfigMaps, Secrets and migrations alone. Traps beyond the two I gave: (1) apply only the changed tsd/prod files, never `kubectl apply -f tsd/prod/` — the folder has a flower-prod deployment that isn't running in the cluster and would be created; (2) `kubectl diff` on tsdtasks-prod shows JUSPRIN_V2_CAPTURE_CONTAINER moving position, a harmless reorder; (3) I didn't run release.sh for obi.4104 — I reused staging's image after checking its web_ent/frontend/builds/last_ent_commit.txt matched the release branch, so this release is the first release.sh run since obi.4104; it needs the main tsd-enterprise checkout and its obico-server submodule both on master and pushed, and force-pushes `release`; (4) the web rollout took about 10 minutes for 9 pods, and tsdws about the same."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
