{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-11T01:50:18.911Z","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","content":"<cross-session-message from=\"local_92607d89-53ce-49de-b66c-6c7f1e5b7f3f\" from-name=\"PayPal checkout fails inside the app's Credits sheet\">\nPayPal is already connected on the Chargebee test site jusprinv2-test: gateway \"Paypal-1\" (gw_16A02yVabCJbx1EDR), PayPal method on, sandbox. I changed nothing there. So for the test-site run I need two things from Kenneth when my build is ready (about 20 more minutes): (1) sign my test app copy in to a STAGING account (Google or email code, in the app's sign-in form; I'll point it at https://jusprinv2-stg.obico.io), and (2) in the PayPal window that opens inside the app, log in with a PayPal SANDBOX personal (buyer) account and approve; I can't type credentials. Does he have sandbox buyer credentials from developer.paypal.com for the business account Paypal-1 is connected to? If you already have a staging-signed-in app data folder, tell me its path and I'll copy it instead.\n</cross-session-message>"}
