{"parentUuid":"79faa690-7d39-4e12-837d-adba5b3c2f29","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"799b69a1-f264-4fd3-ba48-35d327053b64","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Bash, CrossSessionMessage, Edit, Read, SendMessage, Skill, ToolSearch, WebFetch, WebSearch, Write, mcp__Claude_Browser__computer, mcp__Claude_Browser__get_page_text, mcp__Claude_Browser__navigate, mcp__Claude_Browser__preview_list, mcp__Claude_Browser__preview_start, mcp__Claude_Browser__preview_stop, mcp__Claude_Browser__tabs_context, mcp__ccd_session__start_session, mcp__ccd_session_mgmt__list_sessions, mcp__ccd_session_mgmt__send_message, mcp__ccd_turn__update_plan, mcp__ccd_turn__wrap_up, mcp__claude-in-chrome__browser_batch, mcp__claude-in-chrome__computer, mcp__claude-in-chrome__file_upload, mcp__claude-in-chrome__find, mcp__claude-in-chrome__get_page_text, mcp__claude-in-chrome__javascript_tool, mcp__claude-in-chrome__navigate, mcp__claude-in-chrome__read_console_messages, mcp__claude-in-chrome__read_page, mcp__claude-in-chrome__tabs_close_mcp, mcp__claude-in-chrome__tabs_context_mcp, mcp__claude-in-chrome__tabs_create_mcp</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n\n   **Constraints in force (verbatim or near-verbatim, carried from earlier):**\n   - \"Don't change anything in production, and don't change Chargebee's live site without Kenneth's explicit yes.\"\n     - Kenneth gave yes to copy the test site's settings to the live site.\n     - Kenneth gave yes to deploy (\"Yes, deploy\").\n   - Ask Kenneth before any production change.\n   - Never commit submodule pointer changes.\n   - Use the service account ai-agent@tsdtechnology.iam.gserviceaccount.com for gcloud and kubectl. On this Mac, set `export CLOUDSDK_PYTHON=$HOME/.local/share/uv/python/cpython-3.12.9-macos-aarch64-none/bin/python3.12`.\n   - Don't start a second docker stack.\n   - Server code goes to tsd-enterprise master.\n   - The ops repo push waits on Kenneth.\n   - I may not type passwords, government IDs or API keys; Kenneth does those himself.\n   - Never print API keys.\n     - I accidentally printed Obico's live Chargebee API key and the reCAPTCHA secret from tsd/prod/tsdweb-prod.yaml diff context, and told Kenneth.\n     - Redact secrets in any future diff output.\n   - Key files:\n     - ~/.config/jusprin/chargebee-jusprinv2-test.env\n     - ~/.config/jusprin/chargebee-jusprinv2-stg.env\n     - ~/.config/jusprin/chargebee-jusprinv2-live.env (variable CHARGEBEE_API_KEY)\n   - Fix any bug without asking.\n   - Read-only on Obico's live Chargebee site and on TSD's Stripe and PayPal accounts. Kenneth does the OAuth connects.\n   - Refunds and payments move money: I can't do them; Kenneth does.\n   - The rollout session (local_3e38de32) coordinates server releases. It earlier asked: don't push the tsd-enterprise `release` branch, don't run release.sh, don't change production or staging images, ConfigMaps, Secrets or migrations without telling it first. That hold has been lifted, but tell it before any production or staging change.\n\n   **Requests this stretch, in order:**\n   1. Copy the test site's settings to live (\"Yes, go ahead\").\n   2. Open the Stripe connect window again (\"open it again\"); Kenneth logged in.\n   3. \"I think i'm done. but yu need to check\": verify Stripe.\n   4. \"PayPal connected\": verify PayPal.\n   5. \"Yes, deploy\".\n   6. Mid-deploy asks:\n      - \"open paypal in chrome to check\" (Reference Transactions).\n      - \"chceck wiuthg the session that worked on it for how it wqasn't done\" (Google sign-in).\n   7. \"coordiante with another session to make sure this is done correctly\" (the RUNBOOK fix).\n   8. Kenneth tried to buy in the browser, then in the app, and hit the PayPal popup problem.\n   9. \"skip card testing. it will work. tell the paypal subsession to reproduce and test on test site first; the risk is a lot lower\".\n   10. \"Yes, I have one\" (a PayPal sandbox buyer login).\n   11. LATEST: Kenneth quoted my line about PayPal plans and asked: \"We need to figure this out. What can I do to help you to figure out why?\"\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n\n   **Live Chargebee site jusprinv2 (Product Catalog 2.0):**\n   - Gateways:\n     - Stripe-1 (gw_16A02yVacYD1N1JCL), connected to TSD's Stripe acct_1CrFhqLPS4omY4v8 (authorized 4:42 PM on 2026-11-10). Cards only, no Stripe webhook.\n     - Paypal-1 (gw_16A02yVacaVtI1JI3), connected while Kenneth was signed in to TSD Technology LLC's PayPal (merchant 5LEKESCBJJP9S). PayPal wallet on; cards through PayPal and Venmo off.\n   - Smart Routing (USD): cards go to Stripe-1, PayPal Express Checkout goes to Paypal-1.\n   - Transaction descriptor \"JUSPRIN\". TSD's Stripe prefix is OBICO, so statements read \"OBICO* JUSPRIN\".\n   - Webhook \"production\", whv2_AzZssBVacgRMV7JqS, at https://app.obico.io/ent/jusprin/v2/cb_webhook (API v2, all events). A probe with a fake event id got 400, which means the event was looked up on the live site and not found.\n   - Live yearly prices exist, created at 17:29 on 2026-11-10 by another session:\n     - jusprin-hobby-yearly at $100/year\n     - jusprin-workshop-yearly at $200/year\n     - coupon jusprin1-move-first-term\n     - jusprin2-obico-premium-20 now covers all four plan prices.\n   - Emails: sender is JusPrin Support. All automatic emails are off on live. The PayPal session later rewrote and enabled the credit-pack receipt on both sites.\n   - The test site jusprinv2-test also has a PayPal sandbox gateway, Paypal-1 (gw_16A02yVabCJbx1EDR). My earlier claim that it had no gateways was wrong.\n\n   **Production:**\n   - I deployed obi.4104, the same image staging ran. It was built from a72b271f7e, confirmed by web_ent/frontend/builds/last_ent_commit.txt.\n   - Added REDACTED and JUSPRIN_V2_CHARGEBEE_API_KEY to tsdweb-prod.\n   - tsdws-prod was updated with `kubectl set image` to keep its 10 replicas; the file says 12.\n   - The rollout session later released obi.4111 (yearly plans), then obi.4113, which stores a launch-offer pack as one 1,000-credit lot.\n\n   **App behaviour:**\n   - The prices page is only meant to be opened inside the app, signed in via POST /ent/jusprin/v2/web_link. Signed out, every button goes to /web/done (\"You're all set\").\n   - The app's ServerSheet sends `wxEVT_WEBVIEW_NEWWINDOW` to `wxLaunchDefaultBrowser`. That broke the PayPal popup, which loses `window.opener`. Fixed by the PayPal session (local_92607d89): its automated popup test passes on macOS, Windows and Linux.\n\n   **PayPal plans research:**\n   - Chargebee's PayPal Commerce doc says:\n     - \"Enable reference transactions on your PayPal Business Account. This is required for Chargebee live sites.\"\n     - Reference Transactions are not supported in PayPal sandbox.\n     - They must be enabled through PayPal Customer Support.\n     - Renewals use a Vault ID created at the first purchase.\n     - The legacy BAID (billing agreement ID) is deprecated.\n     - Advanced Card Processing must be enabled; the right scopes are needed.\n   - TSD's PayPal Payment preferences page says \"Save PayPal and Venmo payment methods — Sorry, you haven't been approved… apply again after 90 days.\"\n   - Chargebee's KB says PayPal can alternatively be connected through Braintree, which doesn't require reference transactions.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   **~/Projects/ops** (local commits, not pushed; master is 5 ahead):\n   - a0b8fc7, mine: \"Production: obi.4104, JusPrin 2 sells on its own live Chargebee site (jusprinv2)\".\n     - Changes image tags obi.4098 to obi.4104 in tsd/prod/{tsdbeat,tsdrttasks,tsdws,tsdweb,tsdtasks}-prod.yaml, including tsdweb's migrate initContainer.\n     - Adds to tsdweb-prod.yaml after CHARGEBEE_SITE:\n       ```\n       - name: JUSPRIN_V2_CHARGEBEE_SITE\n         value: jusprinv2\n       - name: JUSPRIN_V2_CHARGEBEE_API_KEY\n         value: <live key>\n       ```\n   - 518f49a and b2beb75, by the server-host session: tsd/RUNBOOK.md steps 3–4 now point to docs/jusprin2-host-setup.md sections 1–2. I reviewed and approved them.\n   - Don't `kubectl apply -f tsd/prod/`: it would create flower-prod.\n\n   **tsd-enterprise:**\n   - web_ent/jusprin/ledger/billing.py: `ensure_customer` creates the Chargebee customer at checkout start.\n   - web_ent/jusprin/v2/web.py: `prices` and `checkout`.\n   - web_ent/jusprin/templates/jusprin/v2/web/prices.html: the \"Sign up to buy\" link goes to `jusprin_v2_web_done`.\n   - views.py `cb_webhook`: returns 400 for an unknown event.\n   - 76d5b25d41 (by the other session, I reviewed it): adds the syndicate sequence reset to docs/jusprin2-host-setup.md section 1.\n\n   **JusPrin:**\n   - src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Shell/ServerSheet.cpp line 169: the NEWWINDOW handler.\n   - \"Open in browser\" calls `open_in_browser()`, which requests a fresh web_link.\n\n   **Scratchpad** /private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79/scratchpad/:\n   - cbl.sh: live API helper.\n   - prod-app/JusPrinProd.app with data folder prod-app/data, signed in to production. It is still running as pid 65314.\n\n   **Shared notes** (…/side-session-notes/local_3e38de32…/chargebee-jusprin-emails-draft.md): appended the live-site status, the gateways, the webhook and the yearly-price note.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - Printed Obico's live key and the reCAPTCHA secret in a diff: told Kenneth (rotation optional). Redact in future.\n   - Chrome tabs lost after reconnect: re-created a tab group. Chargebee had signed out, and Kenneth signed in himself.\n   - A zsh glob error with an unquoted `--include=*.py`: fixed by quoting.\n   - Kenneth's browser purchase went to \"You're all set\": by design for signed-out pages. Launched a scratch app on production instead.\n   - The PayPal popup is stuck in the in-app sheet: proposed a task, which Kenneth started, and it is now fixed and tested.\n   - Wrong claim that the test site had no PayPal: corrected to Kenneth.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Done:\n     - Live site copied from the test site.\n     - Stripe and PayPal connected and verified.\n     - Production deployed and verified (prices read from live, webhook probe OK).\n     - Production Google sign-in switched to the \"JusPrin Google\" SocialApp (id 4), verified.\n     - RUNBOOK and doc fixed.\n     - Real-card purchase skipped by Kenneth.\n   - Ongoing: why PayPal plans may fail.\n     - Evidence: TSD's PayPal has vaulting (\"save PayPal payment methods\") declined. Chargebee requires Reference Transactions on live for PayPal Commerce.\n     - Unknown: whether Reference Transactions is enabled on TSD's account, and whether Obico's live site renews PayPal subscriptions on this same account (would tell if RT/vaulting exists via the older Express Checkout).\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"open it again\"\n   - \"logged in\"\n   - \"I think i'm done. but yu need to check\"\n   - \"PayPal connected\" (repeated)\n   - \"Yes, deploy\"\n   - Reply quoting the Reference Transactions paragraph: \"open paypal in chrome to check\"\n   - Reply quoting the Google sign-in line: \"chceck wiuthg the session that worked on it for how it wqasn't done\"\n   - Reply quoting the RUNBOOK line: \"coordiante with another session to make sure this is done correctly\"\n   - Screenshot of jusprinv2.obico.io/ent/jusprin/v2/web/done: \"I clicked the $10 pack. but I got this without the chance of entering CC number\"\n   - Screenshot of the in-app PayPal overlay: \"paypal gave me this\"\n   - \"skip card testing. it will work. tell the paypal subsession to reproduce and test on test site first; the risk is a lot lower\"\n   - \"Yes, I have one\"\n   - Latest, quoting \"PayPal plans. PayPal turned down TSD's application to save customers' PayPal accounts, and plans need that to renew. A PayPal plan purchase on production hasn't been tried, so I don't know yet whether it fails.\": \"We need to figure this out. What can I do to help you to figure out why?\"\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Figure out whether and why PayPal plans fail on the live site, and tell Kenneth concretely what he can do. Remaining task-list steps:\n     - Check how Obico's live Chargebee site (thespaghettidetective, read-only) handles PayPal subscriptions: gateway type, and whether PayPal subscriptions renew successfully.\n     - Check which PayPal integration jusprinv2's Paypal-1 is (PayPal Commerce vs Express Checkout).\n     - Report.\n   - Report the PayPal session's latest outcome in one line: the credit-pack receipt was rewritten and published on both Chargebee sites and is still switched on, with a copy in Kenneth's inbox.\n   - Still open, reported earlier:\n     - Ops repo push (5 commits).\n     - Scratch app pid 65314 still running.\n     - Whether to turn other emails on.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Researching PayPal plan renewals in answer to \"What can I do to help you to figure out why?\". Done so far:\n   - Searched the web.\n   - Fetched Chargebee's PayPal Commerce doc page, which requires Reference Transactions on live (enabled only by PayPal Customer Support, possibly needing a phone call from an authorized person) and uses Vault IDs for renewals.\n   - Found Braintree as an alternative that doesn't need Reference Transactions.\n\n   Sources gathered (to cite):\n   - https://www.chargebee.com/docs/payments/2.0/payment-gateways-and-configuration/paypal-commerce\n   - https://www.chargebee.com/docs/payments/2.0/kb/billing/why-do-i-need-reference-transactions\n   - https://www.chargebee.com/docs/payments/2.0/payment-gateways-and-configuration/paypal_express_checkout\n   - https://www.chargebee.com/docs/payments/2.0/kb/billing/can-paypal-be-added-as-a-payment-method\n   - https://developer.paypal.com/limited-release/commerce-platform/accept-payments/standard/customize/save-payment-methods-for-recurring-payments/\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Continue the task list for Kenneth's question \"We need to figure this out. What can I do to help you to figure out why?\":\n   1. Read-only, check Obico's live Chargebee site (in Chrome, if access exists) for its PayPal gateway type and whether PayPal-paid subscriptions renew. That shows whether TSD's PayPal account already supports recurring charges.\n   2. Check Paypal-1's integration type on jusprinv2.\n   3. Tell Kenneth what is known, what is my hypothesis (labelled as such), and the concrete things only he can do:\n      - Call PayPal Customer Support to ask whether Reference Transactions and vaulting are enabled on TSD's business account, and request them.\n      - Or approve a small real PayPal plan purchase on production and cancel/refund it, to test directly.\n      - Or, as a fallback, consider Braintree, or hide PayPal for plans.\n   Cite the sources above as markdown links.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"261ba134-cadd-4b24-81fe-c07ad474ca17","timestamp":"2026-11-11T22:24:44.194Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":45,"turnIndex":71},"turnOrigin":"human","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/ops","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"jusprin-dev","slug":"rosy-bubbling-whisper"}
{"parentUuid":"261ba134-cadd-4b24-81fe-c07ad474ca17","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"invoked_skills","skills":[{"name":"anthropic-skills:chrome-browser","path":"plugin:anthropic-skills:chrome-browser","content":"Base directory for this skill: /Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/local-agent-mode-sessions/skills-plugin/68a648b0-98a4-49c7-902b-ff471f8d1d46/7911d73c-5552-4877-a943-6a0eba3d7c4d/skills/chrome-browser\n\n# Claude in Chrome\n\nClaude in Chrome is a browser extension. Its tools, named `mcp__claude-in-chrome__*`, act in the person's real Chrome, in new tabs alongside the person's own, with their existing sign-ins. Claude in Chrome is available only while the person's Chrome is running with the extension connected; if its tool calls report that the extension is not connected or get no response, Claude says so rather than retrying, and follows the session's browser guidance on whether to continue with the other browser or ask first.\n\nIf the only Claude in Chrome tool present is `enable__mcp__claude-in-chrome`, Claude calls it first: it turns Claude in Chrome on for this conversation, and the `mcp__claude-in-chrome__*` tools appear once it has run.\n\n## Loading the tools\n\nIf the `mcp__claude-in-chrome__*` tools are deferred (meaning they have to be loaded through ToolSearch before use), Claude loads every tool it expects to need in ONE ToolSearch call, because the select query accepts a comma-separated list and each extra ToolSearch call costs a full round trip. The core set to start with:\n\n```\nToolSearch with query \"select:mcp__claude-in-chrome__tabs_context_mcp,mcp__claude-in-chrome__navigate,mcp__claude-in-chrome__computer,mcp__claude-in-chrome__read_page,mcp__claude-in-chrome__tabs_create_mcp,mcp__claude-in-chrome__tabs_close_mcp\"\n```\n\nClaude adds task-specific tools to that same call when the task obviously needs them: `read_console_messages` and `read_network_requests` for debugging, `form_input` for forms, `gif_creator` for recordings, `javascript_tool` for page scripting. A second ToolSearch is only for a tool the task turned out to need later.\n\n## Starting a session: tab context first, then a new tab\n\nAt the start of each browser session Claude calls `mcp__claude-in-chrome__tabs_context_mcp` first, to see the person's current tabs and understand what they may want to work with. Then:\n\n1. Claude reuses an existing tab only when the person explicitly asks to work with it.\n2. Otherwise Claude opens a new tab with `mcp__claude-in-chrome__tabs_create_mcp` and works there, and, unless the person wants them kept, closes the tabs it created before finishing.\n3. Claude never reuses tab IDs remembered from an earlier or different session. If a tool reports that a tab does not exist or is invalid, or the person closes a tab, or a navigation error occurs, Claude calls `tabs_context_mcp` again for fresh tab IDs.\n\n## Site permissions\n\nClaude in Chrome acts on a site only once the person has allowed it; depending on their settings the person may be prompted per site, in the extension or in the app. When a tool call is waiting on or refused that permission, Claude tells the person and waits for them to allow it rather than working around it. A site the person declines is their decision; Claude moves on.\n\n## Recording a GIF\n\nFor multi-step interactions the person may want to review or share, Claude can record them with `mcp__claude-in-chrome__gif_creator`. Claude captures a few extra frames before and after each action so playback is smooth, and gives the file a meaningful name (for example \"login_process.gif\").\n\n## Reading console output\n\n`mcp__claude-in-chrome__read_console_messages` reads the page's console. Console output can be verbose, so when Claude is looking for specific entries it passes the `pattern` parameter (a regular expression), for example pattern \"[MyApp]\" to keep only the application's own logs.\n\n## Alerts and dialogs\n\nClaude does not trigger JavaScript alerts, confirms, prompts, or other browser modal dialogs through its actions. Those dialogs block all further browser events, so the extension stops receiving commands. Instead:\n\n1. Claude avoids clicking elements likely to raise a confirmation dialog (for example a \"Delete\" button) unless necessary.\n2. If it must interact with such an element, Claude warns the person first that this may interrupt the session.\n3. Claude can use `mcp__claude-in-chrome__javascript_tool` to check for and dismiss an existing dialog before proceeding, and prefers `console.log` plus `read_console_messages` over `alert` for debugging.\n\nIf a dialog does get triggered and the browser stops responding, Claude tells the person they need to dismiss it manually in Chrome.\n\n## Staying on task, and when to stop\n\nClaude stays focused on the specific task and does not wander into unrelated pages. Claude stops and asks the person how to proceed, explaining what it tried and what went wrong, when any of these happen:\n\n- browser tool calls fail or return errors after 2 or 3 attempts\n- the extension gives no response\n- page elements do not respond to clicks or input, or pages do not load or time out\n- the task turns out to involve unexpected complexity or tangents\n- several approaches have not completed the task\n\nClaude does not keep retrying the same failing action.\n"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"63cb5bf5-2579-4459-867e-c747fbf04549","timestamp":"2026-11-11T22:24:44.217Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nThe following skills were invoked EARLIER in this session (before the conversation was compacted), not on the current turn. They are shown here for context only so you remain aware of their guidelines.\n\nIMPORTANT: Do NOT re-execute these skills or perform their one-time setup actions (e.g., scheduling, creating files) again. Any request or argument text embedded in the skill bodies below — for example under a \"## User Request\" or \"## Input\" heading — was captured when that skill was first invoked. It is NOT the user's current message and NOT a new request: do not act on it as if it were live. Only continue to apply ongoing behavioral guidelines from these skills where still relevant.\n\n### Skill: anthropic-skills:chrome-browser\nPath: plugin:anthropic-skills:chrome-browser\n\nBase directory for this skill: /Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/local-agent-mode-sessions/skills-plugin/68a648b0-98a4-49c7-902b-ff471f8d1d46/7911d73c-5552-4877-a943-6a0eba3d7c4d/skills/chrome-browser\n\n# Claude in Chrome\n\nClaude in Chrome is a browser extension. Its tools, named `mcp__claude-in-chrome__*`, act in the person's real Chrome, in new tabs alongside the person's own, with their existing sign-ins. Claude in Chrome is available only while the person's Chrome is running with the extension connected; if its tool calls report that the extension is not connected or get no response, Claude says so rather than retrying, and follows the session's browser guidance on whether to continue with the other browser or ask first.\n\nIf the only Claude in Chrome tool present is `enable__mcp__claude-in-chrome`, Claude calls it first: it turns Claude in Chrome on for this conversation, and the `mcp__claude-in-chrome__*` tools appear once it has run.\n\n## Loading the tools\n\nIf the `mcp__claude-in-chrome__*` tools are deferred (meaning they have to be loaded through ToolSearch before use), Claude loads every tool it expects to need in ONE ToolSearch call, because the select query accepts a comma-separated list and each extra ToolSearch call costs a full round trip. The core set to start with:\n\n```\nToolSearch with query \"select:mcp__claude-in-chrome__tabs_context_mcp,mcp__claude-in-chrome__navigate,mcp__claude-in-chrome__computer,mcp__claude-in-chrome__read_page,mcp__claude-in-chrome__tabs_create_mcp,mcp__claude-in-chrome__tabs_close_mcp\"\n```\n\nClaude adds task-specific tools to that same call when the task obviously needs them: `read_console_messages` and `read_network_requests` for debugging, `form_input` for forms, `gif_creator` for recordings, `javascript_tool` for page scripting. A second ToolSearch is only for a tool the task turned out to need later.\n\n## Starting a session: tab context first, then a new tab\n\nAt the start of each browser session Claude calls `mcp__claude-in-chrome__tabs_context_mcp` first, to see the person's current tabs and understand what they may want to work with. Then:\n\n1. Claude reuses an existing tab only when the person explicitly asks to work with it.\n2. Otherwise Claude opens a new tab with `mcp__claude-in-chrome__tabs_create_mcp` and works there, and, unless the person wants them kept, closes the tabs it created before finishing.\n3. Claude never reuses tab IDs remembered from an earlier or different session. If a tool reports that a tab does not exist or is invalid, or the person closes a tab, or a navigation error occurs, Claude calls `tabs_context_mcp` again for fresh tab IDs.\n\n## Site permissions\n\nClaude in Chrome acts on a site only once the person has allowed it; depending on their settings the person may be prompted per site, in the extension or in the app. When a tool call is waiting on or refused that permission, Claude tells the person and waits for them to allow it rather than working around it. A site the person declines is their decision; Claude moves on.\n\n## Recording a GIF\n\nFor multi-step interactions the person may want to review or share, Claude can record them with `mcp__claude-in-chrome__gif_creator`. Claude captures a few extra frames before and after each action so playback is smooth, and gives the file a meaningful name (for example \"login_process.gif\").\n\n## Reading console output\n\n`mcp__claude-in-chrome__read_console_messages` reads the page's console. Console output can be verbose, so when Claude is looking for specific entries it passes the `pattern` parameter (a regular expression), for example pattern \"[MyApp]\" to keep only the application's own logs.\n\n## Alerts and dialogs\n\nClaude does not trigger JavaScript alerts, confirms, prompts, or other browser modal dialogs through its actions. Those dialogs block all further browser events, so the extension stops receiving commands. Instead:\n\n1. Claude avoids clicking elements likely to raise a confirmation dialog (for example a \"Delete\" button) unless necessary.\n2. If it must interact with such an element, Claude warns the person first that this may interrupt the session.\n3. Claude can use `mcp__claude-in-chrome__javascript_tool` to check for and dismiss an existing dialog before proceeding, and prefers `console.log` plus `read_console_messages` over `alert` for debugging.\n\nIf a dialog does get triggered and the browser stops responding, Claude tells the person they need to dismiss it manually in Chrome.\n\n## Staying on task, and when to stop\n\nClaude stays focused on the specific task and does not wander into unrelated pages. Claude stops and asks the person how to proceed, explaining what it tried and what went wrong, when any of these happen:\n\n- browser tool calls fail or return errors after 2 or 3 attempts\n- the extension gives no response\n- page elements do not respond to clicks or input, or pages do not load or time out\n- the task turns out to involve unexpected complexity or tangents\n- several approaches have not completed the task\n\nClaude does not keep retrying the same failing action.\n\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/ops","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"jusprin-dev","slug":"rosy-bubbling-whisper"}
