')!='assistant': continue\n    for c in m.get('message',{}).get('content',[]):\n        if c.get('type')=='text' and ('ends_at' in c['text'] or 'plan-ends' in c['text'] or '6f1f0386' in c['text'] or 'Ends 10 Dec' in c['text']):\n            print(m.get('timestamp'), c['text'][:1500]); print('=====')\nEOF","description":"Find what this session said about the plan-ends-line branch"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"cbcac8d4-d5ae-4431-b596-5b6d34dd9e1d","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgwvqSkMhV7HX7qBMShmN","requestRef":"d33935a7-4a54-46e3-8b63-cf47154249a3","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"29a75a72-39ee-41f7-9fb1-2530403f6060","timestamp":"2026-11-11T22:28:01.065Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"jusprin-dev","slug":"rosy-bubbling-whisper"}
{"parentUuid":"29a75a72-39ee-41f7-9fb1-2530403f6060","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"f7eb275a-159c-48fe-9b20-ec17dee1e5f9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G7b12AdFmKhCfpAft7DZpf","type":"tool_result","content":"2026-11-10T02:57:00.466Z JusPrin 2 can't take money in production yet. Chargebee's live site has none of the four things checkout needs, and credit-pack checkout also fails on the test site. On staging the credits mostly land correctly, but I found three server bugs. I changed nothing in production or on the live site.\n\n**What I tested on staging.** I never entered a card, because the safety rules I run under don't let me make test payments on a hosted site. Instead I recorded offline payments on Chargebee's test site and watched the webhook grant credits.\n- **Prices page, signed out (`?guest=1`) and signed in:** right. An address with a paying Obico account sees $8 and $16, struck through from $10 and $20.\n- **Obico Premium discount:** Chargebee's checkout page shows \"JusPrin Hobby $10.00, Obico Premium 20% off −$2.00, $8.00\". It carries Obico's logo, not JusPrin's.\n- **Credit pack checkout:** fails with \"Checkout couldn't start\". Chargebee says \"One time checkout is not enabled under Checkout & Self-Serve Portal\", a switch in its settings screen. The pack addon was also missing; I created it on the test site only.\n- **Pack paid through the webhook:** 500 credits plus the 500 launch bonus, granted exactly once.\n- **Hobby to Workshop:** Hobby's credits expire, Workshop's 1,000 plus 1,000 are granted once. Correct.\n- **Cancel:** works, and the billing page says \"Ends 10 Dec.\"\n- **Not tested:** a real card checkout and the done page after it, a failed card, Chargebee's emails, and the desktop app itsel\n=====\n2026-11-10T17:44:11.771Z I committed the port as 637f823933 on branch `jusprin-v2-own-chargebee-site` in the tsd-enterprise worktree. It is not pushed.\n\nTo your question: of the items I listed, two need a decision from you, three are things only you can do, and the rest I can do myself.\n\n**Decision needed: fix the three billing problems before launch?**\n- **Credits before payment:** say someone buys Hobby and their card is declined. The server grants the 1,500 credits anyway when Chargebee creates the subscription, so the person gets them without paying.\n- **Switching back:** someone who moves from Workshop back to Hobby in the same month loses their Hobby credits.\n- **\"Renews\" after a cancel:** after someone cancels, the app still shows \"Renews 10 Dec.\" instead of \"Ends 10 Dec.\"\n\nYou have two options:\n- I fix all three on this branch now. The proposed patch was written for Obico's site, so I'd adapt it to the new one and test it the same way. That should take a few hours.\n- You launch with them. The first one gives away credits whenever a card fails.\n\nMy pick is to fix them now. Do you want them fixed before this lands?\n\n**Decision needed: which API key does staging use?**\nWhen you approved the test-site key, you said it should stay in local dev only. Staging needs a key for the same test site. You have two options:\n- Allow that same key on staging. It's one less thing to manage.\n- I create a second test-site key just for staging. Then either one can be revoked without breaking the other.\n\nMy pick i\n=====\n2026-11-10T18:17:03.781Z You're right, and I shouldn't have asked. Nobody had given a reason to keep those bugs. If I had doubted one, the right move was to ask the session that wrote the code, not you. I saved that as a standing rule.\n\nAll three are now fixed and committed, with nothing pushed. Before each change I made the bug happen on the jusprinv2-test site using real Chargebee events, then checked it again after the fix.\n\n- **Credits before payment.** I started a Hobby subscription whose $10 invoice was unpaid and fed its three real events to the webhook. The old code granted 750 plus 750 credits; the fixed code grants nothing. Once the invoice is paid, the credits are granted.\n- **Switching back.** On the old code, going from Hobby to Workshop and back to Hobby in the same month left the account on Hobby. Its Hobby credits were ended, while Workshop's 2,000 stayed live. Now the switch back restores the Hobby credits and ends Workshop's.\n- **\"Renews\" after a cancel.** After a cancel, `/v2/account` now sends the end date (`ends_at`) instead of a renewal date. Preferences shows \"Ends 10 Dec.\" in place of \"Renews 10 Dec.\".\n\nI fixed one more problem I found along the way. The webhook now reads the subscription's current state from Chargebee instead of the copy inside the event. Chargebee can deliver events late or twice, so an old \"switched to Workshop\" event could otherwise undo a later switch back.\n\n**Where the changes are:**\n- Server: commit 161e2747a2 on `jusprin-v2-own-chargebee-site` in tsd-e\n=====\n2026-11-10T19:33:05.600Z No to both. I haven't tested on staging at all, so we're not ready for production.\n\n**What has been tested:** everything ran on my local server against JusPrin's test Chargebee site, including:\n- a credit pack purchase,\n- Hobby and Workshop plans paid by card through Stripe and by PayPal,\n- plan switches, a payment that hadn't gone through yet, and a cancel.\n\n**Why staging isn't ready:**\n- The server code is committed only on a local tsd-enterprise branch (jusprin-v2-own-chargebee-site, two commits). It has never been pushed, so staging doesn't run it.\n- The staging and production settings files I copied on 9 Nov have no JusPrin 2 Chargebee settings.\n- You approved the test-site API key for local development only, so staging would need its own test-site key.\n- The app change that shows \"Ends 10 Dec.\" after a plan is cancelled is also committed locally only, on its own JusPrin branch.\n\n**Putting it on staging would take five steps:**\n1. Push the server branch to tsd-enterprise master and deploy staging.\n2. You create a second API key on the test Chargebee site for staging.\n3. Put that key and the site name into staging's settings.\n4. Point the test site's webhook at staging, so Chargebee's payment notices reach the staging server.\n5. Then I'd repeat the purchases there (pack, plan by card, plan by PayPal) and check the credits in the app connected to staging.\n\n**Production needs everything above, plus:**\n- You turn on JusPrin's live Chargebee site.\n- Stripe and PayPal are conn\n=====\n2026-11-10T20:32:48.689Z Staging is done and passes. jusprinv2-stg.obico.io now sells JusPrin 2 credits and plans through JusPrin's own test Chargebee site. In Chrome, I bought a credit pack and a Hobby plan, checked the Premium discount, and cancelled the plan; all of it worked.\n\n**What I tested on staging, each with a new test account:**\n- **Credit pack, paid with Stripe's test card:** the page said \"1,000 credits added\" and the account showed 1,500. The checkout's return and Chargebee's webhook both reported the sale, and it counted once (500 plus a 500 launch bonus).\n- **Hobby plan:** the page said \"You're on Hobby\", with 1,500 credits a month until 31 Jan, then 750. Billing and usage showed \"Renews 10 Dec\" and the Visa test card.\n- **Obico Premium subscriber:** Credits and plans showed Hobby at $8 \"With Obico Premium's 20% off\", and Chargebee's cart applied the coupon for $8.00. I stopped there without paying.\n- **Cancel:** the plan stopped renewing and stays until 10 Dec. The account reply sends no renewal date and an end date of 10 Dec, which the app's \"Ends 10 Dec.\" line uses.\n- **Errors:** Sentry shows no new errors since the deploy.\n\n**A bug I found and fixed on the way.** Local development and staging share the test Chargebee site, and both named customers \"jusprinv2-<user id>\". User ids repeat across servers, so a staging account could have taken over a local test customer's saved card and subscription. A local test payment could also have added credits to an unrelated staging account. St\n=====\n2026-11-10T21:28:20.174Z We're not ready for production yet. The server code is ready, but JusPrin's Chargebee account still has only its test site. The site picker shows \"jusprinv2 – TEST Site\" and no live site. Until a live site exists with its catalog, payment gateways and webhook, production has nowhere to sell. I changed nothing during this check.\n\n**What's ready**\n- **Server code:** master holds the move to JusPrin's own Chargebee site, the billing fixes, the customer-name prefix and the setup doc. Staging ran it end to end: a credit pack, a Hobby plan, the Premium discount in the cart, a cancel, and a pack with no billing form. PayPal was tested on a local server.\n- **What master adds over production:** six commits and no database migrations. Production runs image obi.4098, built from master commit 0a75568378.\n- **Production matches the ops files.** The only differences are web-socket replicas scaled down on purpose and env lines in a different order.\n- **Low risk to customers:** production has one JusPrin 2 account, yours (k@obico.io). Buying there already fails today: as of the 9 Nov check, the JusPrin 2 plans did not exist on Obico's live site. Deploying won't break anything that works now.\n- **Sentry:** no errors in the billing code. The one hit on `/ent/cb_webhook/` is the old Obico email bug from August.\n\n**What blocks the rollout**\n1. **The live site.** You have to activate it; Chargebee will ask for business details. Then it needs everything the test site has:\n   - the three prices and\n=====","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"88eff126-6470-4544-818f-3600a6237809","timestamp":"2026-11-11T22:28:01.697Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"2026-11-10T02:57:00.466Z JusPrin 2 can't take money in production yet. Chargebee's live site has none of the four things checkout needs, and credit-pack checkout also fails on the test site. On staging the credits mostly land correctly, but I found three server bugs. I changed nothing in production or on the live site.\n\n**What I tested on staging.** I never entered a card, because the safety rules I run under don't let me make test payments on a hosted site. Instead I recorded offline payments on Chargebee's test site and watched the webhook grant credits.\n- **Prices page, signed out (`?guest=1`) and signed in:** right. An address with a paying Obico account sees $8 and $16, struck through from $10 and $20.\n- **Obico Premium discount:** Chargebee's checkout page shows \"JusPrin Hobby $10.00, Obico Premium 20% off −$2.00, $8.00\". It carries Obico's logo, not JusPrin's.\n- **Credit pack checkout:** fails with \"Checkout couldn't start\". Chargebee says \"One time checkout is not enabled under Checkout & Self-Serve Portal\", a switch in its settings screen. The pack addon was also missing; I created it on the test site only.\n- **Pack paid through the webhook:** 500 credits plus the 500 launch bonus, granted exactly once.\n- **Hobby to Workshop:** Hobby's credits expire, Workshop's 1,000 plus 1,000 are granted once. Correct.\n- **Cancel:** works, and the billing page says \"Ends 10 Dec.\"\n- **Not tested:** a real card checkout and the done page after it, a failed card, Chargebee's emails, and the desktop app itsel\n=====\n2026-11-10T17:44:11.771Z I committed the port as 637f823933 on branch `jusprin-v2-own-chargebee-site` in the tsd-enterprise worktree. It is not pushed.\n\nTo your question: of the items I listed, two need a decision from you, three are things only you can do, and the rest I can do myself.\n\n**Decision needed: fix the three billing problems before launch?**\n- **Credits before payment:** say someone buys Hobby and their card is declined. The server grants the 1,500 credits anyway when Chargebee creates the subscription, so the person gets them without paying.\n- **Switching back:** someone who moves from Workshop back to Hobby in the same month loses their Hobby credits.\n- **\"Renews\" after a cancel:** after someone cancels, the app still shows \"Renews 10 Dec.\" instead of \"Ends 10 Dec.\"\n\nYou have two options:\n- I fix all three on this branch now. The proposed patch was written for Obico's site, so I'd adapt it to the new one and test it the same way. That should take a few hours.\n- You launch with them. The first one gives away credits whenever a card fails.\n\nMy pick is to fix them now. Do you want them fixed before this lands?\n\n**Decision needed: which API key does staging use?**\nWhen you approved the test-site key, you said it should stay in local dev only. Staging needs a key for the same test site. You have two options:\n- Allow that same key on staging. It's one less thing to manage.\n- I create a second test-site key just for staging. Then either one can be revoked without breaking the other.\n\nMy pick i\n=====\n2026-11-10T18:17:03.781Z You're right, and I shouldn't have asked. Nobody had given a reason to keep those bugs. If I had doubted one, the right move was to ask the session that wrote the code, not you. I saved that as a standing rule.\n\nAll three are now fixed and committed, with nothing pushed. Before each change I made the bug happen on the jusprinv2-test site using real Chargebee events, then checked it again after the fix.\n\n- **Credits before payment.** I started a Hobby subscription whose $10 invoice was unpaid and fed its three real events to the webhook. The old code granted 750 plus 750 credits; the fixed code grants nothing. Once the invoice is paid, the credits are granted.\n- **Switching back.** On the old code, going from Hobby to Workshop and back to Hobby in the same month left the account on Hobby. Its Hobby credits were ended, while Workshop's 2,000 stayed live. Now the switch back restores the Hobby credits and ends Workshop's.\n- **\"Renews\" after a cancel.** After a cancel, `/v2/account` now sends the end date (`ends_at`) instead of a renewal date. Preferences shows \"Ends 10 Dec.\" in place of \"Renews 10 Dec.\".\n\nI fixed one more problem I found along the way. The webhook now reads the subscription's current state from Chargebee instead of the copy inside the event. Chargebee can deliver events late or twice, so an old \"switched to Workshop\" event could otherwise undo a later switch back.\n\n**Where the changes are:**\n- Server: commit 161e2747a2 on `jusprin-v2-own-chargebee-site` in tsd-e\n=====\n2026-11-10T19:33:05.600Z No to both. I haven't tested on staging at all, so we're not ready for production.\n\n**What has been tested:** everything ran on my local server against JusPrin's test Chargebee site, including:\n- a credit pack purchase,\n- Hobby and Workshop plans paid by card through Stripe and by PayPal,\n- plan switches, a payment that hadn't gone through yet, and a cancel.\n\n**Why staging isn't ready:**\n- The server code is committed only on a local tsd-enterprise branch (jusprin-v2-own-chargebee-site, two commits). It has never been pushed, so staging doesn't run it.\n- The staging and production settings files I copied on 9 Nov have no JusPrin 2 Chargebee settings.\n- You approved the test-site API key for local development only, so staging would need its own test-site key.\n- The app change that shows \"Ends 10 Dec.\" after a plan is cancelled is also committed locally only, on its own JusPrin branch.\n\n**Putting it on staging would take five steps:**\n1. Push the server branch to tsd-enterprise master and deploy staging.\n2. You create a second API key on the test Chargebee site for staging.\n3. Put that key and the site name into staging's settings.\n4. Point the test site's webhook at staging, so Chargebee's payment notices reach the staging server.\n5. Then I'd repeat the purchases there (pack, plan by card, plan by PayPal) and check the credits in the app connected to staging.\n\n**Production needs everything above, plus:**\n- You turn on JusPrin's live Chargebee site.\n- Stripe and PayPal are conn\n=====\n2026-11-10T20:32:48.689Z Staging is done and passes. jusprinv2-stg.obico.io now sells JusPrin 2 credits and plans through JusPrin's own test Chargebee site. In Chrome, I bought a credit pack and a Hobby plan, checked the Premium discount, and cancelled the plan; all of it worked.\n\n**What I tested on staging, each with a new test account:**\n- **Credit pack, paid with Stripe's test card:** the page said \"1,000 credits added\" and the account showed 1,500. The checkout's return and Chargebee's webhook both reported the sale, and it counted once (500 plus a 500 launch bonus).\n- **Hobby plan:** the page said \"You're on Hobby\", with 1,500 credits a month until 31 Jan, then 750. Billing and usage showed \"Renews 10 Dec\" and the Visa test card.\n- **Obico Premium subscriber:** Credits and plans showed Hobby at $8 \"With Obico Premium's 20% off\", and Chargebee's cart applied the coupon for $8.00. I stopped there without paying.\n- **Cancel:** the plan stopped renewing and stays until 10 Dec. The account reply sends no renewal date and an end date of 10 Dec, which the app's \"Ends 10 Dec.\" line uses.\n- **Errors:** Sentry shows no new errors since the deploy.\n\n**A bug I found and fixed on the way.** Local development and staging share the test Chargebee site, and both named customers \"jusprinv2-<user id>\". User ids repeat across servers, so a staging account could have taken over a local test customer's saved card and subscription. A local test payment could also have added credits to an unrelated staging account. St\n=====\n2026-11-10T21:28:20.174Z We're not ready for production yet. The server code is ready, but JusPrin's Chargebee account still has only its test site. The site picker shows \"jusprinv2 – TEST Site\" and no live site. Until a live site exists with its catalog, payment gateways and webhook, production has nowhere to sell. I changed nothing during this check.\n\n**What's ready**\n- **Server code:** master holds the move to JusPrin's own Chargebee site, the billing fixes, the customer-name prefix and the setup doc. Staging ran it end to end: a credit pack, a Hobby plan, the Premium discount in the cart, a cancel, and a pack with no billing form. PayPal was tested on a local server.\n- **What master adds over production:** six commits and no database migrations. Production runs image obi.4098, built from master commit 0a75568378.\n- **Production matches the ops files.** The only differences are web-socket replicas scaled down on purpose and env lines in a different order.\n- **Low risk to customers:** production has one JusPrin 2 account, yours (k@obico.io). Buying there already fails today: as of the 9 Nov check, the JusPrin 2 plans did not exist on Obico's live site. Deploying won't break anything that works now.\n- **Sentry:** no errors in the billing code. The one hit on `/ent/cb_webhook/` is the old Obico email bug from August.\n\n**What blocks the rollout**\n1. **The live site.** You have to activate it; Chargebee will ask for business details. Then it needs everything the test site has:\n   - the three prices and\n=====","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"29a75a72-39ee-41f7-9fb1-2530403f6060","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"jusprin-dev","slug":"rosy-bubbling-whisper"}
