{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","id":"cc803a21-5916-4871-8139-cab1fa12c227","timestamp":"2026-11-11T23:10:56.839Z","version":"2.1.321","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"1b4d38a5eb11a691f0e44b7d1ff3ba2b6049d0016dff835cbfcdef92b1844758","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"high"}},"base":"bc9eb0f7-f0ea-48ca-be9a-37017450fefd","keep":119,"tail":["14e8fdb8812ac153cbfe095678b84e6860d2622152e2bd9b6b42e0e0807498ea","7dd6c2c6b09db04b69d918015073ce5a14c4a9cd8198039460b6aaaa03664700","8d5417819870814c986d7076932ad2dcad28287bdd05a674772b4c6ce5fb42e5"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",121,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"4f8c5f9eb463febe74d1232425f2a1d4c57d3987f9144fb79a8f50d5a5d7d644"}
{"parentUuid":"d3598a5f-ae0f-4f8e-8909-7a9ce546c5ea","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgwz7e6nh76ePu8sgVhvq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, that summary is correct. I checked one more piece just now. Production first ran JusPrin 2 billing from tsd-enterprise commit a72b271f7e (image obi.4104). In that commit, the account reply sends `ends_at`, and its tests cover a cancelled plan: no renewal date, plus an end date. Production has moved to later images since, and those build on top of that commit.\n\n**Other open items, still waiting on you:**\n\n1. **The PayPal plan test.** Nothing has been bought yet: JusPrin 2's live site still has no subscriptions and no payments. The production copy of the app is open and signed in as k@obico.io. To buy, open Credits and plans, click \"Open in browser\", choose Hobby monthly, and pay with PayPal. When you're done, tell me and I'll check what Chargebee and PayPal recorded and whether the credits were added. After that, you cancel the plan and refund yourself, and I quit that copy of the app.\n2. **What to do about PayPal for plans.** This depends on the test result. The choices are to call PayPal support and ask them to approve saving PayPal accounts on TSD's account, or to stop offering PayPal for plans until they do.\n3. **Automatic emails on JusPrin 2's live Chargebee site.** All of them are off except the credit-pack receipt. Whether to turn the others on, such as the plan receipt, the renewal reminder and the failed-payment notice, is your call.\n4. **Two secrets I printed by mistake earlier.** They are Obico's live Chargebee API key and the reCAPTCHA secret, which showed up in a diff. Rotating them is optional, and you would have to do it yourself.\n\n**One small mismatch, no action needed:** the ops file for production says tsdws-prod (production's web-socket servers) runs 12 copies, while production runs 10. I kept 10 on purpose when I deployed, so a future `kubectl apply` of that file would raise it to 12.\n\nThe ops repo needs nothing: everything there is already on GitHub."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":376,"cache_read_input_tokens":156557,"output_tokens":667,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":376,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":667,"cache_read_input_tokens":156557,"cache_creation_input_tokens":376,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":376},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"c3ab17aa-abe0-46dc-a991-fe8f3e316e51","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgwz7dquNtUNiBzVQVBPF","requestRef":"cc803a21-5916-4871-8139-cab1fa12c227","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"880becb1-7879-4f3a-ae0e-5790704cf353","timestamp":"2026-11-11T23:11:03.615Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/tsd-enterprise","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"jusprin-dev","slug":"rosy-bubbling-whisper"}
