{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","hash":"aeb0d37f55d8a678ba4e4fc4519e33495447b839448ad44fb5fb70b38cf83053","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A5yduDKM9CSPaToXtQaaMP","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Plan shown (4 steps)."}]},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LpNsHyrSk4PrxerK3dwzGM","type":"tool_result","content":"---\nname: merge-no-ff-not-squash\ndescription: \"2026-11-06: Kenneth removed the AGENTS.md rule 'land feature branches on jusprin-newui with --no-ff, never squash' (removal commit 96c7bda756). No standing rule; ask how to land.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983\n  modified: 2026-11-06T13:12:56.743Z\n---\n\nOn 2026-11-05 Kenneth asked whether to squash for a clean log; I recommended `git merge --no-ff` and he said \"Okay, go with what you suggested.\" I wrote that into AGENTS.md as \"Landing a branch on jusprin-newui\" (a2d5550058), in my own words, and later called it \"the project rules\" to him.\n\nOn 2026-11-06 he asked where the rule said that, then asked to remove it. Removed in 96c7bda756 on claude/first-run-fixes; the removal reached jusprin-newui in the squash b0a2fe3b08. Kenneth confirmed on 2026-11-06 evening that dropping the rule was on purpose.\n\n**Why:** the rule text was mine, not his; he had agreed to one recommendation, not to a standing rule. See [[trace-a-rule-to-kenneths-words]].\n\n**How to apply:** don't cite --no-ff-only as a project rule. When landing a branch, ask Kenneth how he wants it landed (merge or squash) unless he has said so for that branch.\n---\nname: commit-to-integration-branch\ndescription: \"2026-11-08 Kenneth: jusprin-dev is the development branch (cut from the OrcaSlicer 2.5.0 merge 975c703f08); ui-walkthrough and jusprin-newui are superseded; tsd-enterprise server code straight to master\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: b5623e1a-a18f-419a-a231-dcd19830f813\n  modified: 2026-11-09T02:00:03.189Z\n---\n\nFrom 2026-11-08, JusPrin app work lands on `jusprin-dev`. Kenneth: \"branch out a jusprin-dev from the upstream merge commit, and use this branch as the dev branch\". It starts at `975c703f08` (the merge of OrcaSlicer 2.5.0 into ui-walkthrough) and contains `jusprin-newui` and `ui-walkthrough`; start nothing new on those. AGENTS.md's \"Branches\" section records this. `jusprin-v1` holds JusPrin 1. Server code in tsd-enterprise goes straight to `master` (2026-11-06 rule, unchanged).\n\nHistory: 2026-11-06 `jusprin-newui-integration`; 2026-11-07 `ui-walkthrough`; 2026-11-08 `jusprin-dev`.\n\n`main`, Kenneth 2026-11-08: \"main will be the stable branch that doesn't allow force push ( except in some extreme circumstances when no other options are feasible). This is so that the users who clone our repo won't have to force pull.\" and \"for now, it also double a release branch. But this rule is more flexible than the first one.\" GitHub branch protection on `main` blocks force pushes and deletion, admins included (enforce_admins). `main` moves forward from `jusprin-dev` only when a version is released; ask before fast-forwarding it. On 2026-11-08 Kenneth chose to leave `main` at 4da9d7beb4 until 2.0.0 ships, although that means the scheduled nightly keeps running `main`'s older file and doesn't build `jusprin-dev` until then. Start the nightly by hand on `jusprin-dev` with only `-f sign_macos=true`. GitHub runs scheduled workflows from `main`'s copy of the file, and validates dispatch inputs against it.\n\n**Why:** the dev branch is the build Kenneth reviews; work on a side branch never reaches what he tests.\n\n**How to apply:** Kenneth, 2026-11-08: \"I want the main checkout to be always on jusprin-dev\". Since then /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin holds `jusprin-dev`; byoai-newui was moved to its own branch `byoai-newui`. Git allows one checkout per branch, so never check `jusprin-dev` out in a worktree. Commit from a worktree of your own on its own branch or detached at the tip. Then bring the main checkout along so its files match the branch; moving the ref from elsewhere (update-ref, or a push without a pull) leaves the main checkout's `git status` showing the new commits as reversed. When pushing is asked: push to origin jusprin-dev, then `git -C /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin pull --ff-only` (Kenneth: \"you just need to bring the local main checkout by pulling from the remote\"). Push nothing unless asked. Supersedes the landing question in [[merge-no-ff-not-squash]].\n## jusprin-dev...origin/jusprin-dev\n?? new-project-handling-report.md\nWarning: Permanently added 'github.com' (ED25519) to the list of known hosts.\r\n846e01d06c App menus: hide OrcaSlicer items that don't fit JusPrin, and one export each for the project and the G-code\n846e01d06c App menus: hide OrcaSlicer items that don't fit JusPrin, and one export each for the project and the G-code","is_error":false}]}}
