{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","id":"4db97b39-4887-4499-bb10-d250f35dd058","timestamp":"2026-11-11T23:25:45.368Z","version":"2.1.321","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"971934867d59896c86c46fd46b92a3bf2bca009338971d67d4bdde4d352660b0","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"high"}},"base":"a53d2409-1022-46fe-808d-b1e75a58cf18","keep":176,"tail":["b77c66d1a9a3a5993131c584ead54defa27d17a9a55f1b84c0fa264a40ce2749","1541cf03c1949a5a315da79b1d01174788acd903e1b3ec319db3edf58b6c3859","8d5417819870814c986d7076932ad2dcad28287bdd05a674772b4c6ce5fb42e5"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",178,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"b81d20c5af800ba4bb9c9e90e4c854b7b8ad0440fa9d780b528c6fd27dd8f040"}
{"parentUuid":"ca679cff-fd72-438c-b4df-78108aefedda","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgx1F8wvyUtF88RhSJKtX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"jusprin-dev is pushed, but with a mistake I need to own. In a side thread you asked whether I'd make a merge commit and said you hate noisy branches; that thread promised a cherry-pick instead. I missed it and landed the branch with a merge commit (8838af0820), then pushed it. I saved that preference as a standing note so this doesn't happen again.\n\n**Decision needed: should the merge commit on jusprin-dev be replaced with one plain commit?** This is yours because it rewrites history that's already on GitHub. Nobody has pushed anything on top of it yet.\n- **Replace it.** I'd move jusprin-dev back to the commit before it (846e01d06c) and cherry-pick the fix as one ordinary commit. Then I'd re-run the AgentUI tests and push with `--force-with-lease`, which refuses to push if anyone has pushed in the meantime. Last, I'd bring your main checkout along. The cost: any session that already fetched the merge commit would see jusprin-dev rewritten. It was pushed only minutes ago, so that's unlikely.\n- **Leave it.** History keeps one extra merge commit.\n\nMy pick is to replace it now, while nothing sits on top of it.\n\n**Status from the sessions I started.** I read their latest reports instead of waking them; they're all idle.\n- [PayPal checkout fails inside the app's Credits sheet](#local_92607d89-53ce-49de-b66c-6c7f1e5b7f3f) is finished. Its fix for the PayPal window inside the app is on jusprin-dev. It turned on 20 automatic emails on both JusPrin 2 Chargebee sites, the same set Obico's site sends plus a \"Subscription is changed\" email. It rewrote the welcome email and the credit-pack receipt, moved its test email to Trash, and stopped the Windows and Linux test VMs. Nothing from it is waiting on you. That also means the automatic-emails question I raised earlier is settled.\n- The ops repo and jusprin-dev are both on GitHub now.\n\n**Your action items:**\n1. **Answer the question about the merge commit above.**\n2. **Run the PayPal plan test.** In the copy of JusPrin I opened (signed in to production as k@obico.io), open Credits and plans and click \"Open in browser\". Buy Hobby monthly ($10, or $8 with the Obico Premium discount) with PayPal. Tell me what you saw on screen. I'll check what Chargebee and PayPal recorded and whether your 1,500 credits were added. Then cancel the plan and refund yourself.\n3. **After the test, decide about PayPal for plans.** The choices are to call PayPal business support and ask them to approve saving PayPal accounts for TSD (merchant 5LEKESCBJJP9S), or to stop offering PayPal for plans until they do. I'll write that decision up in full once we know what the test shows.\n4. **Optional: rotate two secrets I printed by mistake earlier.** They are Obico's live Chargebee API key and the reCAPTCHA secret. Only you can rotate them."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":331,"cache_read_input_tokens":184729,"output_tokens":1028,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":331,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1028,"cache_read_input_tokens":184729,"cache_creation_input_tokens":331,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":331},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"a054c770-ab2b-4d72-ac4d-0a5b4f8872f5","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgx1F8epJ3PFSe7qCNMqF","requestRef":"4db97b39-4887-4499-bb10-d250f35dd058","requestedMo