{"parentUuid":"b6d5c30f-d21e-4f67-af57-09f9ea80b6f7","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory/no-merge-commits-on-jusprin-dev.md","snippet":"1\t---\n2\tname: no-merge-commits-on-jusprin-dev\n3\tdescription: \"2026-11-11 Kenneth: 'I hate a very noisy branch with a lot of merge commits.' Land a short branch on jusprin-dev by cherry-pick or rebase, not a merge commit.\"\n4\tmetadata:\n5\t  node_type: memory\n6\t  type: feedback\n7\t  originSessionId: 14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79\n8\t  modified: 2026-11-11T23:25:31.883Z\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\tKenneth, 2026-11-11, when asked whether to merge claude/plan-ends-line (one commit) into jusprin-dev: \"Are you going to create a merge commit? I hate a very noisy branch with a lot of merge commits.\"\n12\t\n13\tThe same day the main session missed that side-thread answer and landed it with `git merge --no-ff` (8838af0820) and pushed it. With Kenneth's yes it was replaced by the plain commit 12e1529cb6 (force-push with lease) minutes later.\n14\t\n15\t**Why:** jusprin-dev's history is what Kenneth reads; merge commits for one-commit branches are noise.\n16\t\n17\t**How to apply:** land a branch on jusprin-dev as plain commits (cherry-pick, or rebase then fast-forward). Before landing, check side threads (btw forks of this session) for anything Kenneth said about how to land. Ask only if the branch is long enough that a merge commit might be wanted. Refines [[merge-no-ff-not-squash]] and [[commit-to-integration-branch]].","rereadEntry":{"timestamp":1794439807431,"contentHash":"1he6kjlml2fzj","contentLength":1264}},"type":"attachment","uuid":"415ff60c-fe85-48b0-9ed0-3c315871897f","timestamp":"2026-11-11T23:30:08.262Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory/no-merge-commits-on-jusprin-dev.md changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. Here are the relevant changes (shown with line numbers):\n1\t---\n2\tname: no-merge-commits-on-jusprin-dev\n3\tdescription: \"2026-11-11 Kenneth: 'I hate a very noisy branch with a lot of merge commits.' Land a short branch on jusprin-dev by cherry-pick or rebase, not a merge commit.\"\n4\tmetadata:\n5\t  node_type: memory\n6\t  type: feedback\n7\t  originSessionId: 14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79\n8\t  modified: 2026-11-11T23:25:31.883Z\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\tKenneth, 2026-11-11, when asked whether to merge claude/plan-ends-line (one commit) into jusprin-dev: \"Are you going to create a merge commit? I hate a very noisy branch with a lot of merge commits.\"\n12\t\n13\tThe same day the main session missed that side-thread answer and landed it with `git merge --no-ff` (8838af0820) and pushed it. With Kenneth's yes it was replaced by the plain commit 12e1529cb6 (force-push with lease) minutes later.\n14\t\n15\t**Why:** jusprin-dev's history is what Kenneth reads; merge commits for one-commit branches are noise.\n16\t\n17\t**How to apply:** land a branch on jusprin-dev as plain commits (cherry-pick, or rebase then fast-forward). Before landing, check side threads (btw forks of this session) for anything Kenneth said about how to land. Ask only if the branch is long enough that a merge commit might be wanted. Refines [[merge-no-ff-not-squash]] and [[commit-to-integration-branch]].\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory","sessionId":"14cb6590-7113-489e-aa7f-9aa6dca15e79","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"jusprin-dev","slug":"rosy-bubbling-whisper"}
